te":"2026-09-03T15:30:05Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"jahia-ci","providerType":"User"},"email":"jahia-ci@jahia.com","name":"Jahia"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:08:42.140Z","repositoryId":1177684030,"sha":"82e47139502f72411ac81be74ef5f13500cf4bbb"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:08:42.140Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/ff01b64ad742dd6577780703bbc15284425179ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:17:57Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:17:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: specification of the import of Jahia Forms forms and results (#386)\n\n* docs: draft specification of the import of Jahia Forms forms and submissions\n\n* docs: the import maps send-to-submitter onto the notification and reports redirects; redirect action proposal\n\n* docs: the Forms import ships results first, and a later form attaches to them\n\nIteration 1 imports the submissions alone, from the formFactory export, with a snapshot of the labels; iteration 2 attaches them to a Formidable form by node name, then label, then by hand. Rebuilding a form from the results and importing the forms become iterations 3 and 4. Dates take the nearest UTC midnight instead of one time zone.\n\n* docs: the Forms import keys a form on its export path, starts from an Import button of the Results page, and fixes the split depth and the date rule\n\n* docs: the Forms import dialog runs a dry run and shows its report before the import, into the current site\n\n* docs: the Forms import lives in the engine with source-agnostic markers, matches a form on its field UUIDs, scopes the attachment to one source, and keeps its jobs in the repository\n\n* docs: the Forms import runs one import per site, keeps the Imported status to never-attached entries, and falls back to the field title and placeholder for its labels\n\n* docs: the Forms import recreates each form in an imported-forms content folder before it writes its results\n\nThe orphan-results state is gone: iteration 1 creates an unpublished Formidable form per Forms form\n(same field names, mapped types, labels from the title or else the placeholder, rules, choices, actions;\nwhat has no equivalent is reported) and writes the submissions as the results of that form, so the Results\npage, the exports and the statuses need no change. Iteration 2 moves the results of one source form onto a\nform built by hand. The import reads the zip export taken with live content, which alone carries the\nresults, the jcr:uuid of every node and the files; forms are keyed by jcr:uuid. One import per site goes\nthrough the scheduler''s job name instead of a claim property; the reader streams the XML.\n\n* docs: the Forms import names each field from its label and says what the Results page shows before the form is published\n\nA recreated field gets the system name the Content Editor would generate from its label\n(your-first-name, not text-input_0_1), unique in the form, with the Forms identity kept on the field\n(fmdbmix:importedField) so a later run writes the values of a renamed field under its new name. The import\nnever publishes: until a contributor publishes a form, its entry shows as Unpublished with the system names\nas columns, the final report says so, and the Cypress spec publishes a form before it checks the labels.\n\n* docs: the Forms import keys a form by its results node too, saves only what Forms saved, and keeps a job''s report until it is read\n\nFour review points: a form deleted in Forms between two exports has no jcr:uuid left, so the form keeps\nthe jcr:uuid of its fcnt:formResults as a second key and a later run matches on either; fmdb:save2jcrAction\nis created only when Forms had a saveToJcrAction, else reported, so no form starts keeping personal data by\nan import''s choice; the jobs run on the persistent scheduler, hence on the processing server, where a\nstopped import resumes with that server, and the Importing state can be closed and found again; the job\nnode keeps its end state and report until Close or one hour, dropping only the file.\n\n* docs: final pass on the Forms import spec\n\nUses the extended inputs where they exist (switch, rating, consent) with the elements fallback; the\ncountry code is the key of the JSON; the results entry is named as SaveToJcrFormAction names it; a dry\nrun keeps its file for the import; Failed can be closed; the applied mappings of iteration 2 have their\nproperty; the attachment has its entry point; a form never published nor submitted has no results node.\n\n* docs: the reserved field names are the request parameters the submission pipeline reads, and a fourth spike covers the fields and files the sample lacks\n\n* docs: spike 1 answered, the import sets jcr:created through the addNode overload the Jahia import uses and creates the split folders itself","tree":{"sha":"0891e180cb15d88c7b4db39e43bd3ad5c0cd4974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/0891e180cb15d88c7b4db39e43bd3ad5c0cd4974"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/ff01b64ad742dd6577780703bbc15284425179ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 0891e180cb15d88c7b4db39e43bd3ad5c0cd4974\nparent 7787b56ef4d59d8f458643d11bc46806616951fa\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1791465477 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791465477 +0200\n\ndocs: specification of the import of Jahia Forms forms and results (#386)\n\n* docs: draft specification of the import of Jahia Forms forms and submissions\n\n* docs: the import maps send-to-submitter onto the notification and reports redirects; redirect action proposal\n\n* docs: the Forms import ships results first, and a later form attaches to them\n\nIteration 1 imports the submissions alone, from the formFactory export, with a snapshot of the labels; iteration 2 attaches them to a Formidable form by node name, then label, then by hand. Rebuilding a form from the results and importing the forms become iterations 3 and 4. Dates take the nearest UTC midnight instead of one time zone.\n\n* docs: the Forms import keys a form on its export path, starts from an Import button of the Results page, and fixes the split depth and the date rule\n\n* docs: the Forms import dialog runs a dry run and shows its report before the import, into the current site\n\n* docs: the Forms import lives in the engine with source-agnostic markers, matches a form on its field UUIDs, scopes the attachment to one source, and keeps its jobs in the repository\n\n* docs: the Forms import runs one import per site, keeps the Imported status to never-attached entries, and falls back to the field title and placeholder for its labels\n\n* docs: the Forms import recreates each form in an imported-forms content folder before it writes its results\n\nThe orphan-results state is gone: iteration 1 creates an unpublished Formidable form per Forms form\n(same field names, mapped types, labels from the title or else the placeholder, rules, choices, actions;\nwhat has no equivalent is reported) and writes the submissions as the results of that form, so the Results\npage, the exports and the statuses need no change. Iteration 2 moves the results of one source form onto a\nform built by hand. The import reads the zip export taken with live content, which alone carries the\nresults, the jcr:uuid of every node and the files; forms are keyed by jcr:uuid. One import per site goes\nthrough the scheduler''s job name instead of a claim property; the reader streams the XML.\n\n* docs: the Forms import names each field from its label and says what the Results page shows before the form is published\n\nA recreated field gets the system name the Content Editor would generate from its label\n(your-first-name, not text-input_0_1), unique in the form, with the Forms identity kept on the field\n(fmdbmix:importedField) so a later run writes the values of a renamed field under its new name. The import\nnever publishes: until a contributor publishes a form, its entry shows as Unpublished with the system names\nas columns, the final report says so, and the Cypress spec publishes a form before it checks the labels.\n\n* docs: the Forms import keys a form by its results node too, saves only what Forms saved, and keeps a job''s report until it is read\n\nFour review points: a form deleted in Forms between two exports has no jcr:uuid left, so the form keeps\nthe jcr:uuid of its fcnt:formResults as a second key and a later run matches on either; fmdb:save2jcrAction\nis created only when Forms had a saveToJcrAction, else reported, so no form starts keeping personal data by\nan import''s choice; the jobs run on the persistent scheduler, hence on the processing server, where a\nstopped import resumes with that server, and the Importing state can be closed and found again; the job\nnode keeps its end state and report until Close or one hour, dropping only the file.\n\n* docs: final pass on the Forms import spec\n\nUses the extended inputs where they exist (switch, rating, consent) with the elements fallback; the\ncountry code is the key of the JSON; the results entry is named as SaveToJcrFormAction names it; a dry\nrun keeps its file for the import; Failed can be closed; the applied mappings of iteration 2 have their\nproperty; the attachment has its entry point; a form never published nor submitted has no results node.\n\n* docs: the reserved field names are the request parameters the submission pipeline reads, and a fourth spike covers the fields and files the sample lacks\n\n* docs: spike 1 answered, the import sets jcr:created through the addNode overload the Jahia import uses and creates the split folders itself","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5gFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT+wQAIuRQ/Z0Y7kArU/TDoTGUH9A\nB15cZhvROAfuf/QeCMXVDf99lDdZGYUGXRe/oades+uGw4O4iDfAxzisQKPnNRz4\nR0zw33Oqg0MzNfu9QGhUHKzXetAtJsOS4bdOF+DTScyouyMeMFuC5hWxriWS4NhQ\nq3oc0CFIaxMhxH3vQeIpQyIquq/Gql2BcfWvVfO1PbKgbS9w6oInvrHVu2+7b4nV\nehKJo4izXtDWr+V6fuyUh9CJs2iyHHzVg9RDIip8bLW2aE1c+C0phi+3NJSM60ke\nPlz6wgeS0q8ESdSwR7xWT6CBAbyLBt8m/XK8nxjdO6MU/RgFmDkqZrW87hfcTDDC\nrCdxaLtXbywaB5gapUoh8QeAi4OtDx7ld3qtOTubQu0EWenUdczRcoPVvhpYatjc\nZnE/j+6V1zqnJLTovGUmV3sBVo0GL2ErVIFJ2KzI5tAq54KQI8lSUoAkVUq4VJQX\nYNzYhLyyfqeXtIrflWrbeiuDDHzhMfonHxYjVPSG0wvRU7ZI29D8m5h5Q4heDATy\nLHgVDDS0qDfpEDTd5QeoF9NzdoEL46FLTqx1DURwN6s2o3HKacl6oDoh6sIaekFL\n0YmcGxTxFTu9xg/GogSFNsDLONP5ahQf2qmtd88UDCM1IndVtpqxQ3Ee13EnSPf4\naNx8smRu2AOyTojJYVaU\n=jQjp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T13:17:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/