rmidable/commit/f17cd8204f993766830a3327df229ef2c4e66b4e","sha":"f17cd8204f993766830a3327df229ef2c4e66b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/f17cd8204f993766830a3327df229ef2c4e66b4e"}],"sha":"96c7da1f1b2e0f2f045fb2f1364552309bc39d18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/96c7da1f1b2e0f2f045fb2f1364552309bc39d18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/f17cd8204f993766830a3327df229ef2c4e66b4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:31:56Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:31:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the per-field sensitive flag of the jExperience integration is removed (#379)\n\n* feat: the per-field sensitive flag of the jExperience integration is removed\n\nHDU: remove \"This field is sensitive\". The response block, hence the form\nevent, keeps carrying every answered mappable field, as jExperience''s own\npaths do; nothing holds one back any more.\n\n- engine: profileSensitive leaves fmdbmix:profileMappableField (a bare marker\n  again), FmdbProperty.PROFILE_SENSITIVE, the override hiding it, and\n  ProfileSensitiveFlagMigration with its test.\n- jexperience-engine: the retired fmdbmix:jExperienceSensitiveField and its\n  constants, the override placing the checkbox, the labels and the\n  dropdown''s sensitive message; SensitiveField becomes MappedField (isMapped\n  only); the dropdown, the rule reader, the prefill and the response\n  enricher lose their sensitive branch (the enricher its default-workspace\n  read and withheld names); profileSensitive leaves the mapping''s\n  dependentProperties.\n- playground, tests/README, docs (integration, ownership, layout, upgrade\n  notes, CONTEXT.md), decision logs; changelog 326 reworded, 369 dropped.\n\nNever released (0.4.0 has no jExperience module): nothing is migrated. An\ninstance that ran a 0.5.0 development build refuses the engine (Jahia rates\nthe removed property MAJOR): deploy it with ignoreChecks, then redeploy\nelements and extended-inputs - measured on 8080, the field types then drop\nthe property, a field still holding it reads, saves and publishes normally.\nSuites: engine 505, jexperience 113; all repository checkers green.\n\n* feat: the mapping switch says what it does - Map to the visitor profile\n\nHDU: the switch sat under a section already titled jExperience, so its\nnoun label read twice; it is now the action it performs (fr: Associer au\nprofil visiteur). Labels only: the mixin, its extends and its switch stay,\nsince they let an optional module attach to every mappable field without a\nmixin added on save.\n\n* fix: review of #379 - the retired mixin stays declared, the marker''s reach is said, a test comes back\n\n- fmdbmix:jExperienceSensitiveField and its property stay declared until 0.6,\n  read by nothing: a node a build between #326 and #369 left carrying it\n  would otherwise hold an unknown mixin, which no deploy check flags.\n- upgrade-notes: the development-build procedure (engine once with\n  ignoreChecks, then elements and extended-inputs), next to the others.\n- The third-party guide says the mappable marker sends the field''s answers to\n  jCustomer on a tracked site, with no opt-out; the 2026-09-10 decision row\n  is dated like its siblings.\n- aFormWithNoAnsweredMappableFieldGetsAnEmptyFieldsBlock comes back: it never\n  needed the flag, and without it a mutant dropping an empty block survived.","tree":{"sha":"0ce4bbfe032db2885656f78d1bcaaa0cf63ab180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/0ce4bbfe032db2885656f78d1bcaaa0cf63ab180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/f17cd8204f993766830a3327df229ef2c4e66b4e","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ce4bbfe032db2885656f78d1bcaaa0cf63ab180\nparent 2a924b4835fc9854da4dd989bc0963df8f34322d\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1791217916 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791217916 +0200\n\nfeat: the per-field sensitive flag of the jExperience integration is removed (#379)\n\n* feat: the per-field sensitive flag of the jExperience integration is removed\n\nHDU: remove \"This field is sensitive\". The response block, hence the form\nevent, keeps carrying every answered mappable field, as jExperience''s own\npaths do; nothing holds one back any more.\n\n- engine: profileSensitive leaves fmdbmix:profileMappableField (a bare marker\n  again), FmdbProperty.PROFILE_SENSITIVE, the override hiding it, and\n  ProfileSensitiveFlagMigration with its test.\n- jexperience-engine: the retired fmdbmix:jExperienceSensitiveField and its\n  constants, the override placing the checkbox, the labels and the\n  dropdown''s sensitive message; SensitiveField becomes MappedField (isMapped\n  only); the dropdown, the rule reader, the prefill and the response\n  enricher lose their sensitive branch (the enricher its default-workspace\n  read and withheld names); profileSensitive leaves the mapping''s\n  dependentProperties.\n- playground, tests/README, docs (integration, ownership, layout, upgrade\n  notes, CONTEXT.md), decision logs; changelog 326 reworded, 369 dropped.\n\nNever released (0.4.0 has no jExperience module): nothing is migrated. An\ninstance that ran a 0.5.0 development build refuses the engine (Jahia rates\nthe removed property MAJOR): deploy it with ignoreChecks, then redeploy\nelements and extended-inputs - measured on 8080, the field types then drop\nthe property, a field still holding it reads, saves and publishes normally.\nSuites: engine 505, jexperience 113; all repository checkers green.\n\n* feat: the mapping switch says what it does - Map to the visitor profile\n\nHDU: the switch sat under a section already titled jExperience, so its\nnoun label read twice; it is now the action it performs (fr: Associer au\nprofil visiteur). Labels only: the mixin, its extends and its switch stay,\nsince they let an optional module attach to every mappable field without a\nmixin added on save.\n\n* fix: review of #379 - the retired mixin stays declared, the marker''s reach is said, a test comes back\n\n- fmdbmix:jExperienceSensitiveField and its property stay declared until 0.6,\n  read by nothing: a node a build between #326 and #369 left carrying it\n  would otherwise hold an unknown mixin, which no deploy check flags.\n- upgrade-notes: the development-build procedure (engine once with\n  ignoreChecks, then elements and extended-inputs), next to the others.\n- The third-party guide says the mappable marker sends the field''s answers to\n  jCustomer on a tracked site, with no opt-out; the 2026-09-10 decision row\n  is dated like its siblings.\n- aFormWithNoAnsweredMappableFieldGetsAnEmptyFieldsBlock comes back: it never\n  needed the flag, and without it a mutant dropping an empty block survived.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw9D