420ac12885786c87fb"}],"sha":"2a924b4835fc9854da4dd989bc0963df8f34322d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/2a924b4835fc9854da4dd989bc0963df8f34322d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/2032414d041f75a8b83131420ac12885786c87fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:27:36Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:27:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: the upgrade-only code lives in one migration package, by wave, marked with the version that removes it (#376)\n\n* refactor: the upgrade-only code lives in one migration package, by wave, marked with the version that removes it\n\nEvery class that exists only for an upgrade moves under engine/migration:\nv04 (0.3 -> 0.4 content), v05 (0.4 -> 0.5 content, LegacyConfigurationMigration\nout of config/, and the list-line conversion out of FactoryEntries as\nFormerListLines), common (the shared base, sessions, write flag, markers).\nThe metatype helpers both the migration and the completion use move to\nconfig/common/ConfigurationAttributes.\n\nA source-retention @RemovedIn(\"0.6\") marks those classes and every read\nelsewhere that only keeps content not migrated yet working (retired sensitive\nname, 0.3 choices name, bounds without a mode, the 0.3 options provenance gate,\nthe former-setting warnings); TypeScript carries the same tag in JSDoc.\nNot @Deprecated: the deprecation rules would flag every declaration and use.\n\nThe five migration specs move to tests/cypress/e2e/migrations (80-84).\nNo behaviour change: suites engine 508, jexperience 129, elements 113 green;\nredeployed on a running instance, every migration component active.\n\n* refactor: every 0.6 removal carries the marker, CND declarations included\n\nReview of #376: the claim \"grep @RemovedIn is the 0.6 list\" missed what\nstill said DEPRECATED in prose - FmdbProperty.PROVIDER_ID, JxpMixin''s retired\nsensitive mixin, and the fifteen deprecated CND declarations (now commented\n// @RemovedIn 0.6, with the mandatory flags 0.6 restores). The upgrade notes say\nso, and the jExperience doc quotes the new CND comment. MigrationWrites.begin/end\nsay why they are public; FormerListLines logs under its own name.\n\n* refactor: review of #376 - the holder lint follows MigrationMarker, the migration specs share the site helper\n\n- check-nodetype-names: the static-import guard matches\n  migration.common.MigrationMarker again (it had silently stopped covering it),\n  and its comment and FmdbMixin''s Javadoc name the new path.\n- The upgrade notes say fmdbmix:migratedChoiceOptions clears only at a save:\n  a 0.3 choice field nobody saved keeps it, and what 0.6 must do about such\n  fields (administrator saves them, or a last realignment) is written as an\n  open point; the two Lifecycle notes stop asserting the outcome.\n- The migration specs import the shared useFormidableSite and localDay;\n  migrations/support.ts, a byte-for-byte copy, is gone.","tree":{"sha":"90e248d21ca29912840256b84c309c925c040785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/90e248d21ca29912840256b84c309c925c040785"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/2032414d041f75a8b83131420ac12885786c87fb","verification":{"payload":"tree 90e248d21ca29912840256b84c309c925c040785\nparent 1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1791217656 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791217656 +0200\n\nrefactor: the upgrade-only code lives in one migration package, by wave, marked with the version that removes it (#376)\n\n* refactor: the upgrade-only code lives in one migration package, by wave, marked with the version that removes it\n\nEvery class that exists only for an upgrade moves under engine/migration:\nv04 (0.3 -> 0.4 content), v05 (0.4 -> 0.5 content, LegacyConfigurationMigration\nout of config/, and the list-line conversion out of FactoryEntries as\nFormerListLines), common (the shared base, sessions, write flag, markers).\nThe metatype helpers both the migration and the completion use move to\nconfig/common/ConfigurationAttributes.\n\nA source-retention @RemovedIn(\"0.6\") marks those classes and every read\nelsewhere that only keeps content not migrated yet working (retired sensitive\nname, 0.3 choices name, bounds without a mode, the 0.3 options provenance gate,\nthe former-setting warnings); TypeScript carries the same tag in JSDoc.\nNot @Deprecated: the deprecation rules would flag every declaration and use.\n\nThe five migration specs move to tests/cypress/e2e/migrations (80-84).\nNo behaviour change: suites engine 508, jexperience 129, elements 113 green;\nredeployed on a running instance, every migration component active.\n\n* refactor: every 0.6 removal carries the marker, CND declarations included\n\nReview of #376: the claim \"grep @RemovedIn is the 0.6 list\" missed what\nstill said DEPRECATED in prose - FmdbProperty.PROVIDER_ID, JxpMixin''s retired\nsensitive mixin, and the fifteen deprecated CND declarations (now commented\n// @RemovedIn 0.6, with the mandatory flags 0.6 restores). The upgrade notes say\nso, and the jExperience doc quotes the new CND comment. MigrationWrites.begin/end\nsay why they are public; FormerListLines logs under its own name.\n\n* refactor: review of #376 - the holder lint follows MigrationMarker, the migration specs share the site helper\n\n- check-nodetype-names: the static-import guard matches\n  migration.common.MigrationMarker again (it had silently stopped covering it),\n  and its comment and FmdbMixin''s Javadoc name the new path.\n- The upgrade notes say fmdbmix:migratedChoiceOptions clears only at a save:\n  a 0.3 choice field nobody saved keeps it, and what 0.6 must do about such\n  fields (administrator saves them, or a last realignment) is written as an\n  open point; the two Lifecycle notes stop asserting the outcome.\n- The migration specs import the shared useFormidableSite and localDay;\n  migrations/support.ts, a byte-for-byte copy, is gone.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw8/4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg58QAIObuom8EhyQyCKnnPnHDfa3\na72vfq8Wvs0n/nepeG81n8uOjjUvzOfg5O5PZ4IA4HC+BHdlahUQKek0ffLqApN5\n2aMYop8cjp2t2HxCJXgRTj+5TWYKHy2QQ0yUI8gDESp9K+TiLfOsG4nXA7OKBWdw\n9cYJR3WhGsjSGJNRfIuQz9arXowKOJktZAIQHLY3O5yYmrsQGFOcmrKSNea2BAw/\nkbcT6mFaEST+JGLQJfFTgsDsAYGPg497vjXJsgptk3pflhtCzSiOz/z/b98stPgK\nNyPmGfRotL2WIONIHBHbJateogJcGXJQJNxzZyVajWVohIjZpvAVHbkRtRPlppKp\nDOO4okdw/+9jOzW32QvRYJf69Bidl4cqtUEjidvMiSK15Jpz0WJL/sXPOVi+Il+5\n983PwMs9Cg4yiPrdD3i0ehw0ljbh0kWfGl6Mv3fOHQczl2wIjqc/mKZVhbl1XATY\nUjg1HADr2cM3JHPkEMwOxIyA44cj4mLE/bQa39PgzT0O4FUoABTsCcdLCuh7SNs2\ngyVgUjgeMx5ErStbiP2LZwW5Sca+TJWrHEENJgzXuh3p7+SgijQPyb2zgSdZv74U\nXLBpi1uKHuCO0RKAXOg6b3NDkTFSd6ALbKAUmN0UKZhBcnpA/oyNI9UkPvQU/jAb\nzFpjiBHvYJEkLI05aHs+\n=mUdl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T16:27:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/2032414d041f75a8b83131420ac12885786c87fb","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDIwMzI0MTRkMDQxZjc1YThiODMxMzE0MjBhYzEyODg1Nzg2Yzg3ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b","sha":"1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b"}],"sha":"2032414d041f75a8b83131420ac12885786c87fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/2032414d041f75a8b83131420ac12885786c87fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:26:03Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:26:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the configuration files receive at startup the settings they lack, at their defaults (#374)\n\n* feat: the configuration files receive at startup the settings they lack, at their defaults\n\nA setting added by a later version never reached an existing installation''s\nfile, since Jahia copies a module''s configuration file only once. Every theme\nnow appends the settings its file does not hold, at their defaults, once the\nlegacy migration is over; a value present is never changed, and a complete\nfile is not written (no callback loop). What is missing is read from\nConfigurationAdmin''s copy: the properties DS hands over always hold every\nsetting, bnd writing the definition''s defaults as component properties.\n\nMeasured on a running instance: a removed uploadMaxFileCount came back at its\ndefault, an edited value and the file''s comments were kept, one write only.\n\n* fix: the configuration completion runs once per start and never fails the theme\n\nReview of #374: the completion ran on every callback, so a line an\nadministrator deleted while the module ran was written back at once, under\nthe edit; it now runs once per start of the theme''s service, tried again only\nafter a failed write. A runtime failure of the write (a configuration deleted\nmeanwhile) is caught like an I/O one instead of failing the theme''s\nactivation. Sonar S125: a test comment no longer reads as code.\n\n* test: the completion leaves a complete file alone when a line is deleted while running\n\nReview of #374: done = true on a file already complete carried the\nonce-per-start guarantee in the common case with no test holding it (a\nmutation deleting it went green); a twin of the written-case test now pins\nit. ThemeLifecycle''s Javadoc says the first configuration of each start is\ncompleted, no longer each one.","tree":{"sha":"e073c1e3fe313d6f7d1aa61ab54a7871856fd276","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/e073c1e3fe313d6f7d1aa61ab54a7871856fd276"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b","verification":{"payload":"tree e073c1e3fe313d6f7d1aa61ab54a7871856fd276\nparent 363d7eb2104bc180f99736869235a5c2121ce219\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1791217563 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791217563 +0200\n\nfeat: the configuration files receive at startup the settings they lack, at their defaults (#374)\n\n* feat: the configuration files receive at startup the settings they lack, at their defaults\n\nA setting added by a later version never reached an existing installation''s\nfile, since Jahia copies a module''s configuration file only once. Every theme\nnow appends the settings its file does not hold, at their defaults, once the\nlegacy migration is over; a value present is never changed, and a complete\nfile is not written (no callback loop). What is missing is read from\nConfigurationAdmin''s copy: the properties DS hands over always hold every\nsetting, bnd writing the definition''s defaults as component properties.\n\nMeasured on a running instance: a removed uploadMaxFileCount came back at its\ndefault, an edited value and the file''s comments were kept, one write only.\n\n* fix: the configuration completion runs once per start and never fails the theme\n\nReview of #374: the completion ran on every callback, so a line an\nadministrator deleted while the module ran was written back at once, under\nthe edit; it now runs once per start of the theme''s service, tried again only\nafter a failed write. A runtime failure of the write (a configuration deleted\nmeanwhile) is caught like an I/O one instead of failing the theme''s\nactivation. Sonar S125: a test comment no longer reads as code.\n\n* test: the completion leaves a complete file alone when a line is deleted while running\n\nReview of #374: done = true on a file already complete carried the\nonce-per-start guarantee in the common case with no test holding it (a\nmutation deleting it went green); a twin of the written-case test now pins\nit. ThemeLifecycle''s Javadoc says the first configuration of each start is\ncompleted, no longer each one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw8+bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwxAQAACV6GlnyzmK6Yl31uDQa/V3\nmRU73et6QY4VuqQEsChtyO5/273uP5Ae+xGCd7aIgKFgq9v/ocvPwKs/vGTWEbWP\n6CfMJnp7rjsLTbJULrBHEsCxleNi5PjPxsMQn+ltkXT/C7YAJVD4ntOohkdWnRsk\nTIpp1/Z5WB22XgW11LfN9kDHQujEVj4qJSM+7DZ5xP5UyZKmCHrIitYHkjF6osBQ\ns39NFm4drPq/fZPn8HB6eXA4QwxNUFx+GWem7ZwouJAR+4o9Ri8bucyG7ZnJPCmh\n8mS2Adl0AFMEh+EI5mUYSGKgn7bmmPssPIkUSjOBqG9ho/eXCOhBjF7cVuu64Xzd\nw5SxBTVjK0PUyEbC+RqzPwztxV6kkvYGUxzGkC7llNffKGIUwV6n6NfRV/C2Mf4N\nOL+rZ3YgUIXGRfAia8fnJdFPm3ZufvAsSAuvEuAbmS1w0X0hijAe2yIYy6oVhF3b\nvfwHOI6FcXFFGMoJygKz86GqR6u9YpunJvqTp2iZxbOpgrDBcL86jkfkmlXFKrAo\nnJcy9NCVNd41kXssyl7gGgd//icYZOP9Qzf4pUX5KXbWZ+U4rYSYnakD3mJ485B2\nFozwbqfkVpSTu0/AR52A0S2M6hPgevoY1gwGhpAPPME8uLtnYP1+RiDPP0icHNcc\nbScpRFBRImzPP4VeBypO\n=kwUK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T16:26:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDFhM2NlMDhiODUxMGM3YWRjMzczOTU5ODk3YWYxZTRjYmZkN2NjN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/363d7eb2104bc180f99736869235a5c2121ce219","sha":"363d7eb2104bc180f99736869235a5c2121ce219","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/363d7eb2104bc180f99736869235a5c2121ce219"}],"sha":"1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1a3ce08b8510c7adc373959897af1e4cbfd7cc7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/363d7eb2104bc180f99736869235a5c2121ce219/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:28:54Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:28:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the form editor loses the Multi-step section and the children block, and the validation messages say their note once (#371)\n\n* feat: the form editor loses the Multi-step section and the children block, and the validation messages say their note once\n\nThe steps bar switch, the only setting of the Multi-step section, joins the Step navigation fieldset of\nButtons, before the Previous/Next labels it governs (closes #150). The editor''s children block is hidden\non the form: its children are the field and action lists, nothing a contributor orders. Under Validation\nmessages, one sentence says that a message left empty keeps the browser''s — a fieldset descriptionKey,\ntranslated like a label — instead of the same line under each of the nine messages. The playground\nenables the TSX sample module on its site when it is deployed, so its help text position setting shows.\n\n* fix: the sensitive flag opens the jExperience section without a \"Privacy\" heading over its one checkbox\n\nA fieldset without labelKey renders its field alone (HDU, on the editor of a text field).\n\n* feat: the \"Logic\" section is \"Conditional display\", its fieldset \"Display rules\"\n\nThe rules only show or hide the field (HDU); the technical section name stays, so overrides and specs are untouched.\n\n* feat: the Conditional display rules sit right under the section title, the sentence on what they do on the section\n\nThree titles for one control (HDU): the fieldset is untitled, the section carries the generic sentence through\nits descriptionKey, and the Rules tooltip says what a rule compares — a field placed before, of any value kind,\nor a page value.\n\n* feat: the Multiple emails switch opens the Value & input fieldset of an email field\n\nIt changes what the field accepts (HDU), before the placeholder and the default value it then applies to.\n\n* feat: the Multiple emails switch is in Content after Required, and the Conditional display sentence renders under the section title\n\nmultiple defines what a field accepts and submits, so it is Content on the three types that have it (HDU: the\nselect and the file field already had it there; the email field was the exception). The editor ignores a\nsection description (measured): the sentence goes on the untitled fieldset, which renders it right under the\nsection title.\n\n* feat: the settings of a field action sit right under Configuration, without a fieldset title\n\nA section with one fieldset showed three titles for one group (HDU); the fieldset is untitled, as the rules under\nConditional display.\n\n* feat: the Conditional display rules carry their one sentence in the Rules tooltip, no fieldset description\n\nA fieldset description under the section title read as one more layer (HDU); the tooltip says when the field\nshows and what a rule compares, in two sentences.\n\n* fix: the Results page says \"Form unpublished\" and \"Form deleted\", not where\n\nA form with results was live: it is unpublished or deleted, and neither happens \"in jContent\" (HDU).\n\n* feat: deleting all results says once, under the count, that the form leaves the list\n\nThe checkbox reads \"All results\" (HDU); the sentence under it tells, per state of the form, when it comes back.\n\n* docs: the Results page labels read \"Form deleted\" and \"Form unpublished\" in the docs and the playground too\n\nReview of #371.\n\n* fix: the Conditional display and field-action fieldsets keep their type names, which the editor builds its field ids from\n\nThe Content Editor names each field <fieldset>_<property>; renaming the fieldsets to \"rules\" and \"feedback\" broke\nfmdbmix:formLogicElement_logics, the selector specs 50 and 216 use (CI of #371). Untitled either way.\n\n* fix: the fieldsets stay \"rules\" and \"feedback\", untitled, and the specs select the rules field as rules_logics\n\nA type-named fieldset without labelKey takes the type label as title, so the previous commit put a title back;\nthe Content Editor names a field <fieldset>_<property>, so the page object follows the fieldset (CI of #371,\nspecs 50 and 216).","tree":{"sha":"9ca1d658b15590e400be9d45785590cffc77befb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/9ca1d658b15590e400be9d45785590cffc77befb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/363d7eb2104bc180f99736869235a5c2121ce219","verification":{"payload":"tree 9ca1d658b15590e400be9d45785590cffc77befb\nparent 22619388f47de7c3ad8eb7c3ccbe4ca7e2d4e41f\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790987334 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790987334 +0200\n\nfeat: the form editor loses the Multi-step section and the children block, and the validation messages say their note once (#371)\n\n* feat: the form editor loses the Multi-step section and the children block, and the validation messages say their note once\n\nThe steps bar switch, the only setting of the Multi-step section, joins the Step navigation fieldset of\nButtons, before the Previous/Next labels it governs (closes #150). The editor''s children block is hidden\non the form: its children are the field and action lists, nothing a contributor orders. Under Validation\nmessages, one sentence says that a message left empty keeps the browser''s — a fieldset descriptionKey,\ntranslated like a label — instead of the same line under each of the nine messages. The playground\nenables the TSX sample module on its site when it is deployed, so its help text position setting shows.\n\n* fix: the sensitive flag opens the jExperience section without a \"Privacy\" heading over its one checkbox\n\nA fieldset without labelKey renders its field alone (HDU, on the editor of a text field).\n\n* feat: the \"Logic\" section is \"Conditional display\", its fieldset \"Display rules\"\n\nThe rules only show or hide the field (HDU); the technical section name stays, so overrides and specs are untouched.\n\n* feat: the Conditional display rules sit right under the section title, the sentence on what they do on the section\n\nThree titles for one control (HDU): the fieldset is untitled, the section carries the generic sentence through\nits descriptionKey, and the Rules tooltip says what a rule compares — a field placed before, of any value kind,\nor a page value.\n\n* feat: the Multiple emails switch opens the Value & input fieldset of an email field\n\nIt changes what the field accepts (HDU), before the placeholder and the default value it then applies to.\n\n* feat: the Multiple emails switch is in Content after Required, and the Conditional display sentence renders under the section title\n\nmultiple defines what a field accepts and submits, so it is Content on the three types that have it (HDU: the\nselect and the file field already had it there; the email field was the exception). The editor ignores a\nsection description (measured): the sentence goes on the untitled fieldset, which renders it right under the\nsection title.\n\n* feat: the settings of a field action sit right under Configuration, without a fieldset title\n\nA section with one fieldset showed three titles for one group (HDU); the fieldset is untitled, as the rules under\nConditional display.\n\n* feat: the Conditional display rules carry their one sentence in the Rules tooltip, no fieldset description\n\nA fieldset description under the section title read as one more layer (HDU); the tooltip says when the field\nshows and what a rule compares, in two sentences.\n\n* fix: the Results page says \"Form unpublished\" and \"Form deleted\", not where\n\nA form with results was live: it is unpublished or deleted, and neither happens \"in jContent\" (HDU).\n\n* feat: deleting all results says once, under the count, that the form leaves the list\n\nThe checkbox reads \"All results\" (HDU); the sentence under it tells, per state of the form, when it comes back.\n\n* docs: the Results page labels read \"Form deleted\" and \"Form unpublished\" in the docs and the playground too\n\nReview of #371.\n\n* fix: the Conditional display and field-action fieldsets keep their type names, which the editor builds its field ids from\n\nThe Content Editor names each field <fieldset>_<property>; renaming the fieldsets to \"rules\" and \"feedback\" broke\nfmdbmix:formLogicElement_logics, the selector specs 50 and 216 use (CI of #371). Untitled either way.\n\n* fix: the fieldsets stay \"rules\" and \"feedback\", untitled, and the specs select the rules field as rules_logics\n\nA type-named fieldset without labelKey takes the type label as title, so the previous commit put a title back;\nthe Content Editor names a field <fieldset>_<property>, so the page object follows the fieldset (CI of #371,\nspecs 50 and 216).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwExGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4yIQAIelFB2VldQ3K9IGZpPfHpcr\nU6c0Uy/y/waUq4zyLfQ0iU9vBKp4dD+ygjrcnVGn12m66aC8bPztpXEMtuq8yeq1\n56U1x86Y8ym+Ph4vHP26uZkQ+k2KbfRtxeA4FW3eJIpDlgGxoE+Qon5CL7QGt7jI\nX4MssgmoHy8ShwY/1Gl1LkvjWRIQfX8cr5UA9AKByNMY6KB+Ee63Wf4GU20E86S8\nMk4pz7KaV6Tcu+in85mlD4m4F