s://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/363d7eb2104bc180f99736869235a5c2121ce219"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/22619388f47de7c3ad8eb7c3ccbe4ca7e2d4e41f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:21:07Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:21:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the arrow keys cross the Results page, up and down along the forms, right and left between forms and submissions (#373)\n\n* feat: the arrow keys cross the Results page — up and down along the forms, right and left between the forms and their submissions\n\nThe table already moved its selection with up and down; the list of forms now does the same (the selected\nentry takes the focus, so the next arrow continues from it), right from the list lands on the table — its\nselected row when there is one — and left from the table lands on the selected form (HDU). One helper,\nnextEntryIndex, steps through both lists; spec 75 presses the keys.\n\n* fix: the right arrow from the list selects the first submission and focuses its row\n\nFocusing the table itself showed nothing (HDU): the table registers the way in — the selected row, or the first\nsubmission selected on the way — and the app calls it.\n\n* fix: the arrow keys are handled on the entries and the rows, the native interactive elements, not on the lists around them\n\nSonar S6848 on #373: a div with a key handler is a non-native interactive element. The list buttons take the\nhandler; the table rows take it with a roving tabindex — the selected row is the one Tab reaches, or the first.\n\n* fix: a right arrow pressed while the submissions still load lands on the first one once they are there\n\n* fix: a right arrow waits only for a load in progress, and a pending move never outlives its form\n\nReview of #373: on a form with no submission the pending flag stayed set and pulled the focus into the table\nwhen the next form loaded.\n\n* refactor: the roving tab stop is a named predicate, not a nested ternary (Sonar S3358 on #373)","tree":{"sha":"f960e5fa65016686c60865f8d913732073f4919d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/f960e5fa65016686c60865f8d913732073f4919d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/22619388f47de7c3ad8eb7c3ccbe4ca7e2d4e41f","verification":{"payload":"tree f960e5fa65016686c60865f8d913732073f4919d\nparent 07e03b623cd8edc23f3928b95a9871fc35adf6f2\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790986867 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790986867 +0200\n\nfeat: the arrow keys cross the Results page, up and down along the forms, right and left between forms and submissions (#373)\n\n* feat: the arrow keys cross the Results page — up and down along the forms, right and left between the forms and their submissions\n\nThe table already moved its selection with up and down; the list of forms now does the same (the selected\nentry takes the focus, so the next arrow continues from it), right from the list lands on the table — its\nselected row when there is one — and left from the table lands on the selected form (HDU). One helper,\nnextEntryIndex, steps through both lists; spec 75 presses the keys.\n\n* fix: the right arrow from the list selects the first submission and focuses its row\n\nFocusing the table itself showed nothing (HDU): the table registers the way in — the selected row, or the first\nsubmission selected on the way — and the app calls it.\n\n* fix: the arrow keys are handled on the entries and the rows, the native interactive elements, not on the lists around them\n\nSonar S6848 on #373: a div with a key handler is a non-native interactive element. The list buttons take the\nhandler; the table rows take it with a roving tabindex — the selected row is the one Tab reaches, or the first.\n\n* fix: a right arrow pressed while the submissions still load lands on the first one once they are there\n\n* fix: a right arrow waits only for a load in progress, and a pending move never outlives its form\n\nReview of #373: on a form with no submission the pending flag stayed set and pulled the focus into the table\nwhen the next form loaded.\n\n* refactor: the roving tab stop is a named predicate, not a nested ternary (Sonar S3358 on #373)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwEpzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYqMQAH+ecnLI8SAKH8lh9S5xAHbP\nviL4J2Boa15QsWapGg69BwLqEbDq1pGOS6K4swwOQP8pSvsqo8G+UAALZNSPZ5SS\nlO3exCiOeYlIFx4A6yi2zs3KFL3KW7+0M5se2Ck1hisFIHZO8JUU5YrEj63B7FCG\nFkRfCTZzLQqKxkH4hUhWpH0pFdkOsOzCRLGpgsh+GLnXdLdzaK7X8YlV9dWRqp4G\nrWRqP/mz/Yfe0w6nTJgG6G5NkxP9K4TfTxl7jeTWtP8F5OVQOTkr2Xv/oZ7+AAt/\nK0Mv+oc7FauSBXj5CVcN6Vz7OwDSPXSG/3dSsIcg12rEKQDXWrUf8/nN0DHADLpj\nE4p/tbHbHrk4GRtPobYXe9PI+6oFqlT9ONy1sdwd+0UCA8fWp5T19Sg3zUqTChKy\nVL/CLbb+i62eLEvMdoXwoZkOa7crO8xsvQJ3K54zrUno9EKtuR/7Vi/kM55BWi/N\nDU9VEMU9v3DfZzYy3EMLRlz5VGp