//api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/07e03b623cd8edc23f3928b95a9871fc35adf6f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T23:57:10Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T23:57:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: the rules editor reads a field''s sources once, in one request, shared by its rule rows (#372)\n\n* perf: the rules editor reads a field''s sources once, in one request, shared by its rule rows\n\nMeasured on 8.2.4 (2026-10-02, a field of the complete playground form): the two queries of each rule\nrow left the browser about a second after being issued — the editor client''s batching window, paid\ntwice in sequence — while the server answered in 20 to 35 ms; a field with three rules waited six\nseconds, and adding a rule two more. One GraphQL operation now reads the field, its rule references\nand, under its form ancestor, the form tree (the site default language comes from the editor\ncontext), posted directly to the endpoint; one load per edited field is shared by every rule row\n(acquire on mount, release on unmount, a grace for the editor''s remount storm), so adding a rule\ncosts no request and closing the editor forgets the form. Measured after: adding a rule renders its\nrow at once, without a request; opening the editor costs one request of 190 ms.\n\n* refactor: the rules editor assembles a shared-sources hook and pure row helpers\n\nReview of #372 (SonarQube: cognitive complexity 35 for the component, 15 allowed): useSharedSources holds\nthe load by its key and derives loading and the error from what answered (sharedSourcesView, pure);\nruleRow.ts decides which value control the row shows, the source type, the provider reference error and\nthe reserved line''s message. Both tested; the component keeps one branch, the loader.\n\n* refactor: no nested ternary for the scalar input type, an optional chain on the held load (Sonar S3358, S6582 on #372)","tree":{"sha":"10425cd2bc58324c964e9817c99696038c1888fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/10425cd2bc58324c964e9817c99696038c1888fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/07e03b623cd8edc23f3928b95a9871fc35adf6f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 10425cd2bc58324c964e9817c99696038c1888fb\nparent 9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790985430 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790985430 +0200\n\nperf: the rules editor reads a field''s sources once, in one request, shared by its rule rows (#372)\n\n* perf: the rules editor reads a field''s sources once, in one request, shared by its rule rows\n\nMeasured on 8.2.4 (2026-10-02, a field of the complete playground form): the two queries of each rule\nrow left the browser about a second after being issued — the editor client''s batching window, paid\ntwice in sequence — while the server answered in 20 to 35 ms; a field with three rules waited six\nseconds, and adding a rule two more. One GraphQL operation now reads the field, its rule references\nand, under its form ancestor, the form tree (the site default language comes from the editor\ncontext), posted directly to the endpoint; one load per edited field is shared by every rule row\n(acquire on mount, release on unmount, a grace for the editor''s remount storm), so adding a rule\ncosts no request and closing the editor forgets the form. Measured after: adding a rule renders its\nrow at once, without a request; opening the editor costs one request of 190 ms.\n\n* refactor: the rules editor assembles a shared-sources hook and pure row helpers\n\nReview of #372 (SonarQube: cognitive complexity 35 for the component, 15 allowed): useSharedSources holds\nthe load by its key and derives loading and the error from what answered (sharedSourcesView, pure);\nruleRow.ts decides which value control the row shows, the source type, the provider reference error and\nthe reserved line''s message. Both tested; the component keeps one branch, the loader.\n\n* refactor: no nested ternary for the scalar input type, an optional chain on the held load (Sonar S3358, S6582 on #372)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwETWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtycQAGQJaO7WVVhT5V3MUZXKlqv6\nuDT4G7VHwcrFMKch7o/Dw2SkqvU4Juc1xBHrfCQssm7hFnny8SHXM6bWdDgHt6Xc\nlxruoonGWjAvIU0SpvwOh0vezZM0dIw4w6vq0hJax1GAGs53c3xouayvobrbmZOP\nOeHI4D+00cP3xti6MeSNnv/g3BTrgzu5lNnKEPLMdn08cWKU897qSwof5VPOqf+v\n6TWvj1bAZqmnRAdE/Sw3NdTWqSBuQK5K+Nnbl3qYvytWB3gTH6t8PNftDRj8YUty\n4A2PN6spynYd62Hd8M8Hv/J540J13TvqrvdshJT1O8Z9ylhSIsWZ2zZYc/eJlOk6\n7Rdk84lIvvjv6W/Jog7GSimoaDCw21rjL8gbVKCJ1atAbUQ838YoeAt4G6Z9Zpyk\noKKQEYza/dTgAJaUkQlXkW63ZsbJ8xGrtYnhaQvMl2Iv7IQUCH+dNV4wuhMRqmKT\nd4qfIOHO2bN9yMcM4GLios4gve2E7BbmERIQ3obz0aXjAR1cT4jH/apLh+ofm3cx\nC2Xq5JPtfsjUH9gO3S+T7gODfXvt+4H1xXE0osepNbt1I9JPjdhk+o7m3USgcVWj\nCidU4bbyPRj2nSuq8rYfRdgNOU/YWO4vJDGqaHRYaXgt+VKM9dBlZ97x5KA7yEA5\nVd4ucDdeJi0CGtiV3g8p\n=W68P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T23:57:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/07e03b623cd8edc23f3928b95a9871fc35adf6f2","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDA3ZTAzYjYyM2NkOGVkYzIzZjM5MjhiOTVhOTg3MWZjMzVhZGY2ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a","sha":"9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a"}],"sha":"07e03b623cd8edc23f3928b95a9871fc35adf6f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/07e03b623cd8edc23f3928b95a9871fc35adf6f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:39:04Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:39:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: the sensitive flag of a field is a property of the engine''s marker, not an always-activated jExperience mixin (#369)\n\n* fix: the sensitive flag of a field is a property of the engine''s marker, not an always-activated jExperience mixin\n\nThe author''s \"keep this field''s value out of the visitor profile\" was jExperienceSensitive on\nfmdbmix:jExperienceSensitiveField, a mixin of formidable-jexperience-engine attached to the engine''s\nmarker with `extends` and kept always activated: the editor added it to every mappable field on save,\nwhich a translator''s role cannot do (#365, the finding of #359). The flag is profileSensitive on\nfmdbmix:profileMappableField now — every mappable field has it, nothing to add on save. The engine\ndeclares it and acts on it nowhere: its own override hides it, and the jExperience module''s override of\nthe same type shows it in its section with its labels. The retired mixin stays declared, hidden and\ndetached, until 0.6; ProfileSensitiveFlagMigration (engine) moves the values and drops it in both\nworkspaces, deferring a field until formidable-elements and the jExperience module are redeployed and\nre-running on both. The module''s code reads FmdbProperty.PROFILE_SENSITIVE; the playground sets the\nflag without a mixin.\n\n* fix: the sensitive flag is read under both its names until 0.6, so a field waiting for the migration never fails open\n\nReview of #369: in the upgrade order (engine, jExperience, elements) ProfileSensitiveFlagMigration defers\nevery field until formidable-elements is redeployed, and a field still carrying jExperienceSensitive read\nas not sensitive meanwhile — the enricher would have sent its value to the profile, which cannot be taken\nback. SensitiveField reads the engine''s flag or the retired one; the migration stays the cleanup. The wave\nparagraph of the upgrade notes names the three 0.5.0 migrations.","tree":{"sha":"9f5e2bf704ae5fdccb07cfd5570b11e8e547c895","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/9f5e2bf704ae5fdccb07cfd5570b11e8e547c895"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f5e2bf704ae5fdccb07cfd5570b11e8e547c895\nparent ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790969944 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790969944 +0200\n\nfix: the sensitive flag of a field is a property of the engine''s marker, not an always-activated jExperience mixin (#369)\n\n* fix: the sensitive flag of a field is a property of the engine''s marker, not an always-activated jExperience mixin\n\nThe author''s \"keep this field''s value out of the visitor profile\" was jExperienceSensitive on\nfmdbmix:jExperienceSensitiveField, a mixin of formidable-jexperience-engine attached to the engine''s\nmarker with `extends` and kept always activated: the editor added it to every mappable field on save,\nwhich a translator''s role cannot do (#365, the finding of #359). The flag is profileSensitive on\nfmdbmix:profileMappableField now — every mappable field has it, nothing to add on save. The engine\ndeclares it and acts on it nowhere: its own override hides it, and the jExperience module''s override of\nthe same type shows it in its section with its labels. The retired mixin stays declared, hidden and\ndetached, until 0.6; ProfileSensitiveFlagMigration (engine) moves the values and drops it in both\nworkspaces, deferring a field until formidable-elements and the jExperience module are redeployed and\nre-running on both. The module''s code reads FmdbProperty.PROFILE_SENSITIVE; the playground sets the\nflag without a mixin.\n\n* fix: the sensitive flag is read under both its names until 0.6, so a field waiting for the migration never fails open\n\nReview of #369: in the upgrade order (engine, jExperience, elements) ProfileSensitiveFlagMigration defers\nevery field until formidable-elements is redeployed, and a field still carrying jExperienceSensitive read\nas not sensitive meanwhile — the enricher would have sent its value to the profile, which cannot be taken\nback. SensitiveField reads the engine''s flag or the retired one; the migration stays the cleanup. The wave\nparagraph of the upgrade notes names the three 0.5.0 migrations.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwAhYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtA4QAKdIuBI5kLNRFW3IpOZjlBLl\nNx31YJPRJMMLyKU7YzEBuNpBkxSsk/YhbK/FAdIGAj0GwUYE8DMBNEfdFWEavBld\noiE+tArwMcadCsBhcF1c/n+t71GPDHHZrKOH1vZFYJT6hWyg/vurEEK2kQbFERb7\niVdpJDGiY2SydCZvvfWj5/i3g/N7W9LRcOMENmexr3rlWa79deaS9FhKPXzT4WNl\noNSrqtBq9EMyyJlhJCN4UgU52ObEzeL8OIFIrwiaBPFzoa0tO+uuVdsrmG8HdOLJ\nTHa+QtboKkv5CPiFtWv/rWVw7ZoUXm7pYC5jBjoW97bneCBVz3IX4TFZTfdXRHu+\nvTUk9TCEkQ10ZFY6wGv5k/ONfdwepgL+uljqeKh/aUpsOsLKGrs/FCMOKptGBQuk\naGusCw4AfCIPmyTbk5Le0nbA5na+5v10NN2EWYzl9yjaR+ijTqdQ5XqWvrLk/tE9\nG59S6TDq4ZsiGRtTnzBFXwL3F6OqvcFCmlPoNsnJynna4xrLtleyEYC48gqlImYv\nIWquIOmjut1JC9qc3EN+Zm2hOkfRUtQwAiM7uVEjYRY5sR4jsXm6eaMl3XZi9yGp\n5B9yUOJVJRIVql0LsDNOmWu8NQM0oLF4wmC8ZwNSZ1ljwo7m32MuiB7PLM4DwO4l\ns2jqbAAhGTCSzIUqCIRg\n=N8tY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T19:39:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDk3MzYxNDcxNjFlMmFkZWIzZWE5MDU5MzUxYWYxYzU3YzY4MTlkOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673","sha":"ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673"}],"sha":"9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/9736147161e2adeb3ea9059351af1c57c6819d9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:37:33Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:37:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: the behaviour and message settings of a field action come with its type, not with an always-activated mixin (#368)\n\n* fix: the behaviour and message settings of a field action come with its type, not with an always-activated mixin\n\nfmdbmix:fieldActionFeedback becomes a supertype of the fmdbmix:fieldAction marker instead of a mixin\nattached to it with `extends` and kept always activated in the editor: the editor added the mixin to\nevery existing action on save, which a translator''s role cannot do (the finding of #359 on the field\nsettings, carried over by #365). Every field-action type inherits the four settings through the marker,\nnothing to add on save, defaults shown. The name stays, since Jackrabbit refuses a node whose primary\ntype and mixin declare the same property; the actions saved before still list the mixin, and the\nmigration drops it — AdvancedSettingsMixinMigration renamed RedundantMixinMigration, as it now serves\ntwo families. ResolvedFieldAction reads the settings without asking for the mixin; the Cypress fixtures\nstop pushing it.\n\n* docs: the startup-migrations wave paragraph names RedundantMixinMigration\n\nReview of #368: the row was renamed, the wave paragraph above it still listed the old class name.","tree":{"sha":"d53b69028781c0ff1b72a01cd1a4e2a6b623b29d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/d53b69028781c0ff1b72a01cd1a4e2a6b623b29d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673","verification":{"payload":"tree d53b69028781c0ff1b72a01cd1a4e2a6b623b29d\nparent 9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790969853 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790969853 +0200\n\nfix: the behaviour and message settings of a field action come with its type, not with an always-activated mixin (#368)\n\n* fix: the behaviour and message settings of a field action come with its type, not with an always-activated mixin\n\nfmdbmix:fieldActionFeedback becomes a supertype of the fmdbmix:fieldAction marker instead of a mixin\nattached to it with `extends` and kept always activated in the editor: the editor added the mixin to\nevery existing action on save, which a translator''s role cannot do (the finding of #359 on the field\nsettings, carried over by #365). Every field-action type inherits the four settings through the marker,\nnothing to add on save, defaults shown. The name stays, since Jackrabbit refuses a node whose primary\ntype and mixin declare the same property; the actions saved before still list the mixin, and the\nmigration drops it — AdvancedSettingsMixinMigration renamed RedundantMixinMigration, as it now serves\ntwo families. ResolvedFieldAction reads the settings without asking for the mixin; the Cypress fixtures\nstop pushing it.\n\n* docs: the startup-migrations wave paragraph names RedundantMixinMigration\n\nReview of #368: the row was renamed, the wave paragraph above it still listed the old class name.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwAf9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjWQQABA/H52uSqZjU5eCIHEcBavz\nf3XeT9ky4UBsa0lhj8UD+SiBtPMqya7nTH6KwWwDHt+mnCAakFbyHKD7ewkdiOjS\n/z/OBLErva4lcJHmb9n/s+s93Kcklkj7dZ/P+givxvHisnjzCdU5UrvzBNjaD3kB\n5k6hO/xxZIn360aQEMNeTNUrPTKmU6ogbxooUEoFcOzoBDN7FV3EWYMFltfPrjpx\nIRH0nuyEPsRS43wp5oAefDuiNaei48qEdX6LjV59xnGst1hB6c+CB8oOqFyfLPPU\nQ+loh/7o9M1ye2QtXKXihT4HyRfj98zqZM1du+w7YylPWCuSIjliTiFfwHu+uyml\nQuKhpAqcSB/Msw8KajzRq8GlzTtyA+Fjhc2UiKLjWkFFWM6/+XUdPewf3SINV5QC\nbVwTdnKy9jPO7SoVrw2UdjmzWStzKKq4pfuVQ95e8skpuO2uI5masSaHMdXoTQoy\n64QIp5j/0d+39H9xKceCf8lk5Ef6upgrmONrLYVqDKJY1z4CRYbg9h2sToHm1UbT\n39U1a++tP/GUXlkwBeoGS0ncVYLxQuGacVVKxk5+UP30nj9KAsfvRUmrA/KLfIET\nKcVZuP3K+yC94kBpAUORWoPY9y9sHt+5XWBmcVnJ42iEGY/lfd5UeoXzGq5g6knD\n7RYcqehGB0/9YkubCkGF\n=o4de\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T19:37:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGJhN2NkOWU5NjdlODAxZTFjZjQyZGRiYTc1MjFmOGM4ZjAyMjc2NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70","sha":"9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70"}],"sha":"ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/ba7cd9e967e801e1cf42ddba7521f8c8f0227673"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:16:00Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:16:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: the Results list marks a deleted or unpublished form by the colour of its icon (#367)\n\n* fix: the Results list marks a deleted or unpublished form by the colour of its icon, not a chip\n\nIn a 280px column the chip ate the title (\"Plain - Unp…\") and on its own line read as a second\nentry. The form icon turns red for a deleted form and orange for an unpublished one; the words\nstay in the icon''s tooltip and accessible name, and in the header''s chip once the entry is\nselected, so the status is never carried by colour alone.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the Results list status icon (#367)\n\n* fix: the header chip takes the colours of the list icon — orange for an unpublished form, red for a deleted one (#367)\n\n* test: the playground leaves an emptied results entry too — a form whose only submission was deleted\n\n* test: the playground''s emptying assertion is a call, not a bare expression (lint)\n\n* fix: the whole-entry checkbox says the form leaves the page (#367)\n\n* fix: the Results list is titled Form results, and its flags say the form is deleted or unpublished in jContent (#367)\n\n* fix: the deletion dialog speaks of the form results leaving the page, not of the form (#367)\n\n* fix: the Download control of a submission file no longer takes the browser''s link colour (#367)\n\n* fix: the Export and Delete actions of the Results page say on hover what they act on — the selected form results (#367)\n\n* fix: the deletion dialog''s warning box uses Moonstone''s warning tokens — the icon in warning yellow, a background variable that exists (#367)\n\n* feat: a click on the selected form results deselects them; spec 75 selects an entry only when it is not yet (#367)\n\n* fix: the status icon''s accessible name is a visually hidden text, not an img role on a span (Sonar S6819, #367)\n\n* fix: the Results header keeps its height — the subtitle line is always there, as tall as the status chip (#367)\n\n* fix: the Results list is titled Forms with results, not an echo of the page heading (#367 review)\n\n* fix: the Download control of the file preview dialog no longer takes the browser''s link colour either (#367)\n\n* fix: every JCR node the Results page selects carries its identity, so jContent''s Apollo cache can key it (console: missing fields uuid,workspace) (#367)\n\n* fix: the conditional-logic queries select the identity of the logic source nodes and their references too (#367)","tree":{"sha":"7d6ed4e4e698998f702402d259bda4071d20444d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/7d6ed4e4e698998f702402d259bda4071d20444d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d6ed4e4e698998f702402d259bda4071d20444d\nparent c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790964960 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790964960 +0200\n\nfix: the Results list marks a deleted or unpublished form by the colour of its icon (#367)\n\n* fix: the Results list marks a deleted or unpublished form by the colour of its icon, not a chip\n\nIn a 280px column the chip ate the title (\"Plain - Unp…\") and on its own line read as a second\nentry. The form icon turns red for a deleted form and orange for an unpublished one; the words\nstay in the icon''s tooltip and accessible name, and in the header''s chip once the entry is\nselected, so the status is never carried by colour alone.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the Results list status icon (#367)\n\n* fix: the header chip takes the colours of the list icon — orange for an unpublished form, red for a deleted one (#367)\n\n* test: the playground leaves an emptied results entry too — a form whose only submission was deleted\n\n* test: the playground''s emptying assertion is a call, not a bare expression (lint)\n\n* fix: the whole-entry checkbox says the form leaves the page (#367)\n\n* fix: the Results list is titled Form results, and its flags say the form is deleted or unpublished in jContent (#367)\n\n* fix: the deletion dialog speaks of the form results leaving the page, not of the form (#367)\n\n* fix: the Download control of a submission file no longer takes the browser''s link colour (#367)\n\n* fix: the Export and Delete actions of the Results page say on hover what they act on — the selected form results (#367)\n\n* fix: the deletion dialog''s warning box uses Moonstone''s warning tokens — the icon in warning yellow, a background variable that exists (#367)\n\n* feat: a click on the selected form results deselects them; spec 75 selects an entry only when it is not yet (#367)\n\n* fix: the status icon''s accessible name is a visually hidden text, not an img role on a span (Sonar S6819, #367)\n\n* fix: the Results header keeps its height — the subtitle line is always there, as tall as the status chip (#367)\n\n* fix: the Results list is titled Forms with results, not an echo of the page heading (#367 review)\n\n* fix: the Download control of the file preview dialog no longer takes the browser''s link colour either (#367)\n\n* fix: every JCR node the Results page selects carries its identity, so jContent''s Apollo cache can key it (console: missing fields uuid,workspace) (#367)\n\n* fix: the conditional-logic queries select the identity of the logic source nodes and their references too (#367)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv/TgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADn0QAE5yyX8oC2RAgMgHx4IumZJv\nJxjepIi1zvPuXdeFBxZFFcEo8SMrKoeZcuX8DDJZGxNIsKUuZK518UNUqmQjOhnG\n8G10Hlym2xuGdp1q3XGpE9rspNJRH7256y95cY66GsNGBYD1/XW6chyMOjX8KRdp\nbSC08rJ6P2SVAsUa2VHgbllFVo+BNLtXeJDVmk86mArsO0h4fi8j/po0/qJJgKf6\nW5TePgbtNsPfDem8wl3icd4Q2zcF/9fbLnzJGj7YUOWuZSFyvynD1A/fG+LdiTe7\nrgo3BRIRK7ZHL4IOd5192TG5wEs8PTGDyS/3o1lUNJn97G2oPoshpgjFEA4VL4Dz\nITTWnDvwYYh/CC1Ca6H8kf3cFQ/mKvfKo6sVAZuKbo9FaouOD8PkgDXed5GS8TBQ\nyOwmPihEFDJ3SiH1Gm2R2uD040miSJqVJar7mX5aeMqfkeTWbdUH2Oi2owP3QePA\naNTJqEX118PaZ8l594heVubgoMN2S+q+hDhxJeOIJdQHq/ysjEONQPmSgTHNgA8D\nVA+jUExazoJaDMuRseuVFJvmqC6js8+KgZ2sS5Jipmi+22s5f2RAvDoyIeuksARi\nstQnt/GpNN4Vn3f2TfZevR51WSsCPU9mQPL/HQsrAnnTs76sPFeCjVvFU5vZTdlq\n8+qtQrAEmWkjWFBMZ4Ku\n=VUUD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T18:16:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDlmNDA5MDMxYTczOWZjNDczNjg4ZWExYzIyNTE3NjRjMDk2MGFlNzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd","sha":"c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd"}],"sha":"9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/9f409031a739fc473688ea1c2251764c0960ae70"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T15:24:14Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T15:24:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: the Results page survives a form reference the live workspace cannot resolve (#366)\n\n* fix: the Results page survives a form reference the live workspace cannot resolve\n\nA dangling parentForm weak reference normally answers refNode: null, and the page flags the\nentry. On an unpublished form Jahia has been seen throwing ItemNotFoundException on that\nfield instead (the live path still known, the node gone — a flush of the caches and a fresh\npublish/unpublish cycle did not change it), and with Apollo''s default error policy the one\nfailing field voided the whole list: the page showed the raw exception in place of the\nresults of every form. The list query now keeps its data when a field errors (errorPolicy\n''all''); the failing entry reads as missing in live, and the EDIT lookup tells unpublished\nfrom deleted as for any other. Only an error that comes with no list at all is fatal.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the Results page reference fix (#366)\n\n* test: spec 75 unpublishes its form for real, which is the route that leaves an unresolvable reference (#366 review)\n\nThe fourth case removed the live node with deleteNode, the route that answers refNode: null;\nthe core''s unpublication (unpublishNode per language, what the playground does) is the one\nseen throwing ItemNotFoundException on the entry''s parentForm. The case now unpublishes, and\nasserts the whole list still renders before the entry''s flag. The changelog line fits 120.","tree":{"sha":"1b335317c6739fe2c86b552a35055fa5fa16e78a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/1b335317c6739fe2c86b552a35055fa5fa16e78a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b335317c6739fe2c86b552a35055fa5fa16e78a\nparent d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790954654 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790954654 +0200\n\nfix: the Results page survives a form reference the live workspace cannot resolve (#366)\n\n* fix: the Results page survives a form reference the live workspace cannot resolve\n\nA dangling parentForm weak reference normally answers refNode: null, and the page flags the\nentry. On an unpublished form Jahia has been seen throwing ItemNotFoundException on that\nfield instead (the live path still known, the node gone — a flush of the caches and a fresh\npublish/unpublish cycle did not change it), and with Apollo''s default error policy the one\nfailing field voided the whole list: the page showed the raw exception in place of the\nresults of every form. The list query now keeps its data when a field errors (errorPolicy\n''all''); the failing entry reads as missing in live, and the EDIT lookup tells unpublished\nfrom deleted as for any other. Only an error that comes with no list at all is fatal.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the Results page reference fix (#366)\n\n* test: spec 75 unpublishes its form for real, which is the route that leaves an unresolvable reference (#366 review)\n\nThe fourth case removed the live node with deleteNode, the route that answers refNode: null;\nthe core''s unpublication (unpublishNode per language, what the playground does) is the one\nseen throwing ItemNotFoundException on the entry''s parentForm. The case now unpublishes, and\nasserts the whole list still renders before the entry''s flag. The changelog line fits 120.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv8yeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3Q4QAD/KphqiqHVqR80nZsYm3HGf\nCRkEWXnhijfG3Oc7X1ZLVgTLw26L528VBwKdA+/tYVmL+wwigl/n6OdIrr/12css\n5mImQYSfQSE9tFKl//WDo5HGyc0cAA0S6JNAzFV4GeHSM6y/vu0dt81nNvfMyuzq\nxbhJvOSstWldGp/uBM6T8TgB+8WLADRM7FcnwGpI3vs5JdbWoFNpsAkMe8gS8xIz\n+qV0WKDyF+ra/K/5Z8hp9yaz0+b1VfqsPQOqjnAgI2pNU+ar4TiggG9q1pgSp4R/\nD/CBdRsz0xxa5jYPDoz2RZWeyPTZdrj5r9WRLfSJ4DEZjk7KPqu0BW4yI13/x/jV\nqnNyjmqupoRF+C4lDzNUZekzBrHeDbCr1x1/dtFjj7TLY03Q0IPE3s/+MuRk3UDj\nyPJFCyOacbmLpvvXi0v1LqZo/+VdWZvEHw7H+XK9pvlkYHjq6dVd/0C4TNMQfPvf\nk7SVLE55B3GcKRWbK43kLSujL2MAERGrlRVLE7dsSGAT9CF1Vi3hKtgIGxYjMMPg\nmJvA+ctSlj2oVv5AXcM8vsNMKNE3Gulj45MViKXFelafRGmo1BMs6HC+nl4Tk46W\nk52n16AcpES6mkAiylg4dWBiFmLLaQjLdhKxrHpO0lhcRAZUSldOQ6UdWlChmMqN\nBhfxPErybmfhiY0ooSOR\n=4qHH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T15:24:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGM2NGYyZDhkZDgxMGM3YWU3MmM1NWZjYTU1ZTJkNTllMDgzYzA4Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c","sha":"d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c"}],"sha":"c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/c64f2d8dd810c7ae72c55fca55e2d59e083c08cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:43:50Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:43:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the editor of a consent, rating, scale or switch field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings (#363)\n\n* feat: the editor of a consent, rating, scale or switch field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings\n\nThe last family, laid out from its own module: formidable-extended-inputs ships\none override per type. What defines the control stays in Content with Required —\nthe consent''s statement and terms target, the rating''s maximum (its minimum is\nfixed at 1 and hidden in the CND), the scale''s minimum and maximum — and what\ndresses it goes to Help & presentation: the rating''s icon and end labels, the\nscale''s end labels, the switch''s display mode and state labels, the consent''s\nterms link label. The scale''s step and the switch''s default state are Value &\ninput. The shared section and fieldset labels resolve through the module''s\ndependency on formidable-elements, which is what a third-party module relies on.\n\nSpec 225 asserts the seventeen types; the layout page closes the family table —\nevery built-in family has moved.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the extended inputs field editor layout (#363)","tree":{"sha":"9822a7bc9c124f8782c6e736b32a523b99c7d3ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/9822a7bc9c124f8782c6e736b32a523b99c7d3ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c","verification":{"payload":"tree 9822a7bc9c124f8782c6e736b32a523b99c7d3ce\nparent a37664b29b1ce2cb7a38a0022e877c795e4e6d61\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790952230 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790952230 +0200\n\nfeat: the editor of a consent, rating, scale or switch field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings (#363)\n\n* feat: the editor of a consent, rating, scale or switch field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings\n\nThe last family, laid out from its own module: formidable-extended-inputs ships\none override per type. What defines the control stays in Content with Required —\nthe consent''s statement and terms target, the rating''s maximum (its minimum is\nfixed at 1 and hidden in the CND), the scale''s minimum and maximum — and what\ndresses it goes to Help & presentation: the rating''s icon and end labels, the\nscale''s end labels, the switch''s display mode and state labels, the consent''s\nterms link label. The scale''s step and the switch''s default state are Value &\ninput. The shared section and fieldset labels resolve through the module''s\ndependency on formidable-elements, which is what a third-party module relies on.\n\nSpec 225 asserts the seventeen types; the layout page closes the family table —\nevery built-in family has moved.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the extended inputs field editor layout (#363)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv8MmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZG8QAHElwP9MVvFyCZKkm2GNqIqB\n57S5kDL1ENh0TmCI9C9QpstnI2ep4/7WAGoxWxyA02ei9Sbo/jj204Kr59bR3cM9\nHSylwE5Pr3kVfemOuVmhLhtKya+fdYOvceVP9E+oINnqftCh/2DlZjO6oL2F50pY\nPc5vG4z0ebruq1xqY1yf8ka+RRnBNsD3QLyzQ8NZDFMBlleaUSwX4RlD8kSxV2CY\n4NsKqLvluiNNGHXRTsIBC83MIxdVK/TansYZuiRBpZ4eYL38fc5fD9IssQGdS0RI\nVaA8NayomfoCVCoy9uwGu+uegAoTFWECAU7FJDalviHRSq8eeZ8lP3d28mvT6/WX\nTQH1dmcsxmBOyBcaxaG3Bc8zwn20NJ73fAQ4aFZdZXwep9E1eW17TSbM+V2JDbQF\n79R4xJ3/njcEHEJ7VLUmv0t+n9pPzJDHvJcmone891JfjSz4f2Tk78mcV1EJ+dlk\nkAcLynl9JeCTL9YuW3cS1m77jsnu9Gyf05uEylX3eKUj6FIHmTd5izHZb3/eWGyb\n7r/gbDERs7mtjOgv7vwuQigS8sSLVPU3X1wcaFFoCbWPWfKOfTCnLmt2+0ScYLmI\nmv2BKiCiXsbkb6ydNjBBj9MWGYThhbgsHOcV5YN5BkUCfBBdftxRjkSgUuuEGa5U\nggPi1kCLQMQF2QJjAYw5\n=ygps\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T14:43:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGQ0MjhlMzE5YjJhYTM4MmU4MWRjNGJjNmRlYzBiZTc2MGU0ZDU5NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/a37664b29b1ce2cb7a38a0022e877c795e4e6d61","sha":"a37664b29b1ce2cb7a38a0022e877c795e4e6d61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/a37664b29b1ce2cb7a38a0022e877c795e4e6d61"}],"sha":"d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/d428e319b2aa382e81dc4bc6dec0be760e4d595c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/a37664b29b1ce2cb7a38a0022e877c795e4e6d61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:35:33Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:35:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the editor of a choice, file, colour or hidden field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings (#362)\n\n* feat: the editor of a choice, file, colour or hidden field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings\n\nThe third family moves to the shared layout. A choice field is its options: the\noptions origin and the dynamic fieldset of the chosen origin stay in Content, right\nafter Required, as before — ranked by one content-only override on the engine''s\nfmdbmix:optionsSource contract, since a type''s file now lists only the type''s own\nproperties. The select keeps Multiple beside the origin and gives its empty-option\nlabel to Help & presentation, its number of visible rows to Value & input, disabled\nand autofocus to Behaviour. The file field keeps what it accepts and how many; only\nits help text moves. The colour input gives its default colour to Value & input.\nThe hidden input has nothing to move and no section.\n\nSpec 225 asserts the thirteen types so far, the options fieldsets kept in Content\nand the absence of a switch on the file field included; spec 222 expects the\nsample''s setting right under the select''s help text now that the select is laid\nout. The layout page documents the family.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the choices and files field editor layout (#362)\n\n* fix: the file field hides the editor''s children block too, the select''s empty-option label leaves rank 1.5 to a third-party setting (#362 review)\n\nEvery element is orderable, so the editor drew its Content list & ordering block on the file field — no\nfield actions mixin to key the engine''s hide on, no children to order either: its own override hides it,\nand spec 225 asserts the block hidden on every field. optionsEmptyLabel takes rank 1.6, after the 1.5 the\nsample''s help-text position holds on the select, so spec 222 no longer relies on a tie-break.","tree":{"sha":"5b415d7142d6f95e8e4b65a34f2fac69dff8605c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/5b415d7142d6f95e8e4b65a34f2fac69dff8605c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/a37664b29b1ce2cb7a38a0022e877c795e4e6d61","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b415d7142d6f95e8e4b65a34f2fac69dff8605c\nparent 7ae381175cf592ac16ae11c5757da60a7feefe53\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790951733 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790951733 +0200\n\nfeat: the editor of a choice, file, colour or hidden field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings (#362)\n\n* feat: the editor of a choice, file, colour or hidden field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings\n\nThe third family moves to the shared layout. A choice field is its options: the\noptions origin and the dynamic fieldset of the chosen origin stay in Content, right\nafter Required, as before — ranked by one content-only override on the engine''s\nfmdbmix:optionsSource contract, since a type''s file now lists only the type''s own\nproperties. The select keeps Multiple beside the origin and gives its empty-option\nlabel to Help & presentation, its number of visible rows to Value & input, disabled\nand autofocus to Behaviour. The file field keeps what it accepts and how many; only\nits help text moves. The colour input gives its default colour to Value & input.\nThe hidden input has nothing to move and no section.\n\nSpec 225 asserts the thirteen types so far, the options fieldsets kept in Content\nand the absence of a switch on the file field included; spec 222 expects the\nsample''s setting right under the select''s help text now that the select is laid\nout. The layout page documents the family.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the choices and files field editor layout (#362)\n\n* fix: the file field hides the editor''s children block too, the select''s empty-option label leaves rank 1.5 to a third-party setting (#362 review)\n\nEvery element is orderable, so the editor drew its Content list & ordering block on the file field — no\nfield actions mixin to key the engine''s hide on, no children to order either: its own override hides it,\nand spec 225 asserts the block hidden on every field. optionsEmptyLabel takes rank 1.6, after the 1.5 the\nsample''s help-text position holds on the select, so spec 222 no longer relies on a tie-break.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv8E1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACV8QAHUwXMfVItU4957vsakvKYeL\nt0utwdBoEPIQuBuFoNFsHZZXa9ljiZqEenPlijq27+t/5U1PUU42YMG9+Dz0+FUG\nnOeduxMTf2y8Qnd3Le7x7QAuRC4ChzaDvpN9jZFKYqMGx3B/PL8DOwl3hHzpZvZY\nhoIT+8sKhxY54G8qG4JbWNd9Jf6gjGizOdNp0I6dATYiMYExpkFyBg55Z/d3qtqC\nEJmy8q9TJLpDQhcQ7XcBihFySsORYPqM3oy49nD2J0S96a+cpcAdSu3ck7f1SKcg\nCyvCb+96hEbjnkIz5m8fUjgrZUU5hWRJEtoiWHkq8kqTyY/pwftyAePVb0c/C2KL\nGEPk+ui8A9tN6w0f23B3+VFvVDHkwYQGp9EcnDjHOXuj6Zw9LH057yGMyz52L+7L\ni+fNqkdQPyg+53/wj3j8v/+9Bb1fxl3OwM1DzlueZbgpE6V/J2XbpRqfJFM86BEk\noN13IRwPvYHfHRbJqdGfk2O0dNx8Isv8uIZphuGUgE+nS1TPvV0qE