chesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/7ae381175cf592ac16ae11c5757da60a7feefe53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:21:00Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:21:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the editor of a number, slider, date or datetime field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings (#361)\n\n* feat: the editor of a number, slider, date or datetime field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings\n\nThe second family moves to the layout of the text fields: Content keeps the title,\nthe system name and Required — and, on the slider, the minimum and maximum that\ndraw the control. Everything else sits in the Field settings section, in the\nshared fieldsets: the number''s bounds in Constraints, step and default value in\nValue & input, the slider''s end labels next to the help text.\n\nThe date and datetime bound modes move to Constraints, and the four dynamic bound\nfieldsets of each contract (fixed and relative minimum and maximum) follow at ranks\n3.1 to 3.4, each moved by an override of its own listing its fields, so the mode\nthat selects one still reveals it — in the new section. The fieldsets/ overrides\nmaking the relative offsets mandatory keep working: they merge before the forms/\nones move the fields. The number and slider \"advanced settings\" mixins are\ndissolved into the fieldsets like the text ones, kept as hidden storage for `form`.\n\nSpec 225 now asserts the layout of the seven types, the activated bound fieldset\nincluded; the layout page documents the family and the bound fieldsets'' ranks.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the numbers and dates field editor layout (#361)\n\n* feat: the number and range advanced-settings mixins become supertypes of their types, migrated like the text ones\n\nSame treatment as #359''s text family (review of #359, thread 1): fmdbmix:advancedInputNumberSettings\nand fmdbmix:advancedInputRangeSettings lose extends/itemtype and join the supertypes of\nfmdb:inputNumber and fmdb:inputRange; form is hidden in the CND; their overrides keep placing the\nfields in Field settings without a storage fieldset; AdvancedSettingsMixinMigration drops the\nredundant mixin from the number and range fields saved before. Spec 225 asserts the hidden\nattributes nowhere for the four types and keeps the container''s children block.\n\n* fix: the slider''s end labels take ranks 1.6 and 1.7, leaving 1.5 to a third-party help-text setting (#361 review)\n\n* fix: spec 225 lists the hidden attributes per type — the select''s size is a field, not the text input''s hidden attribute (#362 review)","tree":{"sha":"7363c61853af9af88adbe0ec327f8e3af771c215","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/7363c61853af9af88adbe0ec327f8e3af771c215"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/7ae381175cf592ac16ae11c5757da60a7feefe53","verification":{"payload":"tree 7363c61853af9af88adbe0ec327f8e3af771c215\nparent 391bc118c5500f0fbe4885be4c9fdeab937e3411\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790950860 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790950860 +0200\n\nfeat: the editor of a number, slider, date or datetime field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings (#361)\n\n* feat: the editor of a number, slider, date or datetime field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in Field settings\n\nThe second family moves to the layout of the text fields: Content keeps the title,\nthe system name and Required — and, on the slider, the minimum and maximum that\ndraw the control. Everything else sits in the Field settings section, in the\nshared fieldsets: the number''s bounds in Constraints, step and default value in\nValue & input, the slider''s end labels next to the help text.\n\nThe date and datetime bound modes move to Constraints, and the four dynamic bound\nfieldsets of each contract (fixed and relative minimum and maximum) follow at ranks\n3.1 to 3.4, each moved by an override of its own listing its fields, so the mode\nthat selects one still reveals it — in the new section. The fieldsets/ overrides\nmaking the relative offsets mandatory keep working: they merge before the forms/\nones move the fields. The number and slider \"advanced settings\" mixins are\ndissolved into the fieldsets like the text ones, kept as hidden storage for `form`.\n\nSpec 225 now asserts the layout of the seven types, the activated bound fieldset\nincluded; the layout page documents the family and the bound fieldsets'' ranks.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the numbers and dates field editor layout (#361)\n\n* feat: the number and range advanced-settings mixins become supertypes of their types, migrated like the text ones\n\nSame treatment as #359''s text family (review of #359, thread 1): fmdbmix:advancedInputNumberSettings\nand fmdbmix:advancedInputRangeSettings lose extends/itemtype and join the supertypes of\nfmdb:inputNumber and fmdb:inputRange; form is hidden in the CND; their overrides keep placing the\nfields in Field settings without a storage fieldset; AdvancedSettingsMixinMigration drops the\nredundant mixin from the number and range fields saved before. Spec 225 asserts the hidden\nattributes nowhere for the four types and keeps the container''s children block.\n\n* fix: the slider''s end labels take ranks 1.6 and 1.7, leaving 1.5 to a third-party help-text setting (#361 review)\n\n* fix: spec 225 lists the hidden attributes per type — the select''s size is a field, not the text input''s hidden attribute (#362 review)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv73MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjCQQAGIRXDTD309LIVfdNn0IWLV0\n0kAtL60h+8NBYuJtBkWt45MJ4qS3Aqni4IUuCf9hfLUxs01W/MDUfeV2Wsovpq1C\nWn28cemDNVkrg/i67udIPF+mOQ7NSbCVMCWxcWomlRp4gwX1k52/mRjOnDWKLYcL\nlB5vn9wdZOs3GSCG1DH7bWJyVMelv7wdka5tSMaFXmTgzPEF+I1R6XHubmGVdKd+\nOdlypZi9wdv6P57Jid0ao54nbbi7x89Ipkd7fLwBRq2gyjZbJneavJGCfKvBK8Ht\njUV8hvVjzQoBBp/IR7v+epr/nC40O44KD6lGGVTImzGAOzOexqGMskbfRTDB5aE/\n92HFRcorwh+wYin1ObopnKSTu3kca4ggc3RNGR0NaYs5Rey6T+Kiq4NXwAvTVdpF\nPWGtysKXDpNmWhGqC3rguQtXbOGa25CjlWw15JEhX4mBc7P9wEeHpmOltspnpeO9\nGR4tEIvBRJ1lS19X0EHOCvll3ALU2zoDwyCkX/Ftm6dhg3nXieY6gk3FAef4e/kc\nyPnCvgUyqX6xNwUVJHC2QiEhy8Y9tGFqJvMcEsZA+ssXkEFlAh5HJCJbx8FjTkMp\nnJbBhKKPC4tst4UAJFHVHjaPzlFZv0uI8lDo95Ua+Nod4i9bVYABMtQckJPAmxi3\nzjMCIsgXK9YaElFw9Lg5\n=35Rt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T14:21:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/7ae381175cf592ac16ae11c5757da60a7feefe53","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDdhZTM4MTE3NWNmNTkyYWMxNmFlMTFjNTc1N2RhNjBhN2ZlZWZlNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/391bc118c5500f0fbe4885be4c9fdeab937e3411","sha":"391bc118c5500f0fbe4885be4c9fdeab937e3411","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/391bc118c5500f0fbe4885be4c9fdeab937e3411"}],"sha":"7ae381175cf592ac16ae11c5757da60a7feefe53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/7ae381175cf592ac16ae11c5757da60a7feefe53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/391bc118c5500f0fbe4885be4c9fdeab937e3411/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:24:50Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:24:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the editor of a text, email or textarea field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in a Field settings section (#359)\n\n* feat: the editor of a text, email or textarea field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in a Field settings section\n\nThe editor of a form field showed every property of its type in Content, in CND\norder, the rarely used HTML attributes behind an \"Advanced settings\" switch and\nthe validation messages in a section of their own. Content now keeps the title,\nthe system name and Required; everything else sits in one Field settings section\n(rank 1.05) in fieldsets shared by the types: Help & presentation, Value & input,\nConstraints, Behaviour, the Field actions switch, Validation messages. Laid out by\nContent Editor form overrides only: no property moves, no migration.\n\nThe text family moves first (fmdb:inputText, fmdb:inputEmail, fmdb:textarea). The\n\"advanced settings\" mixins are dissolved into the fieldsets and kept as hidden,\nalways-activated storage, so the CND stays untouched; form, dirname, size and cols\nare no longer offered (no effect, or an effect nothing reads, in a Formidable\nform). The mask and pattern tooltips now say the pattern is derived from the mask.\n\nThe field actions switch is placed by the engine''s own override, under the name\n\"Field actions\" (alwaysPresent: a switch without a property would be pruned once a\nsecond copy of its fieldset exists). The three validation-message overrides feed\none fieldset of the new section; the Validation messages section is retired.\n\nscripts/check-editor-forms.mjs, run by CI, checks that an override declaring the\nsection places every property of its node type exactly once, the hidden ones in\nthe hidden fieldset. Spec 225 asserts the layout of the three types through\nforms.editForm; spec 222 follows the sample''s setting into Help & presentation.\ndocs/architecture/content-editor-layout.md holds the layout, the section ranks,\nthe editor''s merge rules the overrides rely on and the decision log.\n\nCloses #311\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the field editor layout (#359)\n\n* fix: the field actions switch stays at the end of Content, the editor''s children block starts folded\n\nTried in the Field settings section, the switch read as lost between two titled\ngroups of settings. It is a capability of the field, not a setting, and the list\nit creates makes the editor show its \"Content list & ordering\" block right under\nContent whatever a module declares (jContent''s FormBuilder reinserts the\nlistOrdering section in second position, out of the rank order). Back at the end\nof Content, where the editor generates it, the switch and its effect stay together.\n\nThe engine''s override on fmdbmix:fieldActions now does one thing: it declares the\nlistOrdering section folded, one node being nothing to order. No alwaysPresent\ntrick any more; the engine bundle no longer needs the section label. Validation\nmessages take rank 5 in the section. Spec 225 asserts the switch after the type''s\nfieldset in Content and the folded block; the layout page documents the core\nsection ranks and the two the editor draws out of rank order.\n\n* fix: the editor''s children block is hidden on the elements that can carry field actions, not folded\n\nOne node, nothing to order, and the actions are managed in the Page Builder zone\nunder the field: the engine''s override on fmdbmix:fieldActions now declares the\nlistOrdering section hidden rather than folded. Keyed on the mixin, it reaches the\nfield types with a value — the elements that can carry field actions — and nothing\nelse: a form, a step, a fieldset or a button keeps its Content list & ordering\nblock, their children being worth ordering. Spec 225 asserts the section''s absence\non the three text types; the layout page, field-actions.md and the CND comment say\nthe scope.\n\n* fix: spec 225 asserts the storage mixin activated and the children block kept on a container; one rank per section\n\nReview of #359. The spec said \"always activated\" and never read `activated`: it\nnow selects it and asserts it true on the storage fieldset, with and without the\nmixin on the node, which is what lets a moved field be saved on either. A positive\ncontrol reads the editor form of a fieldset container and finds the children block\nthere: the absence on fields comes from the hide, and the hide stays within the\nfield actions mixin''s scope.\n\nThe rank rule of #311 is back in the layout page — a new section takes a rank no\nother section of the product uses, whatever its scope; joining one repeats its\nname and rank — and the two ties are gone: Configuration (field actions) moves\nfrom 1.05 to 1.06, Responses (form) from 1.10 to 1.12, same positions. The\njExperience row names fmdbmix:jExperienceSensitiveField too.\n\n* feat: the advanced-settings mixins become supertypes of the text and textarea types; a migration drops the redundant mixin from older fields\n\nReview of #359, thread 1: the hidden always-activated storage fieldset made the editor add the\nmixin on every save (refused for a translator''s role) and showed no CND default. The settings\ncannot move onto the field types under their names — a node still listing the mixin, every field\nsaved before, has no effective node type for Jackrabbit (\"ambiguous property definition\") and\nrefuses every write, the removal of the mixin included (verified on 8.2.4; a type removed from\nthe CND stays registered). So each mixin becomes a supertype of its type, name kept: every field\nhas the settings, no switch, nothing to add on save, the defaults show. form/dirname/size/cols\nare hidden in the CND; the mixin overrides keep placing their fields in Field settings; the\nfixtures no longer add the mixin; spec 225 asserts the hidden attributes nowhere.\nAdvancedSettingsMixinMigration drops the redundant mixin from the fields saved before (values\nkept, both workspaces, re-run on the elements redeploy), unit-tested; no Cypress spec, the\nlegacy state being unproducible on a fresh instance.\n\n* fix: the migrations share their outcome tally and refresh in the base class; the extension guide says what an always-activated mixin costs\n\nReview of #359, round 2. AdvancedSettingsMixinMigration repeated MixinPropertyNamesMigration\nblock for block (Sonar: 10.2% duplication on new code): the Outcome enum, the counts loop and\nrefreshQuietly now live in ElementsRedeployRetriggeredMigration, both migrations use them.\nThe third-party guide presented the always-activated storage mixin as a deliberate product\nchoice without its cost — the editor adds it on save, which a translator''s role cannot do — and\nnow says so, with the two ways out. The upgrade notes record that the two advanced-settings\nmixins may be inlined into their types once their migration leaves (0.6), optional and cosmetic.\n\n* fix: the migrations run each node and end each pass through the base class (Sonar duplication on #359)\n\nThe second analysis still found 22 duplicated lines between AdvancedSettingsMixinMigration and\nMixinPropertyNamesMigration: the guarded one-node run (save on MIGRATED, log, catch, refresh,\nFAILED) and the four-sentence pass summary. Both now live in ElementsRedeployRetriggeredMigration\n— migrateOne takes the node''s pass and the message of the line administrators look for,\nlogSummary the four templates — with unit tests for the three outcomes of a node.","tree":{"sha":"19a7b3f94f552884c269b0484526081a536cfff1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/19a7b3f94f552884c269b0484526081a536cfff1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/391bc118c5500f0fbe4885be4c9fdeab937e3411","verification":{"payload":"tree 19a7b3f94f552884c269b0484526081a536cfff1\nparent 1a78c62ed7de8d5d77523e5aedf7b6d2eb67a272\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790943890 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790943890 +0200\n\nfeat: the editor of a text, email or textarea field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in a Field settings section (#359)\n\n* feat: the editor of a text, email or textarea field keeps the essentials in Content, every other setting in a Field settings section\n\nThe editor of a form field showed every property of its type in Content, in CND\norder, the rarely used HTML attributes behind an \"Advanced settings\" switch and\nthe validation messages in a section of their own. Content now keeps the title,\nthe system name and Required; everything else sits in one Field settings section\n(rank 1.05) in fieldsets shared by the types: Help & presentation, Value & input,\nConstraints, Behaviour, the Field actions switch, Validation messages. Laid out by\nContent Editor form overrides only: no property moves, no migration.\n\nThe text family moves first (fmdb:inputText, fmdb:inputEmail, fmdb:textarea). The\n\"advanced settings\" mixins are dissolved into the fieldsets and kept as hidden,\nalways-activated storage, so the CND stays untouched; form, dirname, size and cols\nare no longer offered (no effect, or an effect nothing reads, in a Formidable\nform). The mask and pattern tooltips now say the pattern is derived from the mask.\n\nThe field actions switch is placed by the engine''s own override, under the name\n\"Field actions\" (alwaysPresent: a switch without a property would be pruned once a\nsecond copy of its fieldset exists). The three validation-message overrides feed\none fieldset of the new section; the Validation messages section is retired.\n\nscripts/check-editor-forms.mjs, run by CI, checks that an override declaring the\nsection places every property of its node type exactly once, the hidden ones in\nthe hidden fieldset. Spec 225 asserts the layout of the three types through\nforms.editForm; spec 222 follows the sample''s setting into Help & presentation.\ndocs/architecture/content-editor-layout.md holds the layout, the section ranks,\nthe editor''s merge rules the overrides rely on and the decision log.\n\nCloses #311\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the field editor layout (#359)\n\n* fix: the field actions switch stays at the end of Content, the editor''s children block starts folded\n\nTried in the Field settings section, the switch read as lost between two titled\ngroups of settings. It is a capability of the field, not a setting, and the list\nit creates makes the editor show its \"Content list & ordering\" block right under\nContent whatever a module declares (jContent''s FormBuilder reinserts the\nlistOrdering section in second position, out of the rank order). Back at the end\nof Content, where the editor generates it, the switch and its effect stay together.\n\nThe engine''s override on fmdbmix:fieldActions now does one thing: it declares the\nlistOrdering section folded, one node being nothing to order. No alwaysPresent\ntrick any more; the engine bundle no longer needs the section label. Validation\nmessages take rank 5 in the section. Spec 225 asserts the switch after the type''s\nfieldset in Content and the folded block; the layout page documents the core\nsection ranks and the two the editor draws out of rank order.\n\n* fix: the editor''s children block is hidden on the elements that can carry field actions, not folded\n\nOne node, nothing to order, and the actions are managed in the Page Builder zone\nunder the field: the engine''s override on fmdbmix:fieldActions now declares the\nlistOrdering section hidden rather than folded. Keyed on the mixin, it reaches the\nfield types with a value — the elements that can carry field actions — and nothing\nelse: a form, a step, a fieldset or a button keeps its Content list & ordering\nblock, their children being worth ordering. Spec 225 asserts the section''s absence\non the three text types; the layout page, field-actions.md and the CND comment say\nthe scope.\n\n* fix: spec 225 asserts the storage mixin activated and the children block kept on a container; one rank per section\n\nReview of #359. The spec said \"always activated\" and never read `activated`: it\nnow selects it and asserts it true on the storage fieldset, with and without the\nmixin on the node, which is what lets a moved field be saved on either. A positive\ncontrol reads the editor form of a fieldset container and finds the children block\nthere: the absence on fields comes from the hide, and the hide stays within the\nfield actions mixin''s scope.\n\nThe rank rule of #311 is back in the layout page — a new section takes a rank no\nother section of the product uses, whatever its scope; joining one repeats its\nname and rank — and the two ties are gone: Configuration (field actions) moves\nfrom 1.05 to 1.06, Responses (form) from 1.10 to 1.12, same positions. The\njExperience row names fmdbmix:jExperienceSensitiveField too.\n\n* feat: the advanced-settings mixins become supertypes of the text and textarea types; a migration drops the redundant mixin from older fields\n\nReview of #359, thread 1: the hidden always-activated storage fieldset made the editor add the\nmixin on every save (refused for a translator''s role) and showed no CND default. The settings\ncannot move onto the field types under their names — a node still listing the mixin, every field\nsaved before, has no effective node type for Jackrabbit (\"ambiguous property definition\") and\nrefuses every write, the removal of the mixin included (verified on 8.2.4; a type removed from\nthe CND stays registered). So each mixin becomes a supertype of its type, name kept: every field\nhas the settings, no switch, nothing to add on save, the defaults show. form/dirname/size/cols\nare hidden in the CND; the mixin overrides keep placing their fields in Field settings; the\nfixtures no longer add the mixin; spec 225 asserts the hidden attributes nowhere.\nAdvancedSettingsMixinMigration drops the redundant mixin from the fields saved before (values\nkept, both workspaces, re-run on the elements redeploy), unit-tested; no Cypress spec, the\nlegacy state being unproducible on a fresh instance.\n\n* fix: the migrations share their outcome tally and refresh in the base class; the extension guide says what an always-activated mixin costs\n\nReview of #359, round 2. AdvancedSettingsMixinMigration repeated MixinPropertyNamesMigration\nblock for block (Sonar: 10.2% duplication on new code): the Outcome enum, the counts loop and\nrefreshQuietly now live in ElementsRedeployRetriggeredMigration, both migrations use them.\nThe third-party guide presented the always-activated storage mixin as a deliberate product\nchoice without its cost — the editor adds it on save, which a translator''s role cannot do — and\nnow says so, with the two ways out. The upgrade notes record that the two advanced-settings\nmixins may be inlined into their types once their migration leaves (0.6), optional and cosmetic.\n\n* fix: the migrations run each node and end each pass through the base class (Sonar duplication on #359)\n\nThe second analysis still found 22 duplicated lines between AdvancedSettingsMixinMigration and\nMixinPropertyNamesMigration: the guarded one-node run (save on MIGRATED, log, catch, refresh,\nFAILED) and the four-sentence pass summary. Both now live in ElementsRedeployRetriggeredMigration\n— migrateOne takes the node''s pass and the message of the line administrators look for,\nlogSummary the four templates — with unit tests for the three outcomes of a node.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv6KSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUjIQABxps8jz0nmKJlFH4lXj8wvi\nTUQ0Uu6L91x7bOOP/s2j6CxB8dHsNi5BTTOqI0w1uPKBM2/IQP/16tOAhpqrT