l":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1a78c62ed7de8d5d77523e5aedf7b6d2eb67a272"}],"sha":"391bc118c5500f0fbe4885be4c9fdeab937e3411","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/391bc118c5500f0fbe4885be4c9fdeab937e3411"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1a78c62ed7de8d5d77523e5aedf7b6d2eb67a272/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:10:44Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:10:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: a form''s entry can be removed from the Results page, and a deleted form''s entry is flagged (#364)\n\n* feat: a form''s entry leaves the Results page when all its results are deleted; a deleted form''s entry is flagged\n\nCloses #360. \"Delete all results\" now removes the fmdb:formResults node itself (ACL\nand remaining submissions included), zero submissions accepted, so an entry already\nemptied by a date range or whose form was deleted in jContent can be cleared; the\nnext submission recreates the node. Entries whose form no longer exists are flagged\n\"Form deleted\". Deleting a form never removes its results, on purpose.\n\nThe page now takes its site key from the jContent route: contextJsParameters.siteKey\nis rewritten by jContent mid-sync and a render caught in between queried\n/sites/systemsite, showing \"no results\" over a list it had just displayed.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the Results page entry removal (#364)\n\n* fix: the Results page tells an unpublished form from a deleted one, reads its site behind a context path, and closes its dialogs on Escape\n\nReview of #364. The live reference alone cannot tell a deleted form from an\nunpublished one: the entries missing in live are looked up once in EDIT (SQL2 on\njcr:uuid; nodesById fails the whole field as soon as one id is unknown) and flagged\n\"Form not published\" (title kept) or \"Form deleted\". The site key of the jContent\nroute is read behind the servlet context path. The count-label choice is a status\nmap, globalThis replaces window, and both dialogs close on the cancel event\n(Escape) instead of a backdrop click, which also stops Escape from closing the DOM\ndialog while the React state stayed open.\n\n* fix: the route prefix is compared, not escaped into a regex (Sonar S7780/S7781 on #364)\n\n* test: the playground leaves results behind a deleted form and an unpublished one, for the Results page to flag\n\n* fix: the edit lookup of a missing form selects the form marker, not the concrete type (#364 review)","tree":{"sha":"8dff12a230dcee38f789576eb11ac1440410ee39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/8dff12a230dcee38f789576eb11ac1440410ee39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/1a78c62ed7de8d5d77523e5aedf7b6d2eb67a272","verification":{"payload":"tree 8dff12a230dcee38f789576eb11ac1440410ee39\nparent e22851e98159bc147a7a78e439e1435e59056462\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790939444 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790939444 +0200\n\nfeat: a form''s entry can be removed from the Results page, and a deleted form''s entry is flagged (#364)\n\n* feat: a form''s entry leaves the Results page when all its results are deleted; a deleted form''s entry is flagged\n\nCloses #360. \"Delete all results\" now removes the fmdb:formResults node itself (ACL\nand remaining submissions included), zero submissions accepted, so an entry already\nemptied by a date range or whose form was deleted in jContent can be cleared; the\nnext submission recreates the node. Entries whose form no longer exists are flagged\n\"Form deleted\". Deleting a form never removes its results, on purpose.\n\nThe page now takes its site key from the jContent route: contextJsParameters.siteKey\nis rewritten by jContent mid-sync and a render caught in between queried\n/sites/systemsite, showing \"no results\" over a list it had just displayed.\n\n* docs: changelog entry for the Results page entry removal (#364)\n\n* fix: the Results page tells an unpublished form from a deleted one, reads its site behind a context path, and closes its dialogs on Escape\n\nReview of #364. The live reference alone cannot tell a deleted form from an\nunpublished one: the entries missing in live are looked up once in EDIT (SQL2 on\njcr:uuid; nodesById fails the whole field as soon as one id is unknown) and flagged\n\"Form not published\" (title kept) or \"Form deleted\". The site key of the jContent\nroute is read behind the servlet context path. The count-label choice is a status\nmap, globalThis replaces window, and both dialogs close on the cancel event\n(Escape) instead of a backdrop click, which also stops Escape from closing the DOM\ndialog while the React state stayed open.\n\n* fix: the route prefix is compared, not escaped into a regex (Sonar S7780/S7781 on #364)\n\n* test: the playground leaves results behind a deleted form and an unpublished one, for the Results page to flag\n\n* fix: the edit lookup of a missing form selects the form marker, not the concrete type (#364 review)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv5E0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1wQQAIgAGUaUMqXjzGbJk0wu0h2t\nme9dHGE/YNE9iS7+4VTE8ScJ7xvUJSJN/0gbLZZbT4aMzamfaWUEmYouIWwo0QwM\nZtCYchtPVFQTMYgT/0HliLUGMS+YTfbrhZgw3L8o6vn4ChyHK9P7n6u0/3T6AHTi\nHRgB3T2Ks3fXMZyrqWBQFhi3OGpK7ygfWcas9E+IMIpcxtZ62VvS5ZHzTb2iMDGs\nCOM2TqnS2Zv6l2ROoKFdIMnYbLOvaDnZNImR0vLAvQxXldcUCVhymcRb/mk/p5Y9\nx66LPhAHngU29/tKeOk/dy8DUn8zoIbbNwJAW+b+rEGAF3Sxn5Wtoss76vELvsyb\n/aO2chOLWlj2MmoU7syL4AFU2n0rA50jWYsRcKMlupZuuWAZqvsxYAvLTFPyTm5p\nVgmSXfpwCi5ZYJsiN5diqpcT2bbsZIZKEfyeZdQSjZb2CgaQPtncj2MPoVLy/dfC\nR6ppuUED4Ot6x2mn+TNw9tqaEd1nnB8DJxpnvW+Hm8TF5asJ/l70GCRDF4qPESpP\np/gKuzDxoWAzbjI+X07zJqslBxIuC47LPgE7p6jpvFdLc7VH58PgFGQ+NYHcB5kB\n/QVc/CHk4GW7fqhkJGq2mNMcsPFjknVvRkc/S+ESJPaS90xU66lywbrOQk5ThH5J\nd60n1oCFNCU4KXIi8XFM\n=TbBZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T11:10:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/1a78c62ed7de8d5d77523e5aedf7b6d2eb67a272","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDFhNzhjNjJlZDdkZThkNWQ3NzUyM2U1YWVkZjdiNmQyZWI2N2EyNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/e22851e98159bc147a7a78e439e1435e59056462","sha":"e22851e98159bc147a7a78e439e1435e59056462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/e22851e98159bc147a7a78e439e1435e59056462"}],"sha":"1a78c62ed7de8d5d77523e5aedf7b6d2eb67a272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1a78c62ed7de8d5d77523e5aedf7b6d2eb67a272"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/e22851e98159bc147a7a78e439e1435e59056462/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:50:29Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:50:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: the marker that spares an administrator''s configuration copy is in the module''s file (#357)\n\n* docs: the marker that spares an administrator''s copy is in the module''s file — Activator.checkConfigurations reads the shipped file, so the first-line clause of #352 is corrected\n\n* docs: the former csrf-guard file an upgrade leaves in karaf/etc is harmless and may be removed — seen on the 0.3 and 0.4 upgrade tests of 2026-10-01\n\n* docs: the leftover csrf-guard file dates from the 0.3 → 0.4 upgrade, and a shipped file without the marker is written back\n\nReview of #357: the tags say which versions ship the old file — 0.2 and 0.3 ship\norg.jahia.modules.jahiacsrfguard-formidable-engine.cfg, 0.4 already ships\norg.jahia.modules.jahiacsrfguard-formidable.cfg and not the old name. So the\nleftover belongs to the 0.3 → 0.4 upgrade and an instance installed on 0.4 or\nlater has nothing to find; the note moves out of the 0.5 \"How to check\" into a\nsubsection of its own under 0.3 → 0.4, and says why it is harmless (the filter\nskips a request any configuration whitelists).\n\nThe comments of formActions.cfg and choiceOptions.cfg stated \"the module''s copy\ncarries # default configuration\" as a fact of any shipped file; it is a fact of\nFormidable''s own. They now say both cases, as configuration.md does.\n\n* docs: the former csrf-guard file put the submission endpoint under the token check, the new one whitelists it\n\nReview of #357, round 2: the 0.3 file holds urlPatterns, the list of URLs the\nguard checks, not a whitelist; the new file''s whitelist is what lifts the check\nagain, since the wrapper runs the guard only when a request is filtered by some\nconfiguration and whitelisted by none. HDU''s wording, applied.","tree":{"sha":"0ec4690f8c8964ca3ded6084f9807041a151e396","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/0ec4690f8c8964ca3ded6084f9807041a151e396"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/e22851e98159bc147a7a78e439e1435e59056462","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ec4690f8c8964ca3ded6084f9807041a151e396\nparent c29b8f7fe26f88cfa4a7a7f81f4acdab7d95bca2\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790934629 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790934629 +0200\n\ndocs: the marker that spares an administrator''s configuration copy is in the module''s file (#357)\n\n* docs: the marker that spares an administrator''s copy is in the module''s file — Activator.checkConfigurations reads the shipped file, so the first-line clause of #352 is corrected\n\n* docs: the former csrf-guard file an upgrade leaves in karaf/etc is harmless and may be removed — seen on the 0.3 and 0.4 upgrade tests of 2026-10-01\n\n* docs: the leftover csrf-guard file dates from the 0.3 → 0.4 upgrade, and a shipped file without the marker is written back\n\nReview of #357: the tags say which versions ship the old file — 0.2 and 0.3 ship\norg.jahia.modules.jahiacsrfguard-formidable-engine.cfg, 0.4 already ships\norg.jahia.modules.jahiacsrfguard-formidable.cfg and not the old name. So the\nleftover belongs to the 0.3 → 0.4 upgrade and an instance installed on 0.4 or\nlater has nothing to find; the note moves out of the 0.5 \"How to check\" into a\nsubsection of its own under 0.3 → 0.4, and says why it is harmless (the filter\nskips a request any configuration whitelists).\n\nThe comments of formActions.cfg and choiceOptions.cfg stated \"the module''s copy\ncarries # default configuration\" as a fact of any shipped file; it is a fact of\nFormidable''s own. They now say both cases, as configuration.md does.\n\n* docs: the former csrf-guard file put the submission endpoint under the token check, the new one whitelists it\n\nReview of #357, round 2: the 0.3 file holds urlPatterns, the list of URLs the\nguard checks, not a whitelist; the new file''s whitelist is what lifts the check\nagain, since the wrapper runs the guard only when a request is filtered by some\nconfiguration and whitelisted by none. HDU''s wording, applied.","rea