e":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:22:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: one configuration file per entry for forward targets and options sources (#352)\n\n* refactor: one configuration file per entry for forward targets and options sources\n\nTwo lists a theme held as lines each become one factory configuration per entry:\nforward targets (org.jahia.modules.formidable.formActions.target-<id>.cfg) and\noptions sources (org.jahia.modules.formidable.choiceOptions.source-<id>.cfg).\n\n- Every entry has a required, explicit `id` setting — letters, digits, dashes and\n  underscores: it names the file, and a dot would match another entry''s file by\n  prefix in core''s ConfigService. Nothing is read from the PID or the file name.\n- Shared code in config/common (FactoryEntry, FactoryEntries): entries stored\n  through Jahia''s ConfigService; an entry created in the Felix console is adopted,\n  a failed or colliding adoption tried again at the next callback; the lines of\n  earlier builds converted once, off the configuration callback, from the theme''s\n  file or the single legacy PID — a line whose id cannot name a file keeps the\n  lines in place, the ids already converted kept next to them; the\n  standard-then-development merge behind the forward targets'' switch names the\n  configuration kept on an id clash.\n- The forward targets are rebuilt on read when a migration attempt changed the\n  theme without a configuration callback.\n- samples-java ships the `country` source and a `localhost` development target as\n  files; the playground and the Cypress specs declare sources and targets as files.\n- Docs: configuration.md (\"The lists: one file per entry\", retiring a shipped\n  entry, the id rule), upgrade notes, a breaking-change changelog entry, security\n  scenarios §7, tests README.\n\nSquash of the branch as reviewed on #352 (rounds 1-4), rebased on main after #354.\n\n* docs: retiring a shipped entry keeps the file''s first line — without the marker, Jahia writes the shipped file back at every start\n\n* fix: an endpoint refusal is logged again after a configuration change — the gateway''s once-logged refusals are forgotten with each new settings snapshot\n\n* test: the factory-configuration fixture updates a wanted entry in place — deleting then re-creating its file within milliseconds lost it to fileinstall''s late deletion event (spec 46 red on CI)","tree":{"sha":"00a1a94988a1fa7bfa9b9bb7930ed4c9b341fe62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/00a1a94988a1fa7bfa9b9bb7930ed4c9b341fe62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/b8da625b95e4e983e35b07ef64fb2749443d81d5","verification":{"payload":"tree 00a1a94988a1fa7bfa9b9bb7930ed4c9b341fe62\nparent 1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790850169 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790850169 +0200\n\nrefactor: one configuration file per entry for forward targets and options sources (#352)\n\n* refactor: one configuration file per entry for forward targets and options sources\n\nTwo lists a theme held as lines each become one factory configuration per entry:\nforward targets (org.jahia.modules.formidable.formActions.target-<id>.cfg) and\noptions sources (org.jahia.modules.formidable.choiceOptions.source-<id>.cfg).\n\n- Every entry has a required, explicit `id` setting — letters, digits, dashes and\n  underscores: it names the file, and a dot would match another entry''s file by\n  prefix in core''s ConfigService. Nothing is read from the PID or the file name.\n- Shared code in config/common (FactoryEntry, FactoryEntries): entries stored\n  through Jahia''s ConfigService; an entry created in the Felix console is adopted,\n  a failed or colliding adoption tried again at the next callback; the lines of\n  earlier builds converted once, off the configuration callback, from the theme''s\n  file or the single legacy PID — a line whose id cannot name a file keeps the\n  lines in place, the ids already converted kept next to them; the\n  standard-then-development merge behind the forward targets'' switch names the\n  configuration kept on an id clash.\n- The forward targets are rebuilt on read when a migration attempt changed the\n  theme without a configuration callback.\n- samples-java ships the `country` source and a `localhost` development target as\n  files; the playground and the Cypress specs declare sources and targets as files.\n- Docs: configuration.md (\"The lists: one file per entry\", retiring a shipped\n  entry, the id rule), upgrade notes, a breaking-change changelog entry, security\n  scenarios §7, tests README.\n\nSquash of the branch as reviewed on #352 (rounds 1-4), rebased on main after #354.\n\n* docs: retiring a shipped entry keeps the file''s first line — without the marker, Jahia writes the shipped file back at every start\n\n* fix: an endpoint refusal is logged again after a configuration change — the gateway''s once-logged refusals are forgotten with each new settings snapshot\n\n* test: the factory-configuration fixture updates a wanted entry in place — deleting then re-creating its file within milliseconds lost it to fileinstall''s late deletion event (spec 46 red on CI)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvjR5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXbIQAGoe5M6iT10nbYsHwIGs9FFc\nV0N7AZcA5VA2uoaaVfUdDXINpqn3jiD+mS/yuXoOvsMAanzVgvJlUaw9QWuUjwRX\n0HxVFty6REBDRquUPB8rgnofFqU7xbvIe4L9i9P47bikjG09W+AJJMh49oF3vHnV\nSYOY4QL6d02vYJF79m56xFIac9aEk59OUSNBvY0Ba7YjiO+iMAsu2eYcq9DpIrvI\nzJ8JnNYdPgHjDZOR4kl468FAQnfx1DBenPxLhtRgkyQFixw7ZssVQ/Prxdgr4bNg\nkapHxr7GrEhDOF4WC7h05gbTQLGWZ/m3pX38+Yg9t4w9OwXyTiZVdD7wZEZLXS2m\n6SA830blIZGY4h4U7mooErfn+kipqTTyDmRNCN28Kmx7Gd3FXDk7J7dHovf3UiyV\n+YLaQDValRKzLqyWz5iT+TApUdQVTE2fDNMzSZhQy/qpx6kuiiwb5iudnY4PNacR\nv63xpVt9hdVS3csSNz7/lA2H8WTxJZJ0ylALHZTvLtSqP0uV7DU9v3o/auwmaFP+\n3girQeMHF3vJI24bAohS42FPITMrc8RSiDGffdfwnOHQfoydWy+qqCZ3KlmD+f08\nscZf35I0K0086Q8OGZqC1VktIMR1mvWQqS5Ob+f4hPSLYdNi4Z491kVK43KUxlMQ\nArr2EPWyVXO6xGbZ5Rgk\n=FQFw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T10:22:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/b8da625b95e4e983e35b07ef64fb2749443d81d5","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGI4ZGE2MjViOTVlNGU5ODNlMzViMDdlZjY0ZmIyNzQ5NDQzZDgxZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef","sha":"1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef"}],"sha":"b8da625b95e4e983e35b07ef64fb2749443d81d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/b8da625b95e4e983e35b07ef64fb2749443d81d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T06:15:47Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T06:15:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: a field action calling a service reads it from its own module''s configuration (#354)\n\n* refactor: a field action calling a service reads it from its own module''s configuration — no provider list, no provider to pick\n\nA check knows its service: its module ships the service''s configuration file\n(url, credential, development) and reads it into a FieldActionGateway.Endpoint;\nthe contributor has nothing to pick. The gateway keeps what no module should\nrewrite, now handed an Endpoint: the endpoint rule checked on every call, the\nrelative path under the base, the credential injected and never logged, the\ntimeouts, the body cap.\n\n- Engine: FieldActionGateway.Endpoint (Endpoint.of checks a configuration''s\n  values), ProviderFieldAction asks endpoint() and offers endpointOf; the\n  provider settings of the field-actions theme go (a warning names them while a\n  file holds them), with the provider choicelist; fmdbmix:providerFieldAction\n  stays hidden and deprecated, removed in 0.6.\n- Samples: Experian and ZeroBounce read their own PID, shipped pointing at the\n  samples'' doubles (development=true); their types lose the provider picker.\n- Tests: the gateway on endpoints and Endpoint.of, the base''s configuration\n  path, the samples'' configuration, spec 74 on the samples'' own files.\n- Docs: administration (services and limits), architecture with a decision-log\n  row, the field-action how-to, configuration, AGENTS, CONTEXT.\n\n* fix: review round 1 on #354 — development endpoints behind an administrator''s switch, the credential off the service registry\n\n- enableDevFieldActionEndpoints (field-actions theme, off by default): the\n  gateway calls an endpoint marked development only while it is on, the rule\n  of the forward targets'' switch; spec 74 turns it on, security scenario 7.4.\n- The credential is the private property .credential (_credential()), which\n  Declarative Services does not publish with the service; the samples share\n  one configuration definition in their own bundle (bnd generates metatype\n  only there) and ProviderFieldAction holds the endpoint (configure, served by\n  endpoint()), so each sample is one configure line.\n- Endpoint.of refuses a URL with a query or a fragment (the gateway would drop\n  it); the former provider settings are named only when they held a value.\n- Tests: the switch, the query refusal, the quiet warning, each sample''s\n  configure path field by field (URL, header or query, development) —\n  mutation-checked; Sonar S5778 endpoints built outside assertThrows.\n- Docs: Security and trust says where the trust sits now (the module''s\n  configuration and the action''s code); admin page, how-to, configuration,\n  decision log.\n\n* fix: final review of #354 — a malformed URL is not quoted, the samples read their answer in one method\n\n- Endpoint.of no longer quotes a malformed URL nor keeps its parse error as\n  the cause: an administrator may have pasted a key into it, and endpointOf\n  logs the message. The position of the error is given instead; tested.\n- Both samples split the call from the reading of the answer (verdictOf):\n  Sonar''s S1854 on the response variable goes, and the reading can be driven\n  directly.\n\n* fix: an endpoint the gateway refuses is logged once with the reason — the development switch off, a URL the rule refuses\n\nReview of #354: with the switch off, the samples'' out-of-the-box state, the log\nonly said ''could not be asked … IllegalArgumentException'' at INFO, once per\nvalue, since the base class logs an exception''s type alone (right for one the\nJDK raised). The gateway''s own refusals carry no secret nor value: it now logs\neach once, at WARN, with its reason. Tested (three calls, one line) and\nmutation-checked.","tree":{"sha":"47a106b3725d8708368f89b44caa2dd858fb3678","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/47a106b3725d8708368f89b44caa2dd858fb3678"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 47a106b3725d8708368f89b44caa2dd858fb3678\nparent 90bc9f37443cc5b912641fec64170bfb6d646a8d\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790835347 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790835347 +0200\n\nrefactor: a field action calling a service reads it from its own module''s configuration (#354)\n\n* refactor: a field action calling a service reads it from its own module''s configuration — no provider list, no provider to pick\n\nA check knows its service: its module ships the service''s configuration file\n(url, credential, development) and reads it into a FieldActionGateway.Endpoint;\nthe contributor has nothing to pick. The gateway keeps what no module should\nrewrite, now handed an Endpoint: the endpoint rule checked on every call, the\nrelative path under the base, the credential injected and never logged, the\ntimeouts, the body cap.\n\n- Engine: FieldActionGateway.Endpoint (Endpoint.of checks a configuration''s\n  values), ProviderFieldAction asks endpoint() and offers endpointOf; the\n  provider settings of the field-actions theme go (a warning names them while a\n  file holds them), with the provider choicelist; fmdbmix:providerFieldAction\n  stays hidden and deprecated, removed in 0.6.\n- Samples: Experian and ZeroBounce read their own PID, shipped pointing at the\n  samples'' doubles (development=true); their types lose the provider picker.\n- Tests: the gateway on endpoints and Endpoint.of, the base''s configuration\n  path, the samples'' configuration, spec 74 on the samples'' own files.\n- Docs: administration (services and limits), architecture with a decision-log\n  row, the field-action how-to, configuration, AGENTS, CONTEXT.\n\n* fix: review round 1 on #354 — development endpoints behind an administrator''s switch, the credential off the service registry\n\n- enableDevFieldActionEndpoints (field-actions theme, off by default): the\n  gateway calls an endpoint marked development only while it is on, the rule\n  of the forward targets'' switch; spec 74 turns it on, security scenario 7.4.\n- The credential is the private property .credential (_credential()), which\n  Declarative Services does not publish with the service; the samples share\n  one configuration definition in their own bundle (bnd generates metatype\n  only there) and ProviderFieldAction holds the endpoint (configure, served by\n  endpoint()), so each sample is one configure line.\n- Endpoint.of refuses a URL with a query or a fragment (the gateway would drop\n  it); the former provider settings are named only when they held a value.\n- Tests: the switch, the query refusal, the quiet warning, each sample''s\n  configure path field by field (URL, header or query, development) —\n  mutation-checked; Sonar S5778 endpoints built outside assertThrows.\n- Docs: Security and trust says where the trust sits now (the module''s\n  configuration and the action''s code); admin page, how-to, configuration,\n  decision log.\n\n* fix: final review of #354 — a malformed URL is not quoted, the samples read their answer in one method\n\n- Endpoint.of no longer quotes a malformed URL nor keeps its parse error as\n  the cause: an administrator may have pasted a key into it, and endpointOf\n  logs the message. The position of the error is given instead; tested.\n- Both samples split the call from the reading of the answer (verdictOf):\n  Sonar''s S1854 on the response variable goes, and the reading can be driven\n  directly.\n\n* fix: an endpoint the gateway refuses is logged once with the reason — the development switch off, a URL the rule refuses\n\nReview of #354: with the switch off, the samples'' out-of-the-box state, the log\nonly said ''could not be asked … IllegalArgumentException'' at INFO, once per\nvalue, since the base class logs an exception''s type alone (right for one the\nJDK raised). The gateway''s own refusals carry no secret nor value: it now logs\neach once, at WARN, with its reason. Tested (three calls, one line) and\nmutation-checked.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvfqTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE9AQAIdUIuzn5of7XWflq9ABwqVu\nkQzRlVBdudvJpe/r1quAQFNrewhmo3E88nYdITfHiOaQWk9X3d12MV2teOmYMN3f\nVZ6cxBW9Qb+b5kRNi7yWluTRi6WK6YhmC8IOdb55TAmK7L+0BBZIlacdWKwFjLgF\nkQVYvTQnPFvvBxPyx+03lo4u6FeJ8tgJwQ5DV5z3mFVO2VnqpABlwS8wRBqp4Zb6\n5xjjqqDwZ5m5O5lWErIzf0KhPSyBUxgoY10bgvPMtw3VnWiH//e/FB7uyztjtKQj\nGrnM+HeZ5CX90EdS0b/0SY9jAfNL7Bbm89uAcqZnMVhJDOeTc91/jEWhyCZ0DiS1\n+X1OIFv0p2VqQ6g/pytaBcOvveT8T9twhdLYNJiGPxdJ84pwMqXaG9vfV+viH0yf\n+Tf4CjzW+mZbF9vCIomNisC3NQcnrC9D1ZBnd69Nk0R/C0ochheQ2U2ibH4vWuLW\nKH6AT84fmlAWfGg/KZ9t4M321yijUrYqDMX+n7Q294mON+2m10+dowsh3OOwMkXN\nabZgQN6FBDW3bDeierCUJjNyYlZ5GnkiaMvW1ac9qlv6CH+UI/RyEQ02bfvWo5zp\nvKPZP8wPvDT8fLjJaiItLdhWmI/vFEmbF2iy3SroZJx8qwhJbagRnWvyaysb/IFY\nwY2iHVN5u/YHGaRbIObQ\n=VQTA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T06:15:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDFhZjNjNGQxYjA5ZTg4ODRjN2NhZWRhMzE3NWRhY2JmNzY1YmYwZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/90bc9f37443cc5b912641fec64170bfb6d646a8d","sha":"90bc9f37443cc5b912641fec64170bfb6d646a8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/90bc9f37443cc5b912641fec64170bfb6d646a8d"}],"sha":"1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1af3c4d1b09e8884c7caeda3175dacbf765bf0ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/90bc9f37443cc5b912641fec64170bfb6d646a8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:25:02Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:25:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: allowed file types as one list from Apache Tika''s registry — extensions accepted, fields kept within it (#351)\n\n* feat: a file field''s types read from Apache Tika''s registry — the extensions shown and recognised, a default label for the editor — instead of tables in the module\n\n* fix: the accept labels come from the module''s bundle where it words them, else from Tika — Jahia''s resourceBundle initializer keyed on the label, no longer the type\n\n* chore: changelog entry for #351\n\n* chore: the quality gate''s two findings on #351 — the file island''s props read-only, String passed as is\n\n* feat: the allowed file types as one list the fields stay within — extensions accepted, an empty list refusing every file\n\n- uploadAllowedMimeTypes becomes uploadAllowedTypes: an extension (pdf, .docx), a MIME type or a wildcard,\n  each resolved once by Tika into its MIME type (logged); the default is written as extensions, the same\n  seventeen types. The legacy carry-over reads the setting under its former name and leaves 0.4''s default\n  list behind. The shipped file links Tika''s registry of the embedded version, held by a unit test.\n- AllowedTypes is the one reading of what a field accepts, shared by the parser and the file field''s view:\n  the field''s accept within the list (a type no longer listed dropped with a warning naming the field), the\n  whole list when it declares none, nothing when the list is empty — no longer every file. No parent type:\n  allowing txt does not allow SVG.\n- The view hands its node to FileTypeService.allowedFor; the island lists, filters and builds its accept\n  attribute from what the server lets through, the attribute from every recognised extension (.mov for\n  video/quicktime), and says when a field accepts no file.\n- Review round 1: the shown extension is the acronym''s when Tika''s preferred one is no abbreviation of it\n  (MP3 -> .mp3, JPEG keeps .jpg); a wildcard or an unknown type is labelled by the whole type; tests in\n  insertion order with trim cases, mutation-proved; the choicelist''s bundle lookup split and tested; the\n  island''s helpers moved to fileAccept.ts with vitest; Cypress spec 224.\n\n* fix: review round 2 and the quality gate on #351 — aliases read as Tika''s type, the parser''s step tested, the any-file replacement given\n\n- A MIME alias in uploadAllowedTypes is normalised through Tika''s registry (audio/x-wav -> audio/vnd.wave), the\n  type a file is detected as; the resolution is logged like an extension''s.\n- FormDataParser.checkAllowedType holds step 7 and is tested directly (a file part cannot be parsed without\n  JCRContentUtils initialised): an empty list refuses, a field''s type the list dropped is refused, a field without\n  types takes the list. The parser names no field in a log line, the name coming from the request (Sonar S5145);\n  the view warns, naming its node.\n- An empty list''s start warning gives the replacement for \"any file\" (the top-level wildcards), as do the upgrade\n  notes and the changelog; a theme file still holding uploadAllowedMimeTypes is named in a warning.\n- The docs say that pages already rendered keep the former list until the site''s cache is flushed.\n- The console''s description links Tika''s registry (UploadsConfig.TIKA_REGISTRY, held by the test with the\n  shipped file). The choicelist''s key composition is extracted and tested. Sonar S135 and S3358.\n\n* feat: a file whose content is a kind of its listed container type is accepted — an Ogg video named .ogv\n\nTika detects the codec inside a container: an .ogv file is video/theora, an\n.oga Opus track audio/opus, kinds of video/ogg and audio/ogg in its registry,\nso a listed ogv refused every real Ogg video. The parser now also accepts a\ndetected type that specializes the type the file''s name stands for, when that\ntype is listed as such, shares the top-level type and is not a root of the\nhierarchy (text/plain, application/octet-stream): an SVG named .xml or an HTML\npage named .txt stays refused. Each guard is held by a test (mutation-checked).\n\n* fix: review round 3 on #351 — */* for any file, the editor offering the top-level wildcards in its place\n\n- */* is read as any file: the server lets every detected type through, a file\n  field without types restricts nothing in the page (no accept attribute), a\n  field with types keeps its own. It holds whatever a future Tika adds, where\n  the five wildcards given before missed chemical/, message/ (.eml), model/,\n  multipart/ (.mht) and x-conference/.\n- The Accept setting never offers */*: in its place, a wildcard for each\n  top-level type of Tika''s registry, beside the other listed types, labelled\n  in four languages (Any image (image/*)).\n- The field''s warning tells a stored value that is no file type from one the\n  list no longer allows.\n- The shipped uploads file reflowed; the start warning, the console\n  description, the docs, the upgrade notes and the changelog give */*.\n- Sonar S3415: assertEquals arguments in order.\n\n* fix: review round 4 on #351 — the container rule for audio and video only, wildcards refusing a contradicting type, an empty 0.4 list kept as any file\n\n- permitsFile accepts a kind of the listed type the file''s name stands for for\n  audio and video only: elsewhere Tika''s kinds mean readable-as (199 kinds of\n  application/xml incl. XHTML, 76 of application/zip incl. jars and\n  macro-enabled documents). ROOTS goes; a jar named .zip is refused again.\n- The island refuses a file whose browser type contradicts a wildcard, even\n  when the wildcard lists no extension (a field narrowed to image/* under */*).\n- The migration carries an empty uploadAllowedMimeTypes, which meant any file\n  until 0.5, as uploadAllowedTypes=*/*: the upgrade keeps the behaviour.\n- Tests: a real Ogg Theora first page through Tika and permitsFile, XHTML/jar/\n  macro workbook refused, the island''s wildcard, the migration, and spec 224\n  under */* (an .eml attached and stored). Mutation-checked.\n- Docs: to narrow finely under */*, list the types next to it; a caution on\n  HTML and SVG under */*; upgrade notes and changelog no longer call the empty\n  list a breaking case; line lengths and a Javadoc wrap.\n\n* docs: removing an allowed type — the Content Editor keeps only the listed types at the next save, which can widen a field\n\nA stored accept value no longer listed is honoured again if the type comes\nback, but only until a contributor saves the field: the editor offers the\nlisted types only and saves what it shows. A field whose only types were\nremoved then accepts the whole list, or any file under */*; the admin is told\nto check the fields naming a type before removing it, and that */* alone\nremoves every specific type.\n\n* fix: review round 5 on #351 — what the detection proves for containers, a recognised extension over a contradicting browser type\n\n- The docs no longer claim a jar or a macro-enabled workbook named .zip is\n  refused: tika-core alone checks a zip or OLE2 container''s family by content\n  and takes its kind from the name, so any zip named .docx passes as a docx.\n  configuration.md says what the check proves per format; step 7, the console\n  description and the shipped file say it for containers; the XHTML example,\n  detected by its content, stays.\n- The island takes a recognised extension before refusing a contradicting\n  browser type: a .csv that Windows types application/vnd.ms-excel is a CSV on\n  a text/* field again; a wildcard listing no extension (under */*) still\n  refuses a PDF on an image field. Vitest case, mutation-checked.","tree":{"sha":"320f2a0b7def8c3c38441e251236c3810c640882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/320f2a0b7def8c3c38441e251236c3810c640882"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/90bc9f37443cc5b912641fec64170bfb6d646a8d","verification":{"payload":"tree 320f2a0b7def8c3c38441e251236c3810c640882\nparent 5a1b02ef728c9d7a06513aa54ed25cb9b46c5d04\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1790781902 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790781902 +0200\n\nfeat: allowed file types as one list from Apache Tika''s registry — extensions accepted, fields kept within it (#351)\n\n* feat: a file field''s types read from Apache Tika''s registry — the extensions shown and recognised, a default label for the editor — instead of tables in the module\n\n* fix: the accept labels come from the module''s bundle where it words them, else from Tika — Jahia''s resourceBundle initializer keyed on the label, no longer the type\n\n* chore: changelog entry for #351\n\n* chore: the quality gate''s two findings on #351 — the file island''s props read-only, String passed as is\n\n* feat: the allowed file types as one list the fields stay within — extensions accepted, an empty list refusing every file\n\n- uploadAllowedMimeTypes becomes uploadAllowedTypes: an extension (pdf, .docx), a MIME type or a wildcard,\n  each resolved once by Tika into its MIME type (logged); the default is written as extensions, the same\n  seventeen types. The legacy carry-over reads the setting under its former name and leaves 0.4''s default\n  list behind. The shipped file links Tika''s registry of the embedded version, held by a unit test.\n- AllowedTypes is the one reading of what a field accepts, shared by the parser and the file field''s view:\n  the field''s accept within the list (a type no longer listed dropped with a warning naming the field), the\n  whole list when it declares none, nothing when the list is empty — no longer every file. No parent type:\n  allowing txt does not allow SVG.\n- The view hands its node to FileTypeService.allowedFor; the island lists, filters and builds its accept\n  attribute from what the server lets through, the attribute from every recognised extension (.mov for\n  video/quicktime), and says when a field accepts no file.\n- Review round 1: the shown extension is the acronym''s when Tika''s preferred one is no abbreviation of it\n  (MP3 -> .mp3, JPEG keeps .jpg); a wildcard or an unknown type is labelled by the whole type; tests in\n  insertion order with trim cases, mutation-proved; the choicelist''s bundle lookup split and tested; the\n  island''s helpers moved to fileAccept.ts with vitest; Cypress spec 224.\n\n* fix: review round 2 and the quality gate on #351 — aliases read as Tika''s type, the parser''s step tested, the any-file replacement given\n\n- A MIME alias in uploadAllowedTypes is normalised through Tika''s registry (audio/x-wav -> audio/vnd.wave), the\n  type a file is detected as; the resolution is logged like an extension''s.\n- FormDataParser.checkAllowedType holds step 7 and is tested directly (a file part cannot be parsed without\n  JCRContentUtils initialised): an empty list refuses, a field''s type the list dropped is refused, a field without\n  types takes the list. The parser names no field in a log line, the name coming from the request (Sonar S5145);\n  the view warns, naming its node.\n- An empty list''s start warning gives the replacement for \"any file\" (the top-level wildcards), as do the upgrade\n  notes and the changelog; a theme file still holding uploadAllowedMimeTypes is named in a warning.\n- The docs say that pages already rendered keep the former list until the site''s cache is flushed.\n- The console''s description links Tika''s registry (UploadsConfig.TIKA_REGISTRY, held by the test with the\n  shipped file). The choicelist''s key composition is extracted and tested. Sonar S135 and S3358.\n\n* feat: a file whose content is a kind of its listed container type is accepted — an Ogg video named .ogv\n\nTika detects the codec inside a container: an .ogv file is video/theora, an\n.oga Opus track audio/opus, kinds of video/ogg and audio/ogg in its registry,\nso a listed ogv refused every real Ogg video. The parser now also accepts a\ndetected type that specializes the type the file''s name stands for, when that\ntype is listed as such, shares the top-level type and is not a root of the\nhierarchy (text/plain, application/octet-stream): an SVG named .xml or an HTML\npage named .txt stays refused. Each guard is held by a test (mutation-checked).\n\n* fix: review round 3 on #351 — */* for any file, the editor offering the top-level wildcards in its place\n\n- */* is read as any file: the server lets every detected type through, a file\n  field without types restricts nothing in the page (no accept attribute), a\n  field with types keeps its own. It holds whatever a future Tika adds, where\n  the five wildcards given before missed chemical/, message/ (.eml), model/,\n  multipart/ (.mht) and x-conference/.\n- The Accept setting never offers */*: in its place, a wildcard for each\n  top-level type of Tika''s registry, beside the other listed types, labelled\n  in four languages (Any image (image/*)).\n- The field''s warning tells a stored value that is no file type from one the\n  list no longer allows.\n- The shipped uploads file reflowed; the start warning, the console\n  description, the docs, the upgrade notes and the changelog give */*.\n- Sonar S3415: assertEquals arguments in order.\n\n* fix: review round 4 on #351 — the container rule for audio and video only, wildcards refusing a contradicting type, an empty 0.4 list kept as any file\n\n- permitsFile accepts a kind of the listed type the file''s name stands for for\n  audio and video only: elsewhere Tika''s kinds mean readable-as (199 kinds of\n  application/xml incl. XHTML, 76 of application/zip incl. jars and\n  macro-enabled documents). ROOTS goes; a jar named .zip is refused again.\n- The island refuses a file whose browser type contradicts a wildcard, even\n  when the wildcard lists no extension (a field narrowed to image/* under */*).\n- The migration carries an empty uploadAllowedMimeTypes, which meant any file\n  until 0.5, as uploadAllowedTypes=*/*: the upgrade keeps the behaviour.\n- Tests: a real Ogg Theora first page through Tika and permitsFile, XHTML/jar/\n  macro workbook refused, the island''s wildcard, the migration, and spec 224\n  under */* (an .eml attached and stored). Mutation-checked.\n- Docs: to narrow finely under */*, list the types next to it; a caution on\n  HTML and SVG under */*; upgrade notes and changelog no longer call the empty\n  list a breaking case; line lengths and a Javadoc wrap.\n\n* docs: removing an allowed type — the Content Editor keeps only the listed types at the next save, which can widen a field\n\nA stored accept value no longer listed is honoured again if the type comes\nback, but only until a contributor saves the field: the editor offers the\nlisted types only and saves what it shows. A field whose only types were\nremoved then accepts the whole list, or any file under */*; the admin is told\nto check the fields naming a type before removing it, and that */* alone\nremoves every specific type.\n\n* fix: review round 5 on #351 — what the detection proves for containers, a recognised extension over a contradicting browser type\n\n- The docs no longer claim a jar or a macro-enabled workbook named .zip is\n  refused: tika-core alone checks a zip or OLE2 container''s family by content\n  and takes its kind from the name, so any zip named .docx passes as a docx.\n  configuration.md says what the check proves per format; step 7, the console\n  description and the shipped file say it for containers; the XHTML example,\n  detected by its content, stays.\n- The island takes a recognised extension before refusing a contradicting\n  browser type: a .csv that Windows types application/vnd.ms-excel is a CSV on\n  a text/* field again; a wildcard listing no extension (under */*) still\n  refuses a PDF on an image field. Vitest case, mutation-checked.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvSnOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACqQQAILfkjin2mGEJyx/TLjMEpFq\n2XZtjPaS12jNsOT8jBAp/OouceiprbyRB9e7WYIxSmaSllsyC8GQcKqth5zpw5jI\naInF9esY92oP0BXB0PimjXHI+NCfRVWW+aBaP66YcB58rgXRQLYneAhWaBY9lLXa\nmYVzu3IsN84gSmHuBv4DwvIStPOcwU2aTgJCBSVANJy10JzunuUXySvqUJnIY0gw\nO8s4GVXoYOQWndkMduXNGwlv26V2aDj3qawf9pfz2/itdGhKGL8x0QqaIB8EKCiM\nRi3KYQEbkTfDh/Ew2q37i9cBhZv0raVUZwIMSTko7BVD8wDgt5MKvBkhqYRltg+p\nOqCOdkApMAi2EBo8xM3ShNmZMsqVC6MoSGXTbgazffAVhXaBYhAaZo7DycG+uAsm\nc4sa8FeiZv2PUle/HgtELAr+6UtHJkq5OIZW84uNpKIFD4muMbFE0hKYqb0zZHpG\n91up9yJDiRzBAMf83vbpdMijHtl3voCaBxPPIcEeculWMRAn4bh4YXiqQmzqU4/a\nxYVZOYsLMQKws3y0YvURLHIamiz5K8H2WXZHBaTSkXOPxY1oDjpBLSiXK0UisXVL\ngIA62aFWi32LAWl8DMMzHp+be9ZTBKCAy6Vz0y0Ngo41niOgZAyvHdQijPdJN2Lx\nV7Y8+wNeDJz6bW/KttPl\n=F/VV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T15:25:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"http