s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/23c0902fb5862cb9cd71589f801e2bacf79926f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:48:42Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:48:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: the jExperience module''s classes sit in packages named for their concern (#333)\n\n* refactor: the jExperience module names its own model once, and opens what its packages will share\n\nBefore the Java of formidable-jexperience-engine is split into packages, two things it needs:\n\n- Its CND names were spelt in three classes — SensitiveField held the sensitive mixin and flag,\n  FormMappingReader the mapping mixin and strategy, the choicelist initializer the profile\n  property — and SensitiveField read the initializer''s constant, an editor class, to know whether a\n  field is mapped. They now live in model.JxpMixin and model.JxpProperty, the rule #331 set for the\n  engine (the class states the kind, the constant the thing, a use is always qualified), and\n  DefinitionsCndTest checks the holders and the CND both ways, as the engine''s guard does for its own.\n- The three classes every package will read become public — SensitiveField, JExperienceSite, Json —\n  with the members they are read for (isMapped, isSensitive, tracked, configured, string), plus\n  FieldShapes.MULTIPLE_PROPERTY, the initializer''s KEPT_KEY and JExperienceSite.MODULE. Nothing is\n  exported: the bundle keeps Export-Package: !*, so public here means \"across this module''s packages\".\n\n* refactor: the jExperience module''s classes sit in packages named for their concern\n\nA pure move, from one package into eight — profile (the schema as jCustomer describes it),\nchoicelist (the editor''s dropdown), field (a field''s shape and its sensitive flag), rule (the\nmapping rule and its life in jCustomer), render (the page), submission (the answer), util (the two\nhelpers) and model (the module''s own names, from the previous commit): git mv, the package line,\nand the imports the new boundaries need. Tests follow their class; DefinitionsCndTest and\nResourceBundlesTest, which read the module''s resources, stay at the root.\n\nChecked on the built jar: the six DS components regenerate under their new names, the eight\npackages are in the bundle and nothing is left at the root, Export-Package stays !*; nothing\noutside the sources named the old package. The spec gains the table of packages.\n\n* test: the model parity reads the holders'' constants off the class\n\nThe expected side was a hand-written list, so a constant added to JxpMixin or JxpProperty with\nnothing declaring it passed unseen — only the CND → constant direction was held. Both are now:\nthe expected sets are the String constants reflection finds on the two holders. A GHOST constant\nfails the test, and so does a ghost mixin in the CND.","tree":{"sha":"c41e4189ca1567de44505284e5e784710b50b7cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/c41e4189ca1567de44505284e5e784710b50b7cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/23c0902fb5862cb9cd71589f801e2bacf79926f2","verification":{"payload":"tree c41e4189ca1567de44505284e5e784710b50b7cc\nparent cbcf06324203e46ea16aa033bb88d0f05141a139\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789652922 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789652922 +0200\n\nrefactor: the jExperience module''s classes sit in packages named for their concern (#333)\n\n* refactor: the jExperience module names its own model once, and opens what its packages will share\n\nBefore the Java of formidable-jexperience-engine is split into packages, two things it needs:\n\n- Its CND names were spelt in three classes — SensitiveField held the sensitive mixin and flag,\n  FormMappingReader the mapping mixin and strategy, the choicelist initializer the profile\n  property — and SensitiveField read the initializer''s constant, an editor class, to know whether a\n  field is mapped. They now live in model.JxpMixin and model.JxpProperty, the rule #331 set for the\n  engine (the class states the kind, the constant the thing, a use is always qualified), and\n  DefinitionsCndTest checks the holders and the CND both ways, as the engine''s guard does for its own.\n- The three classes every package will read become public — SensitiveField, JExperienceSite, Json —\n  with the members they are read for (isMapped, isSensitive, tracked, configured, string), plus\n  FieldShapes.MULTIPLE_PROPERTY, the initializer''s KEPT_KEY and JExperienceSite.MODULE. Nothing is\n  exported: the bundle keeps Export-Package: !*, so public here means \"across this module''s packages\".\n\n* refactor: the jExperience module''s classes sit in packages named for their concern\n\nA pure move, from one package into eight — profile (the schema as jCustomer describes it),\nchoicelist (the editor''s dropdown), field (a field''s shape and its sensitive flag), rule (the\nmapping rule and its life in jCustomer), render (the page), submission (the answer), util (the two\nhelpers) and model (the module''s own names, from the previous commit): git mv, the package line,\nand the imports the new boundaries need. Tests follow their class; DefinitionsCndTest and\nResourceBundlesTest, which read the module''s resources, stay at the root.\n\nChecked on the built jar: the six DS components regenerate under their new names, the eight\npackages are in the bundle and nothing is left at the root, Export-Package stays !*; nothing\noutside the sources named the old package. The spec gains the table of packages.\n\n* test: the model parity reads the holders'' constants off the class\n\nThe expected side was a hand-written list, so a constant added to JxpMixin or JxpProperty with\nnothing declaring it passed unseen — only the CND → constant direction was held. Both are now:\nthe expected sets are the String constants reflection finds on the two holders. A GHOST constant\nfails the test, and so does a ghost mixin in the CND.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq++6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADgwQADA8s9dkVjYxo65naaSN0rg2\nYMp5BgN5WGA2hC8jtkmFJbv7r9ooRjUhjvdzeHaAjfK9VNZA3TpnpsipEEgyfMYh\n7h0PNI+kMWJ4D9mGMwi1M/29jWpG5UyUcVCAxClXyKaaSoDri9qzBt43bgA5iSoe\n2wbLV4EgUj+Cec55hOD0wFeHZ+PYAXRXlVveyvlZVxwXZuAF/+ZsMjV7VPqVbiTE\nOXvMaQg4bTuWSVV4zBD7JdX12VOvc+buFUIMetm4qHjtYK2Ej9GMGhbPzwv1o2WR\nT/TZRXRUfTH/ZKDFToTIiETez10LT29y4v3jBwJfBed4Xn8/AK/bE0C4+KO+bGB7\nCv99maOknW5n+/Aj++c8XabExR0MrHldIhoGcy0ibdprzH0aShTiEQxTBxCXECK6\nZdDvxN+jfgLoQ2YgMwfy7V87AMpgM1Ysla/Ky9D+2/IgWJ6XWX4bUA7VL/b7LP6x\nc91IUmLc5YgVkoiSyiMQ+zS+APYkmi0bwrtDNq5vQrthPh50QwYbWhyYsHX+0Jbt\n9gFUyPV2eXvyve2WnV4oHG8umvbE9LTENguJg0WXtsD7oL0jU4F6DJMGaFuyJZB+\nvx8wTC+cdChjGFtRFvDMH4Bl/vRlaB6aAwcWrPAXlySZpK3mWCejaak8NzhckYjR\nIc3XxkdLuHqvsDrME4lY\n=x5aF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T13:48:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{