er cannot see: a form deleted by a published deletion, and a field\n  whose jExperience section was switched off — verified on the lab, the rule is deleted when\n  that field alone is published. MappingRuleRemovalListener is folded into it; onEvent runs\n  through a live-session seam the tests exercise, asking the synchronizer''s coalescing entry\n  point, never the immediate one.\n- Locale: LanguageCodeConverters.languageCodeToLocale for Jahia''s en_US-style codes; the\n  per-language fallback loop, dead code, is gone; a form outside a site yields no rule.\n- Pending list: a site with no jExperience configuration (getContextServerStatus null) is\n  left alone, neither error nor retry; a form that cannot be read is dropped; the retry loop\n  catches every error so the scheduler never drops it, and stops at the first form still\n  unreachable — now tested with a store failing per rule.\n- The form''s path is a SQL2 literal with its quotes doubled; the query text has a test.\n- long is a plain value, as for jExperience''s screen; owned() is tested to see a changed\n  priority, condition or action list; MappingRule''s javadoc names the two deliberate\n  differences from the screen''s rules (whole-site source only, typed parameter only).\n- 84 tests. Spec: listener row merged, six decision-log rows, roadmap proof.\n\n* fix: the rule''s JSON keys are constants and a test drops a throws it cannot use (Sonar S1192, S1130)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqELiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEQEQABSIzDMf0xsBceGtB0PlEmXg\nx+lDHJq1im2UVf3rOt9jLcaSYb9mVaCBA/ZEHeo9YvaQshy57nXG52n4x8VleqrV\no0EoesY+jcvnphnZ02x8M8ML/hB5Cqsm2r6ozoiEdKkKRM2FJ9UQA9czrxej+Fvt\nIABr02psZsHXsJ2Xl0DIN0DVA05IqkOexpkOy5Nf+eHHgsabS5uGt5Jt+1tSNt6/\nxdfcdwVYGNqkiAsyxCivX2qhA3dsLAj8m+MS5cVVkDYTCp5Uur3MpVZWsULYF8tF\nWfpn4keHEhKzYBlCl6YbYp1N/DqTdgAIA4RodBClE76/epuHVbO7gWLYWbbr7uAp\nd2o8HKz+IF71k8G4zihTYSXaQBnz+UpkQm3ur+O29CK+tIvAfWqP2/Q0jigqDBBg\n4hFr5t9sXtpYdTjDzA8KpNyLnF0fovYM0ER