/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/c4b755783fe7d82e91abcc98733d497f7a0a54f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:20:54Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T15:20:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: jExperience integration, phase 1 — profile-mappable fields, the jExperience editor section and the form identifier (#324)\n\n* docs: the jExperience integration design specification\n\nAuto-generated form mapping, server-sent form event, server-side prefill: the contract extracted from the Forms stack, the data flows, the trust model, the decisions taken on 2026-09-09 and the roadmap. Not implemented yet; this branch carries the implementation.\n\n* docs: the jExperience integration goes browser-side — tracker-sent event with the pipeline''s accepted values, prefill from the tracker''s context, formidable-jxp-<uuid>, the send condition\n\nRevision of the 2026-09-09 specification after Romain''s review (CSR, no server-side probe of\njCustomer''s rules) and the design discussion of 2026-09-10 with HDU. Every decision is dated\nand reasoned in the decision log: why the server-side event and prefill were dropped (personal\ndata in cacheable HTML, a jCustomer call per page view), why the event still carries only the\nvalues the pipeline accepted (a generic SubmissionResponseEnricher SPI puts them in the 200),\nwhy getFormNamesToWatch() is kept and confined to one function (a goal on an unmapped form must\ncount; Romain may remove trackedConditions later, this is the line to change), why\ndisableTrackedConditionsListeners is honoured (Forms goes silent under it, Formidable too),\nand why the identifier is formidable-jxp-<uuid> and never the DOM form id (the tracker attaches\nits raw-fields listener by id/name match). Sources: the Unomi tracker 1.5.0, jExperience''s\nwem.js and tests, the Forms bridge, the Unomi form event schemas.\n\n* feat: the field types carry the marker a jExperience profile mapping builds on\n\nfmdbmix:profileMappableField, declared by the engine, says \"this field can take part in a\nprofile mapping\". Sixteen field types claim it as a supertype next to fmdbmix:element — every\nvalue-holding input of the elements and extended-inputs modules; not the file input, the\nbutton, the containers. The jExperience module attaches its property mixin to this single\nmarker (extends), so a third-party field opts in from its own CND, exactly as it opts into a\nvalue kind, and no module enumerates field types.\n\nThe elements now need the 0.5 engine (the marker), the extended inputs the 0.5 elements and\nengine: module-dependencies say so, and the extension guides pin the same versions. The CND\nownership catalog and the new-field-type recipes name the marker.\n\n* feat: formidable-jexperience-engine — the jExperience section of a field and the form''s identifier\n\nPhase 1 of docs/architecture/jexperience-integration.md, on jExperience 4.2.1 with open OSGi\nranges ([4,5) on its admin package, [3,4) on the Unomi API):\n\n- fmdbmix:jExperienceProfileMapping extends the engine''s marker with the profile property, the\n  prefill toggle and the write strategy, shown as a \"jExperience\" section (rank 1.15, after\n  Logic) of every mappable field, switch-gated: switching it on is the author''s \"map this field\".\n- The dropdown is fed by ProfilePropertiesChoiceListInitializer: FieldShapes infers the field''s\n  value types and cardinality from its value-kind mixins (fmdb:checkbox is the one type name\n  read — no mixin tells the checkbox group from a radio group), ProfilePropertyFilter drops\n  hidden, read-only, protected, system and mapping-hidden properties, ProfilePropertyCatalog\n  reads jCustomer through jExperience''s admin client and keeps the list five minutes per site,\n  serving the previous one when a refresh fails; an unreachable jCustomer on a first read yields\n  one message entry with an empty value, never a broken editor.\n- fmdbmix:jExperienceForm shows the form its identity in jCustomer, formidable-jxp-<uuid>,\n  read-only: FormIdentifierListener stamps it when a form is created or first edited after the\n  module arrived (climbing from the j:translation_* subnode an i18n edit fires on).\n- Jahia EE refuses an unsigned org.jahia.modules bundle: the pom carries the keymaker signature.\n\n23 unit tests: shape inference, property filter, catalog cache and failure paths, initializer,\nidentifier. Deployed next to jExperience 4.2.1 on the test instance: the section lists 18 string\nproperties on a text field; the identifier is stamped on creation and on the first edit. The\ndesign document records the phase, the decisions it took and what jCustomer 3 actually exposes.\n\n* fix: the catalog holds jExperience''s service in an AtomicReference, and two names Sonar flagged\n\nS3077: a volatile reference is not thread-safe enough for Sonar — the dynamic OSGi reference is\nbound and unbound into an AtomicReference, as the engine''s servlet does with its PermissionService.\nS1845: the initializer''s instance field no longer reads like its KEY constant. S125: a test\ncomment with a semicolon read as commented-out code.\n\n* fix: the author reads \"visitor profile\", never \"jCustomer\"\n\njCustomer is the platform''s name, not the author''s vocabulary: the labels, tooltips and the\nunavailability message of the jExperience section speak of the visitor profile — the same words\nthe prefill toggle already used. jExperience stays, as the name of the section and of the product\nthe author configures goals in.\n\n* docs: the mapping mixin extends the marker without inheriting from it, as the code does\n\nThe design''s CND block still wrote \"> fmdbmix:profileMappableField\" next to extends; the code\nnever did. A node carrying the mapping must not become mappable by inheritance — the type declares\nthat — and no property mixin of the repository inherits from its extends target. Recorded in the\ndecision log.\n\n* docs: the hidden 0.4 spellings are marked deprecated since 0.5, removed in 0.6, in the CND itself\n\nEighteen \"- fmdb:\" properties stay declared, hidden, so that a 0.4 export still imports and\nMixinPropertyNamesMigration can copy them into their unprefixed names at startup. The definition\nnow says so where a reader meets them, with the version that removes them — the one the upgrade\nnotes and the migrations'' javadoc already give.\n\n* fix: the engine CND''s namespace URIs are back to /1.0\n\nThe previous commit''s version replacement also rewrote the six namespace declarations to /0.6,\nwhich made jahia-maven-plugin:dependencies see a second jnt prefix with another URI when it read\nthe jExperience module''s CND after the engine''s (CI: NullPointerException; locally: prefix\nalready declared). The instance never received that CND.\n\n* feat: the profile-property dropdown says when nothing matches, and forgets its list after a minute\n\njCustomer''s default schema has no boolean property: an author opening the jExperience section of a\nswitch met a blank dropdown with nothing to explain it. An empty match now yields one entry with an\nempty value that says so, like the unreachable case. The catalog''s time to live goes from five\nminutes to one, so a property just created in jExperience shows at the next opening of a field.\n\n* docs: the property tooltip says a property just created in jExperience can take a minute to appear\n\nThe author who creates a profile property in jExperience and comes straight back to the field\nmeets the previous list for up to a minute; the tooltip says so, in the author''s words, and what\nto do.\n\n* docs: the profile-property catalog''s cache — when jCustomer is called, what it costs, what the minute buys\n\nThe Content Editor evaluates the initializer at every opening or creation of a mappable field,\nsection unfolded or not; the call costs 10-17 ms next to jCustomer and a network round trip\naway from it; the catalog''s one-minute, per-site memory is shared by every author of the node,\nserves the previous list on a failed refresh, and is the one-minute delay the tooltip explains.\nRemoving it was weighed and declined (same worst case, no resilience) — decision logged.\n\n* docs: the property tooltip leads with the note on the delay, in bold, then the description\n\nNote first, the one-minute delay in bold, a blank line, then what the field is — the Content Editor\nrenders descriptions as HTML, as the engine''s own tooltips already rely on.\n\n* feat: the message entry of an empty dropdown is pre-selected, and the tooltip breaks one line\n\nWith jCustomer unreachable or no property of the field''s kind, the single entry now carries\njcontent''s defaultProperty flag: the Content Editor takes it as the initial value, so the author\nreads the message in the closed select instead of finding it in the list. Saving it still stores\nnothing. The tooltip''s note is followed by one line break, not two.\n\n* feat: one duration for the profile-property list — past the minute, a failed read gives the message\n\nThe catalog served an expired list through any outage, without limit: an author could map to a\nlist an hour old without knowing. Now a list is served while under a minute old; past that, the\nnext opening reads jCustomer again and a failed read reports the schema unavailable — the\nmessage entry — and drops the stale list so a later success starts a fresh minute. One rule to\nexplain instead of a grace period needing a second duration.\n\n* fix: a field''s stored mapping stays in the dropdown when the list lacks it\n\njcontent''s single select resets a value absent from its constraints: opening a mapped field while\njCustomer is down — or after the property left the schema — and saving anything would have wiped\nthe mapping silently. The stored value is now offered first, flagged \"(current mapping, kept)\",\nthe explanatory entry second; the author keeps it or picks another entry, knowingly. An empty\nstored value is not a mapping and gets no such entry.\n\n* feat: every existing form gets its jExperience identifier when the module starts\n\nA form created before the module arrived showed an empty read-only identifier until its next save\n— a dead field with nothing to do about it. The listener now stamps every fmdb:form it finds when\nit activates (the identifier derives from the UUID: idempotent, no jExperience or jCustomer\nneeded), and keeps stamping forms created afterwards.\n\n* fix: the catalog''s logger went unused once the stale list stopped being served (Sonar S1068)\n\n* fix: the jCustomer resource read by the profile-property catalog is named as an endpoint, not a path (Sonar S1075)\n\n* fix: phase-1 review — a copied form gets its own identifier, the start-up pass follows the engine''s rules, failures are remembered, cardinality follows the editor''s toggle\n\nReview of PR #324 (2026-09-14), every inline thread:\n\n- FormIdentifierListener: the stamp compares the stored identifier with the one the\n  node''s own UUID gives instead of trusting its presence, so a JCR copy or an import is\n  re-stamped; the start-up pass is scoped to /sites, saves one form at a time with a\n  refresh(false) on failure, and the observation is scoped the same way; the default-only\n  write is documented (Lifecycle note, upgrade notes, spec).\n- ProfilePropertyCatalog: a failed read is remembered for ten seconds, so a hung jCustomer\n  (30 s admin timeout) is not paid at every field opening by every author.\n- FieldShapes / ProfilePropertiesChoiceListInitializer: the choicelist declares\n  dependentProperties=''multiple'' and the unsaved toggle is read from the editor''s context,\n  on an existing node and in create mode (which now takes the javax.jcr NodeType interface);\n  the `multiple` cardinality convention and the one-option checkbox limit are written into\n  the compatibility table; setKey is a no-op like the engine''s initializers.\n- fmdbmix:jExperienceForm inherits jmix:templateMixin: the identifier fieldset has no\n  enable switch any more (switching it off dropped the mixin and the value).\n- pom: nothing exported, analyze-only with failOnWarning, jahia-depends names\n  formidable-elements, the range comment reads as the manifest does, the unused servlet\n  dependency is gone, commons-lang is declared for the mocked wrapper signatures.\n- 47 JUnit tests (26 before): the listener, the entry points on nodes and types, the\n  initializer through the editor''s context, the failure memory, the durations, a bodyless\n  answer; the subclass mock maker as in the engine.\n- docs: banner, identifier derivation, decision log, roadmap, open questions, README,\n  upgrade notes, dependency decisions, extension guide.\n\n* fix: the servlet API the Jahia modules parent hands to the CI build is ignored by the dependency analysis of the jExperience module\n\n* fix: the failure memory of the profile-property catalog is dated from the end of the call, the CND clauses are pinned, the test smells are gone\n\nSecond review round on PR #324 (2026-09-14 09:53):\n\n- ProfilePropertyCatalog read the clock before the blocking fetch: after a 30 s admin\n  timeout the \"unavailable\" entry was stored already expired and the next author waited\n  the timeout again. The clock is read when the entry is stored; a test advances it inside\n  the stubbed call.\n- DefinitionsCndTest pins the three CND clauses the Java relies on and no test environment\n  guards yet: the mapping mixin extends the marker, the choicelist declares\n  dependentProperties=''multiple'', the form mixin inherits jmix:templateMixin.\n- Fixtures: the start-up pass fixture carries a form that already has its identifier, so\n  the returned count is pinned; the empty-list case is asserted on a node stored\n  multiple = true, where \"stored applies\" and \"forced single\" differ.\n- Sonar: assertions on toSeconds() literals (S3415) and assertEquals on the key (S5785).\n- 50 JUnit tests; spec: two decision-log rows and the failure-memory paragraph.\n\n* fix: a test comment no longer reads as commented-out code to Sonar (S125)\n\n* feat: a checkbox''s profile-property list follows its number of choices, counted as the view renders them\n\nHDU, 2026-09-14: no `multiple` property on the checkbox — one choice is one checkbox, one\nvalue; anything else is a group, exactly the renderer''s rule.\n\n- Engine: a new api interface, ChoiceOptionsResolver, counts a field''s choices the way the\n  views resolve them (the options source when the field uses one, the manual list aligned on\n  the default language otherwise, the stored list as a last resort); implemented in the\n  options package, registered as an OSGi service, 5 tests.\n- jExperience module: FieldShapes takes the count for the checkbox rule; the initializer\n  gets it from the options the editor holds unsaved (dependentProperties now names\n  `options` and `optionsMode` too) or from the engine on the saved node; an unsaved switch\n  to a sourced mode leaves the count unknown, a group, until the save. The module depends\n  on the engine''s exported api package.\n- Docs: compatibility table and checkbox rule, decision log (the \"known limit\" row is\n  superseded), the open question closed, dependency decisions, extension guide.\n- Verified on the local instance: a one-choice checkbox lists the single-valued strings, a\n  three-choice one the multivalued entry, and the unsaved `options` list reshapes both.\n\n* fix: a stored mapping the available property list does not carry is no longer offered — \"kept\" is for an outage only\n\nHDU, 2026-09-14: a checkbox that became a group showed \"gender (current mapping, kept)\",\na mapping phase 2 would never turn into a rule. When jCustomer answers, the list is the\ntruth: a stored property whose cardinality or type no longer fits the field, or one gone\nfrom the schema, is not offered, the editor resets the select and the next save clears the\ninvalid mapping. The flagged entry stays for the one case where the list says nothing about\nthe mapping — jCustomer cannot be asked — so an outage still cannot wipe a mapping the\nauthor never touched. Tests and the spec''s decision log follow.\n\n* fix: during a jCustomer outage the stored mapping is the one entry of the list, described, so nothing else can be picked\n\nHDU, 2026-09-14: two entries during an outage — \"gender (current mapping, kept)\" and the\n\"not connected\" message — let the author pick the message and wipe the mapping, and \"kept\"\nsaid nothing. Now the stored value is the only entry, labelled by its id, with a description\nunder it: \"Current mapping, left unchanged: the visitor profile properties cannot be listed\nright now (jExperience is not connected)\". Nothing else to choose, nothing to break. A true\nread-only is out of reach from an initializer: jcontent disables a select only when its list\nis empty, and an empty list also resets the value. Without a stored mapping the message\nentry stands alone, as before. EN/FR labels, tests, spec.\n\n* fix: the choice count is asked for a checkbox only — a supplier FieldShapes calls in that one branch\n\nReview of d4b839a: `choiceCountOf` was an eager argument, so every mappable field the editor\nopened paid the count — for a content- or category-sourced select or radio, a repository\nquery whose result the select''s rule never reads. FieldShapes now takes a ChoiceCount\nsupplier and calls it under isNodeType(fmdb:checkbox) only; the initializer hands it the\nlazy computation. A test pins the laziness: a text field and a select never reach the\nengine''s resolver, a checkbox does.\n\n* fix: the Sonar smells of the last three commits (method references, a needless throws, an orphan local, a useless eq(), a comment read as code)\n\n* fix: the description under the kept entry carries no i18next separator\n\nReview of 0e531e3: jcontent hands an entry''s description to i18next''s t() as if it were a\nkey, whose default separators are \":\" (namespace) and \".\" (key path); on a miss only the part\nafter them may render. Both sentences (EN, FR) lose their colon; ResourceBundlesTest pins the\nabsence of both separators in every language.\n\n* docs: the separator-free kept description is a precaution, not an observed truncation\n\nThree reservations on 43b8ea2, applied where the next reader looks: the code and test\ncomments say that whether jcontent''s i18next truncates a plain sentence at \":\" or \".\" has\nnot been observed (the fix is safe either way, the on-screen check is still to do); the\nlabel/description asymmetry is written down — \"none\" and \"unavailable\" are entry labels\nrendered verbatim and keep their colon, only \"kept\" travels as a description, which is the\ntest''s scope; and the assertion messages say why the colon and the period are refused. A\ndecision-log row records the same.","tree":{"sha":"80336f5c08dfefd2cf1083d10b6554141c8b7ec0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/80336f5c08dfefd2cf1083d10b6554141c8b7ec0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/c4b755783fe7d82e91abcc98733d497f7a0a54f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 80336f5c08dfefd2cf1083d10b6554141c8b7ec0\nparent 36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789399254 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789399254 +0200\n\nfeat: jExperience integration, phase 1 — profile-mappable fields, the jExperience editor section and the form identifier (#324)\n\n* docs: the jExperience integration design specification\n\nAuto-generated form mapping, server-sent form event, server-side prefill: the contract extracted from the Forms stack, the data flows, the trust model, the decisions taken on 2026-09-09 and the roadmap. Not implemented yet; this branch carries the implementation.\n\n* docs: the jExperience integration goes browser-side — tracker-sent event with the pipeline''s accepted values, prefill from the tracker''s context, formidable-jxp-<uuid>, the send condition\n\nRevision of the 2026-09-09 specification after Romain''s review (CSR, no server-side probe of\njCustomer''s rules) and the design discussion of 2026-09-10 with HDU. Every decision is dated\nand reasoned in the decision log: why the server-side event and prefill were dropped (personal\ndata in cacheable HTML, a jCustomer call per page view), why the event still carries only the\nvalues the pipeline accepted (a generic SubmissionResponseEnricher SPI puts them in the 200),\nwhy getFormNamesToWatch() is kept and confined to one function (a goal on an unmapped form must\ncount; Romain may remove trackedConditions later, this is the line to change), why\ndisableTrackedConditionsListeners is honoured (Forms goes silent under it, Formidable too),\nand why the identifier is formidable-jxp-<uuid> and never the DOM form id (the tracker attaches\nits raw-fields listener by id/name match). Sources: the Unomi tracker 1.5.0, jExperience''s\nwem.js and tests, the Forms bridge, the Unomi form event schemas.\n\n* feat: the field types carry the marker a jExperience profile mapping builds on\n\nfmdbmix:profileMappableField, declared by the engine, says \"this field can take part in a\nprofile mapping\". Sixteen field types claim it as a supertype next to fmdbmix:element — every\nvalue-holding input of the elements and extended-inputs modules; not the file input, the\nbutton, the containers. The jExperience module attaches its property mixin to this single\nmarker (extends), so a third-party field opts in from its own CND, exactly as it opts into a\nvalue kind, and no module enumerates field types.\n\nThe elements now need the 0.5 engine (the marker), the extended inputs the 0.5 elements and\nengine: module-dependencies say so, and the extension guides pin the same versions. The CND\nownership catalog and the new-field-type recipes name the marker.\n\n* feat: formidable-jexperience-engine — the jExperience section of a field and the form''s identifier\n\nPhase 1 of docs/architecture/jexperience-integration.md, on jExperience 4.2.1 with open OSGi\nranges ([4,5) on its admin package, [3,4) on the Unomi API):\n\n- fmdbmix:jExperienceProfileMapping extends the engine''s marker with the profile property, the\n  prefill toggle and the write strategy, shown as a \"jExperience\" section (rank 1.15, after\n  Logic) of every mappable field, switch-gated: switching it on is the author''s \"map this field\".\n- The dropdown is fed by ProfilePropertiesChoiceListInitializer: FieldShapes infers the field''s\n  value types and cardinality from its value-kind mixins (fmdb:checkbox is the one type name\n  read — no mixin tells the checkbox group from a radio group), ProfilePropertyFilter drops\n  hidden, read-only, protected, system and mapping-hidden properties, ProfilePropertyCatalog\n  reads jCustomer through jExperience''s admin client and keeps the list five minutes per site,\n  serving the previous one when a refresh fails; an unreachable jCustomer on a first read yields\n  one message entry with an empty value, never a broken editor.\n- fmdbmix:jExperienceForm shows the form its identity in jCustomer, formidable-jxp-<uuid>,\n  read-only: FormIdentifierListener stamps it when a form is created or first edited after the\n  module arrived (climbing from the j:translation_* subnode an i18n edit fires on).\n- Jahia EE refuses an unsigned org.jahia.modules bundle: the pom carries the keymaker signature.\n\n23 unit tests: shape inference, property filter, catalog cache and failure paths, initializer,\nidentifier. Deployed next to jExperience 4.2.1 on the test instance: the section lists 18 string\nproperties on a text field; the identifier is stamped on creation and on the first edit. The\ndesign document records the phase, the decisions it took and what jCustomer 3 actually exposes.\n\n* fix: the catalog holds jExperience''s service in an AtomicReference, and two names Sonar flagged\n\nS3077: a volatile reference is not thread-safe enough for Sonar — the dynamic OSGi reference is\nbound and unbound into an AtomicReference, as the engine''s servlet does with its PermissionService.\nS1845: the initializer''s instance field no longer reads like its KEY constant. S125: a test\ncomment with a semicolon read as commented-out code.\n\n* fix: the author reads \"visitor profile\", never \"jCustomer\"\n\njCustomer is the platform''s name, not the author''s vocabulary: the labels, tooltips and the\nunavailability message of the jExperience section speak of the visitor profile — the same words\nthe prefill toggle already used. jExperience stays, as the name of the section and of the product\nthe author configures goals in.\n\n* docs: the mapping mixin extends the marker without inheriting from it, as the code does\n\nThe design''s CND block still wrote \"> fmdbmix:profileMappableField\" next to extends; the code\nnever did. A node carrying the mapping must not become mappable by inheritance — the type declares\nthat — and no property mixin of the repository inherits from its extends target. Recorded in the\ndecision log.\n\n* docs: the hidden 0.4 spellings are marked deprecated since 0.5, removed in 0.6, in the CND itself\n\nEighteen \"- fmdb:\" properties stay declared, hidden, so that a 0.4 export still imports and\nMixinPropertyNamesMigration can copy them into their unprefixed names at startup. The definition\nnow says so where a reader meets them, with the version that removes them — the one the upgrade\nnotes and the migrations'' javadoc already give.\n\n* fix: the engine CND''s namespace URIs are back to /1.0\n\nThe previous commit''s version replacement also rewrote the six namespace declarations to /0.6,\nwhich made jahia-maven-plugin:dependencies see a second jnt prefix with another URI when it read\nthe jExperience module''s CND after the engine''s (CI: NullPointerException; locally: prefix\nalready declared). The instance never received that CND.\n\n* feat: the profile-property dropdown says when nothing matches, and forgets its list after a minute\n\njCustomer''s default schema has no boolean property: an author opening the jExperience section of a\nswitch met a blank dropdown with nothing to explain it. An empty match now yields one entry with an\nempty value that says so, like the unreachable case. The catalog''s time to live goes from five\nminutes to one, so a property just created in jExperience shows at the next opening of a field.\n\n* docs: the property tooltip says a property just created in jExperience can take a minute to appear\n\nThe author who creates a profile property in jExperience and comes straight back to the field\nmeets the previous list for up to a minute; the tooltip says so, in the author''s words, and what\nto do.\n\n* docs: the profile-property catalog''s cache — when jCustomer is called, what it costs, what the minute buys\n\nThe Content Editor evaluates the initializer at every opening or creation of a mappable field,\nsection unfolded or not; the call costs 10-17 ms next to jCustomer and a network round trip\naway from it; the catalog''s one-minute, per-site memory is shared by every author of the node,\nserves the previous list on a failed refresh, and is the one-minute delay the tooltip explains.\nRemoving it was weighed and declined (same worst case, no resilience) — decision logged.\n\n* docs: the property tooltip leads with the note on the delay, in bold, then the description\n\nNote first, the one-minute delay in bold, a blank line, then what the field is — the Content Editor\nrenders descriptions as HTML, as the engine''s own tooltips already rely on.\n\n* feat: the message entry of an empty dropdown is pre-selected, and the tooltip breaks one line\n\nWith jCustomer unreachable or no property of the field''s kind, the single entry now carries\njcontent''s defaultProperty flag: the Content Editor takes it as the initial value, so the author\nreads the message in the closed select instead of finding it in the list. Saving it still stores\nnothing. The tooltip''s note is followed by one line break, not two.\n\n* feat: one duration for the profile-property list — past the minute, a failed read gives the message\n\nThe catalog served an expired list through any outage, without limit: an author could map to a\nlist an hour old without knowing. Now a list is served while under a minute old; past that, the\nnext opening reads jCustomer again and a failed read reports the schema unavailable — the\nmessage entry — and drops the stale list so a later success starts a fresh minute. One rule to\nexplain instead of a grace period needing a second duration.\n\n* fix: a field''s stored mapping stays in the dropdown when the list lacks it\n\njcontent''s single select resets a value absent from its constraints: opening a mapped field while\njCustomer is down — or after the property left the schema — and saving anything would have wiped\nthe mapping silently. The stored value is now offered first, flagged \"(current mapping, kept)\",\nthe explanatory entry second; the author keeps it or picks another entry, knowingly. An empty\nstored value is not a mapping and gets no such entry.\n\n* feat: every existing form gets its jExperience identifier when the module starts\n\nA form created before the module arrived showed an empty read-only identifier until its next save\n— a dead field with nothing to do about it. The listener now stamps every fmdb:form it finds when\nit activates (the identifier derives from the UUID: idempotent, no jExperience or jCustomer\nneeded), and keeps stamping forms created afterwards.\n\n* fix: the catalog''s logger went unused once the stale list stopped being served (Sonar S1068)\n\n* fix: the jCustomer resource read by the profile-property catalog is named as an endpoint, not a path (Sonar S1075)\n\n* fix: phase-1 review — a copied form gets its own identifier, the start-up pass follows the engine''s rules, failures are remembered, cardinality follows the editor''s toggle\n\nReview of PR #324 (2026-09-14), every inline thread:\n\n- FormIdentifierListener: the stamp compares the stored identifier with the one the\n  node''s own UUID gives instead of trusting its presence, so a JCR copy or an import is\n  re-stamped; the start-up pass is scoped to /sites, saves one form at a time with a\n  refresh(false) on failure, and the observation is scoped the same way; the default-only\n  write is documented (Lifecycle note, upgrade notes, spec).\n- ProfilePropertyCatalog: a failed read is remembered for ten seconds, so a hung jCustomer\n  (30 s admin timeout) is not paid at every field opening by every author.\n- FieldShapes / ProfilePropertiesChoiceListInitializer: the choicelist declares\n  dependentProperties=''multiple'' and the unsaved toggle is read from the editor''s context,\n  on an existing node and in create mode (which now takes the javax.jcr NodeType interface);\n  the `multiple` cardinality convention and the one-option checkbox limit are written into\n  the compatibility table; setKey is a no-op like the engine''s initializers.\n- fmdbmix:jExperienceForm inherits jmix:templateMixin: the identifier fieldset has no\n  enable switch any more (switching it off dropped the mixin and the value).\n- pom: nothing exported, analyze-only with failOnWarning, jahia-depends names\n  formidable-elements, the range comment reads as the manifest does, the unused servlet\n  dependency is gone, commons-lang is declared for the mocked wrapper signatures.\n- 47 JUnit tests (26 before): the listener, the entry points on nodes and types, the\n  initializer through the editor''s context, the failure memory, the durations, a bodyless\n  answer; the subclass mock maker as in the engine.\n- docs: banner, identifier derivation, decision log, roadmap, open questions, README,\n  upgrade notes, dependency decisions, extension guide.\n\n* fix: the servlet API the Jahia modules parent hands to the CI build is ignored by the dependency analysis of the jExperience module\n\n* fix: the failure memory of the profile-property catalog is dated from the end of the call, the CND clauses are pinned, the test smells are gone\n\nSecond review round on PR #324 (2026-09-14 09:53):\n\n- ProfilePropertyCatalog read the clock before the blocking fetch: after a 30 s admin\n  timeout the \"unavailable\" entry was stored already expired and the next author waited\n  the timeout again. The clock is read when the entry is stored; a test advances it inside\n  the stubbed call.\n- DefinitionsCndTest pins the three CND clauses the Java relies on and no test environment\n  guards yet: the mapping mixin extends the marker, the choicelist declares\n  dependentProperties=''multiple'', the form mixin inherits jmix:templateMixin.\n- Fixtures: the start-up pass fixture carries a form that already has its identifier, so\n  the returned count is pinned; the empty-list case is asserted on a node stored\n  multiple = true, where \"stored applies\" and \"forced single\" differ.\n- Sonar: assertions on toSeconds() literals (S3415) and assertEquals on the key (S5785).\n- 50 JUnit tests; spec: two decision-log rows and the failure-memory paragraph.\n\n* fix: a test comment no longer reads as commented-out code to Sonar (S125)\n\n* feat: a checkbox''s profile-property list follows its number of choices, counted as the view renders them\n\nHDU, 2026-09-14: no `multiple` property on the checkbox — one choice is one checkbox, one\nvalue; anything else is a group, exactly the renderer''s rule.\n\n- Engine: a new api interface, ChoiceOptionsResolver, counts a field''s choices the way the\n  views resolve them (the options source when the field uses one, the manual list aligned on\n  the default language otherwise, the stored list as a last resort); implemented in the\n  options package, registered as an OSGi service, 5 tests.\n- jExperience module: FieldShapes takes the count for the checkbox rule; the initializer\n  gets it from the options the editor holds unsaved (dependentProperties now names\n  `options` and `optionsMode` too) or from the engine on the saved node; an unsaved switch\n  to a sourced mode leaves the count unknown, a group, until the save. The module depends\n  on the engine''s exported api package.\n- Docs: compatibility table and checkbox rule, decision log (the \"known limit\" row is\n  superseded), the open question closed, dependency decisions, extension guide.\n- Verified on the local instance: a one-choice checkbox lists the single-valued strings, a\n  three-choice one the multivalued entry, and the unsaved `options` list reshapes both.\n\n* fix: a stored mapping the available property list does not carry is no longer offered — \"kept\" is for an outage only\n\nHDU, 2026-09-14: a checkbox that became a group showed \"gender (current mapping, kept)\",\na mapping phase 2 would never turn into a rule. When jCustomer answers, the list is the\ntruth: a stored property whose cardinality or type no longer fits the field, or one gone\nfrom the schema, is not offered, the editor resets the select and the next save clears the\ninvalid mapping. The flagged entry stays for the one case where the list says nothing about\nthe mapping — jCustomer cannot be asked — so an outage still cannot wipe a mapping the\nauthor never touched. Tests and the spec''s decision log follow.\n\n* fix: during a jCustomer outage the stored mapping is the one entry of the list, described, so nothing else can be picked\n\nHDU, 2026-09-14: two entries during an outage — \"gender (current mapping, kept)\" and the\n\"not connected\" message — let the author pick the message and wipe the mapping, and \"kept\"\nsaid nothing. Now the stored value is the only entry, labelled by its id, with a description\nunder it: \"Current mapping, left unchanged: the visitor profile properties cannot be listed\nright now (jExperience is not connected)\". Nothing else to choose, nothing to break. A true\nread-only is out of reach from an initializer: jcontent disables a select only when its list\nis empty, and an empty list also resets the value. Without a stored mapping the message\nentry stands alone, as before. EN/FR labels, tests, spec.\n\n* fix: the choice count is asked for a checkbox only — a supplier FieldShapes calls in that one branch\n\nReview of d4b839a: `choiceCountOf` was an eager argument, so every mappable field the editor\nopened paid the count — for a content- or category-sourced select or radio, a repository\nquery whose result the select''s rule never reads. FieldShapes now takes a ChoiceCount\nsupplier and calls it under isNodeType(fmdb:checkbox) only; the initializer hands it the\nlazy computation. A test pins the laziness: a text field and a select never reach the\nengine''s resolver, a checkbox does.\n\n* fix: the Sonar smells of the last three commits (method references, a needless throws, an orphan local, a useless eq(), a comment read as code)\n\n* fix: the description under the kept entry carries no i18next separator\n\nReview of 0e531e3: jcontent hands an entry''s description to i18next''s t() as if it were a\nkey, whose default separators are \":\" (namespace) and \".\" (key path); on a miss only the part\nafter them may render. Both sentences (EN, FR) lose their colon; ResourceBundlesTest pins the\nabsence of both separators in every language.\n\n* docs: the separator-free kept description is a precaution, not an observed truncation\n\nThree reservations on 43b8ea2, applied where the next reader looks: the code and test\ncomments say that whether jcontent''s i18next truncates a plain sentence at \":\" or \".\" has\nnot been observed (the fix is safe either way, the on-screen check is still to do); the\nlabel/description asymmetry is written down — \"none\" and \"unavailable\" are entry labels\nrendered verbatim and keep their colon, only \"kept\" travels as a description, which is the\ntest''s scope; and the assertion messages say why the colon and the period are refused. A\ndecision-log row records the same.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqBDWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgUgQAAHJ/Toz+8e4uCblTLusr26q\nbXv9lVyCDDvV661LvAhTSXNLT/i0t+PpppZUWdcFtV9CIoI2NYGaZvwTjtv5s2zk\njBq+KSSZ3DLSzq48XFkqAgh2C+FURSG1cTrYu6yiiD9wX4vT/RT42gZAhC+U7lKx\na1vqoVj2X6gPA6fY5zyIUDXteqEAJvUX3Jpl/c7Q4Cl1n7S5uPwiFo56ae1EwGnK\npaMztpbpK7GUhIDJIz8NqpNYVEHutrHqWuzynqj0QwUpRRXwQbwffMkpquWSWbTN\nw4SsQUq8JAdVXanPsQCrT82PIRdNlGGQMCoDXueGhnND93jL2tLiqg0BwSlAoHtJ\nkXbueesGb1ExZ5ytAt3+i1od77fECWdWOjjvMRinNzBTOdhTGCGv69t+nbEkTQ+C\noOeHGLFImjTOzWilECxTXPK+mmuc+VUpBXsCOWlHxcZ/RYjSe9KZOnn74kJP82pY\nPA17Tq5HxOSy/Vlauv7lcl5p+iDiWCCfeovDGkAnQhteQuldAWY+26rhKWWWGZ1i\nK3uNzOyYdqq7ZpsFJTf83SsUPIzcKWxBJepTvW9eb+vwCeY1WL8zbVMDaQ/bgCR6\nAW+i9KDofCZHQ35F8npWSw8XbDfL2U9WC8Ly56TSO/f7OceSU8UclrMw8pq1p9GL\ncxx/WxhSlRZyBmr05dug\n=yUnv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T15:20:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/c4b755783fe7d82e91abcc98733d497f7a0a54f2","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGM0Yjc1NTc4M2ZlN2Q4MmU5MWFiY2M5ODczM2Q0OTdmN2EwYTU0ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b","sha":"36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b"}],"sha":"c4b755783fe7d82e91abcc98733d497f7a0a54f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/c4b755783fe7d82e91abcc98733d497f7a0a54f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:03:26Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:03:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: the samples module says what to change when you copy it — workspace:* versus the published @jahia/formidable (#320)\n\n* docs: the samples module says what to change when you copy it — workspace:* here, the published @jahia/formidable in yours\n\nThe README of the samples module claimed it depended on the published package; its package.json\nsays workspace:*, which links the monorepo''s sources and resolves nothing outside this repository.\nThe README now opens with the one line to change when copying the module and why the sample does\nnot write the published version itself (a version range that matches the workspace still resolves\nto the workspace, only the npm: protocol forces the registry). The package README explains what\n\"inside this repository\" means, the extension guide points to it next to its yarn add, the\nhelp-text sample page too, and AGENTS.md / CONTEXT.md finally list packages/formidable,\nformidable-extended-inputs and the samples module.\n\n* docs: the copy command names no in-development version, the manifest lines that are ours are listed, both sample modules are named\n\nyarn add @jahia/formidable@0.5.0 fails until the release is cut (the package is not on the\nregistry yet) and dates the snippet at every release; the README now writes <release>. The\nsnapshot flag and the unversioned formidable-elements dependency are the sample''s own, not a\ncopier''s — said so, with the pin extended-inputs uses as the model. AGENTS.md and CONTEXT.md\nlisted three of the four test modules.\n\n* docs: the copying section''s heading matches its five lines, and the snapshot flag says what it does\n\nThe section grew from one line to change to five; the heading still promised one. The snapshot\nsentence asserted a semantic without a source: the JavaScript modules engine reads jahia.snapshot\nand suffixes the bundle version with .SNAPSHOT, which is what lets a build redeploy over the same\nversion (JavascriptProtocolConnection.getVersionWithSnapshotSuffix).","tree":{"sha":"e8cdb90bb051aa248e7de5d9f0e4bbcce3271185","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/e8cdb90bb051aa248e7de5d9f0e4bbcce3271185"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b","verification":{"payload":"tree e8cdb90bb051aa248e7de5d9f0e4bbcce3271185\nparent f10030abec41558b225a97c276a9f141830c425f\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789131806 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789131806 +0200\n\ndocs: the samples module says what to change when you copy it — workspace:* versus the published @jahia/formidable (#320)\n\n* docs: the samples module says what to change when you copy it — workspace:* here, the published @jahia/formidable in yours\n\nThe README of the samples module claimed it depended on the published package; its package.json\nsays workspace:*, which links the monorepo''s sources and resolves nothing outside this repository.\nThe README now opens with the one line to change when copying the module and why the sample does\nnot write the published version itself (a version range that matches the workspace still resolves\nto the workspace, only the npm: protocol forces the registry). The package README explains what\n\"inside this repository\" means, the extension guide points to it next to its yarn add, the\nhelp-text sample page too, and AGENTS.md / CONTEXT.md finally list packages/formidable,\nformidable-extended-inputs and the samples module.\n\n* docs: the copy command names no in-development version, the manifest lines that are ours are listed, both sample modules are named\n\nyarn add @jahia/formidable@0.5.0 fails until the release is cut (the package is not on the\nregistry yet) and dates the snippet at every release; the README now writes <release>. The\nsnapshot flag and the unversioned formidable-elements dependency are the sample''s own, not a\ncopier''s — said so, with the pin extended-inputs uses as the model. AGENTS.md and CONTEXT.md\nlisted three of the four test modules.\n\n* docs: the copying section''s heading matches its five lines, and the snapshot flag says what it does\n\nThe section grew from one line to change to five; the heading still promised one. The snapshot\nsentence asserted a semantic without a source: the JavaScript modules engine reads jahia.snapshot\nand suffixes the bundle version with .SNAPSHOT, which is what lets a build redeploy over the same\nversion (JavascriptProtocolConnection.getVersionWithSnapshotSuffix).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo/weCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi+MQAEZwJc6R35YbkfLEk0+Peixj\nSwHXCtDJZfWVKFVcppVSQiVwopfsKnUR+JPUThIXb+hz9I7eylB+T0bdCBEZZvCU\nR81iA+3PaLBQaicaXkMoprKMcOaXKjUlso8vDiNg6TiDKdrQyko3+MplGtfd5c3W\n+nwhZWJ0y1qSMjO90tNf41S3xnzD1vkkxZkwPi3pzCCta0lAcuYJu6cckidUMa2h\nYTnBC3n4G2triEq7qlLcRzxz771u1V1IJdPX+HpEDFTOQZHUjlbtWeQB2MrlU0sX\nocu50KUT0hacTVvvCiC1+o9HxsklvAjTiBZj/3bdiqWLVXSEC3YJJ7TpQkWW12me\nVBrfGAOgkfyq/NEGOuilTzXOgDmm4TeJpalyQWZTIbI5mCLU1qz3GbZb1E8CKrqU\nKCY+YtfPlz7t/kphRe0WWZMvfuuvz5X4vgF2LVeUlOuju/ngddN7bsXek3wRd2Ka\n9EcD7+3o0dOwSNNDCcnnRZarrSNyXz/8SHB4Vze/W8487kocaGI8xwqf9K/4ibeG\nv03lTIk3GxPBBj6jY3fAx76i8wieMJh+Ap5XUkFYv8C1rgEqJrEQ1xIbNlsJUqHj\nhDH57eIBoqSxFTYVGyfTepHFX0IyqoeQBO915YazQjvea8W/HJfbNTx2kJrVYb2u\nVwe1yOxTDg2Ee4EbzuCk\n=eNza\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T13:03:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDM2NzQ2Yzg4ZTQzMGEyNjM0MjQ4NzI4NjUyM2IwMTNkZjU5NzFmOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/f10030abec41558b225a97c276a9f141830c425f","sha":"f10030abec41558b225a97c276a9f141830c425f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/f10030abec41558b225a97c276a9f141830c425f"}],"sha":"36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/36746c88e430a26342487286523b013df5971f8b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/f10030abec41558b225a97c276a9f141830c425f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:57:59Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:57:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: the help block and the validation attributes of the npm package have unit tests (#323)\n\n* test: the help block and the validation attributes of the npm package have unit tests\n\nOnly the mask and its hook were tested. HelpText: nothing without a text, the div.fmdb-form-help\nwith the help-<nodeId> id and the rich text rendered as HTML, the decorative repeat without id and\nhidden from assistive technology. validationDataAttributes: every message prop to its\ndata-fmdb-msg-* attribute for the text and range shapes, no attribute for an absent prop, a blank\nmessage to an undefined attribute React omits, foreign props ignored.\n\n* test: the blank-message case asserts the key is present, not only that its value is undefined\n\ntoBeUndefined() also passes when the key is never emitted; the presence check pins the ''in''\nsemantic the case exists to show. Found by mutating the source: a truthiness check in\nvalidationDataAttributes left all 20 tests green.","tree":{"sha":"aea8d53d6005aae4ba27067e5fd7d1a59eceda76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/aea8d53d6005aae4ba27067e5fd7d1a59eceda76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/f10030abec41558b225a97c276a9f141830c425f","verification":{"payload":"tree aea8d53d6005aae4ba27067e5fd7d1a59eceda76\nparent d585260766b422960513055a534b223a65d130f4\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789131479 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789131479 +0200\n\ntest: the help block and the validation attributes of the npm package have unit tests (#323)\n\n* test: the help block and the validation attributes of the npm package have unit tests\n\nOnly the mask and its hook were tested. HelpText: nothing without a text, the div.fmdb-form-help\nwith the help-<nodeId> id and the rich text rendered as HTML, the decorative repeat without id and\nhidden from assistive technology. validationDataAttributes: every message prop to its\ndata-fmdb-msg-* attribute for the text and range shapes, no attribute for an absent prop, a blank\nmessage to an undefined attribute React omits, foreign props ignored.\n\n* test: the blank-message case asserts the key is present, not only that its value is undefined\n\ntoBeUndefined() also passes when the key is never emitted; the presence check pins the ''in''\nsemantic the case exists to show. Found by mutating the source: a truthiness check in\nvalidationDataAttributes left all 20 tests green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo/rXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk/sQAG+hIqJXa7I0dFkVnFSETJVq\nInnkUU6nBl36CNFSKBBXSwWF87EpXm8IUmCkTf7wsOaIWEhcCckQQEfh+RaKo8pa\nUoKr84ao9Nw2NOMPDnkfmfU2pHfvX6mTxyzC8b43Z24qvpq7b8pc/peIXX188+q4\nx0XDGR/loaxh8acjXFK+p1mqukf2/J2m1w6q20XjYxBReP1Yw8rEcqtr3VJXzFRF\ny8EFQgAeoPoPTkcURHWN7kU/ewsohN1PI7fqvpnbmzt2Ry2ddl5lct9+IksZjNb/\nlyF