mmits/f10030abec41558b225a97c276a9f141830c425f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/d585260766b422960513055a534b223a65d130f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:59:33Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:59:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: the 0.4 wave of startup migrations stays in 0.5.0, with the supported upgrade paths (#318)\n\n* docs: the 0.4 wave of startup migrations stays in 0.5.0, with the supported upgrade paths\n\nDecision of 2026-09-10 (HDU): the four startup migrations and the elements\nreactivation introduced in 0.4.x are kept through 0.5.x, so that a 0.3.x instance can\nupgrade to 0.5.0 directly, and leave in 0.6 together with the 0.5.0 wave. The upgrade\nnotes said the opposite (removed when 0.5.0 is cut, 0.4.x the minimum source), as did\nthe Lifecycle javadoc of the five classes and the two marker-mixin comments of the\nengine''s CND. The notes now open with the supported upgrade paths, stating which ones\nwere verified on a real instance (0.3.0 → 0.4.0, 0.4.0 → 0.5.0) and that 0.3.x → 0.5.0\ndirectly is expected by construction but not exercised yet. Comments and docs only,\nno behaviour change.\n\n* docs: the direct 0.3.x → 0.5.0 upgrade path is verified on a real 0.3.0 instance\n\nReplayed the documented reinstall procedure with the 0.5.0-SNAPSHOT artifacts of main (ad60100) on\na pristine 0.3.0 instance (three bilingual forms, divergent legacy option values, a 0.3-shaped\nlogic rule, seven stored submissions): both waves of startup migrations ran when the elements\ndeployed, in both workspaces, no property left prefixed, no live-owned property, forms render,\nhonest submissions pass and tampered ones are refused, a republished field reaches live, an engine\nrestart changes nothing. Each row of the supported upgrade paths now says when it was verified.\n\n* docs: the 0.6 precondition is that both migration waves ran, and the permanent site marker survives the migrations'' removal\n\nStarting the 0.5.x engine once was a weaker condition than the rename needs: elements 0.4.x\naccepts engine 0.5.x, so the 0.5.0 wave may never have run. The removal checklist treated the\ntwo marker mixins alike, but only fmdbmix:migratedChoiceOptions clears itself;\nfmdbmix:elementsReactivated stays on every healed site, and a dropped declaration is flagged\nby nothing at deploy time.\n\n* docs: the CND and the javadoc say what the upgrade notes conclude about the two marker mixins\n\nThe removal checklist now keeps fmdbmix:elementsReactivated declared after its code leaves, and drops\nfmdbmix:migratedChoiceOptions only once no field carries it; the comments next to the declarations —\nthe lines a developer reads while doing the 0.6 removal — still promised both would go with the\ncode. They state the same conclusion now and point at the notes.","tree":{"sha":"71ea3b31c34acf62f90e1fadfc2ffcb259c4a60c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/71ea3b31c34acf62f90e1fadfc2ffcb259c4a60c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/d585260766b422960513055a534b223a65d130f4","verification":{"payload":"tree 71ea3b31c34acf62f90e1fadfc2ffcb259c4a60c\nparent 73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789120773 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789120773 +0200\n\ndocs: the 0.4 wave of startup migrations stays in 0.5.0, with the supported upgrade paths (#318)\n\n* docs: the 0.4 wave of startup migrations stays in 0.5.0, with the supported upgrade paths\n\nDecision of 2026-09-10 (HDU): the four startup migrations and the elements\nreactivation introduced in 0.4.x are kept through 0.5.x, so that a 0.3.x instance can\nupgrade to 0.5.0 directly, and leave in 0.6 together with the 0.5.0 wave. The upgrade\nnotes said the opposite (removed when 0.5.0 is cut, 0.4.x the minimum source), as did\nthe Lifecycle javadoc of the five classes and the two marker-mixin comments of the\nengine''s CND. The notes now open with the supported upgrade paths, stating which ones\nwere verified on a real instance (0.3.0 → 0.4.0, 0.4.0 → 0.5.0) and that 0.3.x → 0.5.0\ndirectly is expected by construction but not exercised yet. Comments and docs only,\nno behaviour change.\n\n* docs: the direct 0.3.x → 0.5.0 upgrade path is verified on a real 0.3.0 instance\n\nReplayed the documented reinstall procedure with the 0.5.0-SNAPSHOT artifacts of main (ad60100) on\na pristine 0.3.0 instance (three bilingual forms, divergent legacy option values, a 0.3-shaped\nlogic rule, seven stored submissions): both waves of startup migrations ran when the elements\ndeployed, in both workspaces, no property left prefixed, no live-owned property, forms render,\nhonest submissions pass and tampered ones are refused, a republished field reaches live, an engine\nrestart changes nothing. Each row of the supported upgrade paths now says when it was verified.\n\n* docs: the 0.6 precondition is that both migration waves ran, and the permanent site marker survives the migrations'' removal\n\nStarting the 0.5.x engine once was a weaker condition than the rename needs: elements 0.4.x\naccepts engine 0.5.x, so the 0.5.0 wave may never have run. The removal checklist treated the\ntwo marker mixins alike, but only fmdbmix:migratedChoiceOptions clears itself;\nfmdbmix:elementsReactivated stays on every healed site, and a dropped declaration is flagged\nby nothing at deploy time.\n\n* docs: the CND and the javadoc say what the upgrade notes conclude about the two marker mixins\n\nThe removal checklist now keeps fmdbmix:elementsReactivated declared after its code leaves, and drops\nfmdbmix:migratedChoiceOptions only once no field carries it; the comments next to the declarations —\nthe lines a developer reads while doing the 0.6 removal — still promised both would go with the\ncode. They state the same conclusion now and point at the notes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo9EFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ3IQAC9u4gdYCB0h2ZU1k3IRyMTH\nBi+cGpX9salgLDeaU5jM7Lz21XHHuZ8PVaebHcEF3jW1nfBRZ+m054sTbRZH1oWu\n9nGzNS/wVf/KI43VC4PaSWtrhY754gEZyVck5LubiTldBhuTY9wttCIpqf5IyewY\noxDCDHE89wRIBS0R4aqi1bYxX9v5azdvp9H6VRKav7XRLfcNWdpV1uMPBYk2N3Ws\n3yB48ew3FR3AnfZ/R9/3S9qPcZZ+Iy4A6I7VjJBDMiKT4qMxOIsjEQHnP860DNHF\nQpo008LCGupXwIGzb8s1VbH1E5HnS9MLIt6mG70RMns7cLIratdW15qg/Ga5YlUJ\nrrBVCjcvskgDFDmVkST2PvYaf4Hpg147mvLmHm6xUtDeKk+q2rQkYcgbyi4pjNI4\nAySzK8lwGph8XVSulGIEal1OHGqlEquDkVvPqJe6T38SCnIOxse0ijqArattNJQI\nS6vMhMsrcWtqQ7fDETfPp8ZcBBpEZbVgeV09KFG3V3LzgDugM8QE3A0jjDJqcLvt\n5cmC0xzJY90rA7DbSm8ZS5xIFWK9Fj0Pk64mWfxrU42kYooyEXcf9NuiW0GFfJeV\nu5D1ReePal6E7sgdWdlTzUPDqUjal5xfOzVCMekTBKiICmEPrtARCcwcEooEdt1l\nY/BTgBUVbFoKG+YzHdmU\n=vQKK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T09:59:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/d585260766b422960513055a534b223a65d130f4","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGQ1ODUyNjA3NjZiNDIyOTYwNTEzMDU1YTUzNGIyMjNhNjVkMTMwZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265","sha":"73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265"}],"sha":"d585260766b422960513055a534b223a65d130f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/d585260766b422960513055a534b223a65d130f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:59:03Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:59:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: publish the npm package as @jahia/formidable-library (#321)\n\n* refactor: publish the npm package as @jahia/formidable-library\n\nThree things are already called formidable — the repository, the root Maven artifact and the\nengine module; the published package now follows @jahia/javascript-modules-library instead of\nclaiming the bare name. Nothing is on the registry yet, so no consumer breaks. The folder\npackages/formidable and the Maven artifactId formidable-npm are unchanged.\n\nThe smoke script reads the package name from the manifest: its unpack path was hardcoded, so the\nprobe resolved the renamed import to the workspace sources — the failure this rename surfaced.\n\n* ci: the static analysis fails on any reference to the pre-rename package name\n\nThe rename is complete at this head, but nothing kept it so: a branch opened before it — #320 is\none — merges the old name back into AGENTS.md, CONTEXT.md or a README without a conflict, every\ncheck stays green, and the documentation points at a package that never exists on the registry.\nThe gate greps the tracked files, yarn.lock included, next to the smoke step.\n\n* ci: the name guard tells a failed search from an empty one\n\ngit grep exits 128 when it cannot search — a broken pattern is enough — and an if-statement takes\nthat for \"nothing found\": the guard went green on a tree it never read. The three exit codes are\nnow told apart, the way on-release.yml already separates the registry''s answers.","tree":{"sha":"de7f488624ec1ca5c162b9944ea30fcf06a05756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/de7f488624ec1ca5c162b9944ea30fcf06a05756"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265","verification":{"payload":"tree de7f488624ec1ca5c162b9944ea30fcf06a05756\nparent 4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789120743 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789120743 +0200\n\nrefactor: publish the npm package as @jahia/formidable-library (#321)\n\n* refactor: publish the npm package as @jahia/formidable-library\n\nThree things are already called formidable — the repository, the root Maven artifact and the\nengine module; the published package now follows @jahia/javascript-modules-library instead of\nclaiming the bare name. Nothing is on the registry yet, so no consumer breaks. The folder\npackages/formidable and the Maven artifactId formidable-npm are unchanged.\n\nThe smoke script reads the package name from the manifest: its unpack path was hardcoded, so the\nprobe resolved the renamed import to the workspace sources — the failure this rename surfaced.\n\n* ci: the static analysis fails on any reference to the pre-rename package name\n\nThe rename is complete at this head, but nothing kept it so: a branch opened before it — #320 is\none — merges the old name back into AGENTS.md, CONTEXT.md or a README without a conflict, every\ncheck stays green, and the documentation points at a package that never exists on the registry.\nThe gate greps the tracked files, yarn.lock included, next to the smoke step.\n\n* ci: the name guard tells a failed search from an empty one\n\ngit grep exits 128 when it cannot search — a broken pattern is enough — and an if-statement takes\nthat for \"nothing found\": the guard went green on a tree it never read. The three exit codes are\nnow told apart, the way on-release.yml already separates the registry''s answers.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo9DnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWr8QAKiPLd0pzRLtoqvIfB0TaqHx\nke9KQEtR1OTomtUR9axAeqQvwscfnSimOnuBcCQQc+L76FFnLTF4heCVfukrEnAe\njBFjfwk0Erv9j8x71RB2bszF5yGvD+D4JCnix2HtZx7CBdIk2VArUE7emiz7xSLs\nZeUutPcimi1xoYaQcZ6aL/eUx7AiEDSFcLLybgY1gMEx+7swm54KdcBZJhvwEnlg\nDdfpaK6LMLn5HVmebWzcC7pHzb2Wr52oeDrQ8Onh43tDgPu5U/tmkraSHITTZElL\nzN2abvhDdWFv2uYiQQMZTQcFEDGDjNYGfO/M2IPV9oRo7sAaphVJgJtxoy0f7wYT\n/Nmx0hzawTsfn2jmGPK+WSYo1MN2wajcgRCjgDPd9E6ZV96I5qsTZCatqpbn1dIc\nCQFIfr51NG/NPRKKT2UhbSluy4G38IFtY3EplHRjU1nwkeuiHS7OmHBLOqNW66Sm\nbvSiiY3e9HHQtLGZSc6lpVAbsz+OGOdCFqk1g2JwT5rSwtBvnTjBugQUs3di64Nw\nSrdZ2T7MK6N67/JNBkWVkv184VLFEC4VxtJekIClzJ85UfdREyxSQQwsRoeKbsI2\nUT+QGUsFNe9vvBrl8RL2dm7s70Klpl+0C9SHB1yi64bxS5hELnXBQhlix8zo4Uo3\n51z25itLWPVlGWfuqcKW\n=7GpX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T09:59:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDczZjQxYTY2MWExNjBmZGRmMTdiMzRlNWNlYzRlOTI1Mzc4YTcyNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a","sha":"4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a"}],"sha":"73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/73f41a661a160fddf17b34e5cec4e925378a7265"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:29:19Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:29:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: the submission flow follows the code on the CAPTCHA field, the scope check and the action types (#322)\n\n* docs: the submission flow follows the code on the CAPTCHA field, the scope check and the action types\n\nThe CAPTCHA section listed three hardcoded widget fields: the field has been the configured\ncaptchaTokenField since the provider keys moved to the .cfg, and the key list named four\nshorthand keys instead of the eight real ones. Gate 0 named a method that does not exist\n(checkSecurityFilter): the check is FormSubmitServlet''s PermissionService call on the\nformidable-submit scope. The step-12 diagram showed two of the four action types.\n\n* docs: the CAPTCHA connect timeout is also the client''s wait budget for the widget, and the filter hands five attributes to the view\n\ncaptchaHttpConnectTimeoutSeconds reaches the browser as formidable.captcha.widgetTimeoutSeconds:\nCaptcha.client.tsx polls for window.<widgetVar> until that deadline, so lowering it to tighten the\nverify call also shortens how long the page waits for the provider script. The paragraph also\nsaid the filter hands two attributes; it hands the site key, the script URL, both provider names\nand that budget.","tree":{"sha":"ac69112294a7eef7ce2ff3acd66c8c27f6e3f7c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/ac69112294a7eef7ce2ff3acd66c8c27f6e3f7c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a","verification":{"payload":"tree ac69112294a7eef7ce2ff3acd66c8c27f6e3f7c7\nparent ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789118959 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789118959 +0200\n\ndocs: the submission flow follows the code on the CAPTCHA field, the scope check and the action types (#322)\n\n* docs: the submission flow follows the code on the CAPTCHA field, the scope check and the action types\n\nThe CAPTCHA section listed three hardcoded widget fields: the field has been the configured\ncaptchaTokenField since the provider keys moved to the .cfg, and the key list named four\nshorthand keys instead of the eight real ones. Gate 0 named a method that does not exist\n(checkSecurityFilter): the check is FormSubmitServlet''s PermissionService call on the\nformidable-submit scope. The step-12 diagram showed two of the four action types.\n\n* docs: the CAPTCHA connect timeout is also the client''s wait budget for the widget, and the filter hands five attributes to the view\n\ncaptchaHttpConnectTimeoutSeconds reaches the browser as formidable.captcha.widgetTimeoutSeconds:\nCaptcha.client.tsx polls for window.<widgetVar> until that deadline, so lowering it to tighten the\nverify call also shortens how long the page waits for the provider script. The paragraph also\nsaid the filter hands two attributes; it hands the site key, the script URL, both provider names\nand that budget.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo8nvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdyYQAB1XmGUJwxouioTmLYaXFQKd\nESotz+DJgK9aFM6PB6KsMBvvWnoLc8mgpp1A68te9iJzkRFhgiUyP4Fv+8AFJdGk\nKcXsyQ55sUvevJImD7xIlumtprUgABu5+aTudmtVrPQRwLOQR6/xduXxq+AWktF4\nXW5UP3kHkTjSWwFZhGBaYt3oWq5O6ogiN1NUl6/B70deJ8TxClN48oQvmlratRzt\nUicPChWUEopVDkGbFgve+WKQG8MEVKp70Xrw+mIWyWoG8xMMFIIMXt8EYHZ0QLiO\ncofP3HimkeowxkfP6EIynyjuy/qmfwobwhkccp0nETbLqKTvLk3PQgmhSfRJQvXn\nWriPoUt3zXCTdoYCEUdoT/MezOi5Lk9LZ5x1Xxk0K+7nkElrPbuHPFfLNKXCSgn3\nYNXQsSh+dYTYvg/a4WA9aOU9/MTvBCq5Z+OvaM8PBkhwEoRsYW20yyJVrEQXG7Hy\nfFISVsd4YrENiLvrAfJ1IOcQD2fLYwczdgewSIZs8yVZs0DNK/ufdKOD+EpTb7GG\n90pFwZjeBlyfliueIYyPbcKcSB6wwOq8BWS/QP6Eha3THAikY17UUvsMurYaxJMr\nrc2/azXhrERvlKtmoQB8wLre9GtMDeDGNsWYo/fIBU0aGDkNmxfEjc+Voz+DEb7o\n6odVmxOkKhZpzgyXJZ2E\n=Uo1g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T09:29:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDRkY2E5YTYxZGJjMTVkNzQ0YTZlYTU3ZDU0ZDZmMGE5YzZiOWJjOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8","sha":"ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8"}],"sha":"4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/4dca9a61dbc15d744a6ea57d54d6f0a9c6b9bc8a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:01:33Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:01:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: publish the form contract and input mask as @jahia/formidable (#317)\n\n* feat: @jahia/formidable-library — the form contract and the input mask, published on npm for modules outside the monorepo\n\nThe private formidable-shared workspace package becomes @jahia/formidable-library:\nbuilt with tsc to dist/ (ESM + types), versioned with the release through a reactor\npom (sync-version), published by a publish-npm job of on-release.yml with npm trusted\npublishing (OIDC, provenance, no token). The mask utilities and the useMask hook move\nfrom formidable-elements into the package, so a module outside the monorepo gets the\nlive mask too. The samples module depends on the package like any third-party module\nwould: its text-input view imports the contract instead of copying it and gains a\nmasked island. Docs stop telling third parties to copy the markup. Closes #308.\n\n* chore: changelog entry for #317\n\n* fix: the library declares eslint and prettier, so its lint script never falls back to a global binary\n\nIn the Maven build container, yarn lint of the library picked the image''s global\nESLint 6.4.0 (\"couldn''t find a configuration file\"): the package declared no eslint\ndevDependency, unlike the modules, so yarn had no binary of its own to run.\n\n* ci: the npm package check runs before the doc-link check, so it reports while the latter is red on main (#316)\n\n* refactor: the package is @jahia/formidable — shorter, folder packages/formidable, Maven artifact formidable-npm\n\nRenamed from @jahia/formidable-library on review: the scope already says Jahia, the\nname only has to say Formidable. Nothing else changes.\n\n* fix: the package imports under Node ESM and its tarball is proven before publishing\n\nReview of #317. The build now runs under nodenext, so an extensionless specifier is a\nbuild error rather than something an external consumer discovers (the specifiers\nthemselves carry .js in the sources). Source maps inline their sources, since the\ntarball ships dist/ only. scripts/smoke.mjs packs the tarball, unpacks it under a\nscratch node_modules and imports the package by name through its exports map — the\ncheck the CI step and the pom run instead of a file listing. The release job replaces\n--tolerate-republish with a guard: an identical tarball already on npm is a no-op, a\ndifferent one under the same version fails the job. The manifest points the workspace\nat the sources (publishConfig.exports keeps dist/ for the tarball), and the package\ngets the .editorconfig its sources were written under.\n\n* refactor: the public API is the contract — help text (with its decorative repeat), validation attributes, maskToPattern, applyMask, useMask\n\nReview of #317. The mask tokens, the raw-value and caret arithmetic and the\ntrailing-literal option stay inside the package: applyMask(value, mask) is the public\nentry point, formatWithMask the internal one the hook uses on deletions. HelpText gains\na decorative flag (no id, aria-hidden) so the sample no longer hand-writes the help\nmarkup for its repeat. The hook gets a jsdom test on the caret arithmetic: typing at\nthe end, editing in the middle, deleting a trailing literal. README names handleInput.\n\n* chore: one @types/react@19 hoisted at the root, no build step in the consumers, changelog entry renamed\n\nReview of #317. The root declares @types/react@19 so the package and its workspace\nconsumers share one physical copy (the engine keeps its nested 18); the consumers''\nbuild scripts drop the package build, since the workspace reads its sources; the\nchangelog entry takes the PR number in its name and spends its second sentence on the\npackage name and the install line.\n\n* fix: the smoke check proves the declarations too, the caret test discriminates its branches, no dangling declaration maps, @types/react-dom in step with @types/react\n\nSecond review of #317. scripts/smoke.mjs checks that every exports target of the packed\nmanifest exists (a consumer''s TypeScript would silently fall back from a dangling types\ntarget) and type-checks a nodenext consumer of the unpacked tarball with skipLibCheck\noff, so a missing .d.ts behind a re-export fails the step — both mutations verified red.\nThe trailing-literal test asserts the caret at 4, where the raw count alone would say 3.\ndeclarationMap is dropped: the tarball ships no src/ for it to point at (the JS maps\ninline their sources). @types/react-dom is held at ~19.2, whose peer matches the hoisted\n@types/react 19.2 — the YN0060 warning is gone.\n\n* fix: the publish step tells a registry failure from an unpublished version and guards its hash; the package type-checks its tests; .editorconfig covers .mjs\n\nThird review of #317. The publish step fails when the local tarball could not be hashed,\nbranches on npm''s E404 rather than on an empty output (a failed lookup is an error, not\n\"not published yet\"), and keeps --tolerate-republish as a belt for a retry racing the check\n— each branch exercised locally (real E404, unreachable registry, existing version with\ndifferent and with identical content). A typecheck script runs tsc on tsconfig.json, tests\nincluded, from the pom (process-sources) — the build excludes them, nothing else read\nthem. The .editorconfig glob gains mjs, so prettier keeps the tabs of scripts/smoke.mjs.","tree":{"sha":"f43919ec100211339f63c2d3974c39bd4d4773a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/f43919ec100211339f63c2d3974c39bd4d4773a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8","verification":{"payload":"tree f43919ec100211339f63c2d3974c39bd4d4773a6\nparent 3d04fae284d907fcd96e0149c37ee8c73e1df360\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789052493 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789052493 +0200\n\nfeat: publish the form contract and input mask as @jahia/formidable (#317)\n\n* feat: @jahia/formidable-library — the form contract and the input mask, published on npm for modules outside the monorepo\n\nThe private formidable-shared workspace package becomes @jahia/formidable-library:\nbuilt with tsc to dist/ (ESM + types), versioned with the release through a reactor\npom (sync-version), published by a publish-npm job of on-release.yml with npm trusted\npublishing (OIDC, provenance, no token). The mask utilities and the useMask hook move\nfrom formidable-elements into the package, so a module outside the monorepo gets the\nlive mask too. The samples module depends on the package like any third-party module\nwould: its text-input view imports the contract instead of copying it and gains a\nmasked island. Docs stop telling third parties to copy the markup. Closes #308.\n\n* chore: changelog entry for #317\n\n* fix: the library declares eslint and prettier, so its lint script never falls back to a global binary\n\nIn the Maven build container, yarn lint of the library picked the image''s global\nESLint 6.4.0 (\"couldn''t find a configuration file\"): the package declared no eslint\ndevDependency, unlike the modules, so yarn had no binary of its own to run.\n\n* ci: the npm package check runs before the doc-link check, so it reports while the latter is red on main (#316)\n\n* refactor: the package is @jahia/formidable — shorter, folder packages/formidable, Maven artifact formidable-npm\n\nRenamed from @jahia/formidable-library on review: the scope already says Jahia, the\nname only has to say Formidable. Nothing else changes.\n\n* fix: the package imports under Node ESM and its tarball is proven before publishing\n\nReview of #317. The build now runs under nodenext, so an extensionless specifier is a\nbuild error rather than something an external consumer discovers (the specifiers\nthemselves carry .js in the sources). Source maps inline their sources, since the\ntarball ships dist/ only. scripts/smoke.mjs packs the tarball, unpacks it under a\nscratch node_modules and imports the package by name through its exports map — the\ncheck the CI step and the pom run instead of a file listing. The release job replaces\n--tolerate-republish with a guard: an identical tarball already on npm is a no-op, a\ndifferent one under the same version fails the job. The manifest points the workspace\nat the sources (publishConfig.exports keeps dist/ for the tarball), and the package\ngets the .editorconfig its sources were written under.\n\n* refactor: the public API is the contract — help text (with its decorative repeat), validation attributes, maskToPattern, applyMask, useMask\n\nReview of #317. The mask tokens, the raw-value and caret arithmetic and the\ntrailing-literal option stay inside the package: applyMask(value, mask) is the public\nentry point, formatWithMask the internal one the hook uses on deletions. HelpText gains\na decorative flag (no id, aria-hidden) so the sample no longer hand-writes the help\nmarkup for its repeat. The hook gets a jsdom test on the caret arithmetic: typing at\nthe end, editing in the middle, deleting a trailing literal. README names handleInput.\n\n* chore: one @types/react@19 hoisted at the root, no build step in the consumers, changelog entry renamed\n\nReview of #317. The root declares @types/react@19 so the package and its workspace\nconsumers share one physical copy (the engine keeps its nested 18); the consumers''\nbuild scripts drop the package build, since the workspace reads its sources; the\nchangelog entry takes the PR number in its name and spends its second sentence on the\npackage name and the install line.\n\n* fix: the smoke check proves the declarations too, the caret test discriminates its branches, no dangling declaration maps, @types/react-dom in step with @types/react\n\nSecond review of #317. scripts/smoke.mjs checks that every exports target of the packed\nmanifest exists (a consumer''s TypeScript would silently fall back from a dangling types\ntarget) and type-checks a nodenext consumer of the unpacked tarball with skipLibCheck\noff, so a missing .d.ts behind a re-export fails the step — both mutations verified red.\nThe trailing-literal test asserts the caret at 4, where the raw count alone would say 3.\ndeclarationMap is dropped: the tarball ships no src/ for it to point at (the JS maps\ninline their sources). @types/react-dom is held at ~19.2, whose peer matches the hoisted\n@types/react 19.2 — the YN0060 warning is gone.\n\n* fix: the publish step tells a registry failure from an unpublished version and guards its hash; the package type-checks its tests; .editorconfig covers .mjs\n\nThird review of #317. The publish step fails when the local tarball could not be hashed,\nbranches on npm''s E404 rather than on an empty output (a failed lookup is an error, not\n\"not published yet\"), and keeps --tolerate-republish as a belt for a retry racing the check\n— each branch exercised locally (real E404, unreachable registry, existing version with\ndifferent and with identical content). A typecheck script runs tsc on tsconfig.json, tests\nincluded, from the pom (process-sources) — the build excludes them, nothing else read\nthem. The .editorconfig glob gains mjs, so prettier keeps the tabs of scripts/smoke.mjs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqosZNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3gMQADZNYViCGi57AXbwc2AF/AxT\nH6vQVwbFH+6xKIz2MrTT/B9GO721AGA9y2d23RDWsA2F0L3q+sfioRP59l96202M\nLkOQTygx10OUa1sRRfdbRHGsOIrh6/SHCMzT8ATr27OT2Uwm/dz6Vub9m7ONNb4m\nA6/5D+lKDiNadq/j8Zchai13hBup3zWQbmxKBq5fj0IQIYD2HlFda448mP69Xgoy\nu62XrYsYpKRihemGQL3MKd0NtLvoYHxf418DZfVNUZkdEsWAMBJg1MJ4IHCYH3w6\nT5zwm1T4oo5XYfTpZGfBGKuQoxvIYr76QqmTJ8rkk8Y2MNdfjDaqQrScbEkz2UtX\ndd2SjZCXeBTnqTZh7OVYUwbQil3Mrb9jIIogxYPsm/Ek+Akf3mNzZGukHhXsWDpN\nRvEblSkYV58yefXMlnIdikpc09INk+xNoAIYf299SQ+IiTphyTXUN1p2ZmtC3W2X\nSRQaydIrWAgeaONDQMj76P8u5ZqdxjO1vlcUxX+Wf5+pl8f6XBx0sK5Bfn2/YWMb\nnZOs+lpkhnTxlCMCXWrT2WpFOwRJOd64Fh5qZJO+DKedxMOZj7M2ka0Bx+YKzTjD\n9ILnjHpb+4wioM9SFpcDUk4YQQkTYCikiS+YjIkWykNsVecjMhhxru4yCRlWZWHf\nI91hch8zMVFmMLJklS/L\n=WPgW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T15:01:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGFkNjAxMDBkNjM2YmMxMDQ5ODdhMTRmNTc5NzQwZTJhMTc4NzQ2Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/3d04fae284d907fcd96e0149c37ee8c73e1df360","sha":"3d04fae284d907fcd96e0149c37ee8c73e1df360","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/3d04fae284d907fcd96e0149c37ee8c73e1df360"}],"sha":"ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/ad60100d636bc104987a14f579740e2a178746b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/3d04fae284d907fcd96e0149c37ee8c73e1df360/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:01:11Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:01:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: the mixin properties lose their fmdb: prefix, with a migration for 0.4.0 content (#312)\n\n* fix: the mixin properties lose their fmdb: prefix, with a migration for 0.4.0 content\n\nThe options-source and date-bounds mixins carried the only prefixed\nproperties of the model (fmdb:optionsMode, fmdb:options, fmdb:optionsSourceKey,\nfmdb:optionsRootCategory, fmdb:optionsRootNode, fmdb:optionsNodeType,\nfmdb:minBoundMode, fmdb:maxBoundMode, fmdb:min/maxRelativeAmount,\nfmdb:min/maxRelativeUnit) while fieldKey, logics, msg*, min and max never had\none (#310). They are renamed everywhere — CND, Java, views, Content Editor\noverrides, label keys, locale keys, Cypress fixtures, docs.\n\nMixinPropertyNamesMigration renames the properties of fields stored by 0.4.0\nin both workspaces at startup and on an elements redeploy, translations\nincluded; the twelve old definitions stay in the CND for one release, hidden,\nso a 0.4 export imported later is still accepted and migrated.\nChoiceOptionsContentMigration follows: the unified property now bears the\nlegacy select name, so a 0.3 select keeps its values in place and only gains\nthe mixin, the mode and a multi-valued shape.\n\nThe disabled fmdb_inputText.json override is removed.\n\n* test: the prefixed properties of a 0.4.0 field are renamed at startup, live follows — with the upgrade note\n\nSpec validation/48 produces the 0.4.0 shape through the deprecated hidden\ndefinitions (prefixMixinProperties.groovy), restarts the engine, and checks\nboth workspaces: modes, offset, fixed max and translated options back under\ntheir unprefixed names, the prefixed ones gone, nothing live-owned, and a\nlater edit + publication reaching live. docs/administration/upgrade-notes.md\ngets the 0.4.x → 0.5.0 section (who is affected, what the migration does,\nthe restart after importing a 0.4 export, how to check, what to change in\nyour own code) and the migration''s row; cnd-module-ownership.md states the\nnaming rule so the prefix does not come back. Changelog entry, breaking.\n\n* test: spec 219 checks the legacy residue on the radio — the select''s ''options'' is the unified property since #310\n\nThe first CI run of #312 failed spec 219 on the residue check: it asserted that\n''options'' had left the select''s translation node, while the migration now keeps a\n0.3 select''s values in place under that very name (normalised, mixin and mode\nstamped). The moved property is the radio''s ''choices'': that is where nothing may\nremain.\n\n* refactor: the migrations share one both-workspaces loop, the choice fixtures one node builder (Sonar duplication)\n\nThe Sonar quality gate flagged 4% duplicated new code: MixinPropertyNamesMigration\nrepeated the default-then-live loop of ListTitlesContentMigration and\nChoiceOptionsContentMigration, and the three sourced-choice fixture builders\nrepeated the same node assembly. The loop moves to\nElementsRedeployRetriggeredMigration.migrateBothWorkspaces(WorkspacePass); the\nfixtures share getChoiceFieldNode. Behaviour unchanged, 26 migration unit tests\ngreen.\n\n* style: plain shorthand for the destructured unprefixed properties (Sonar S6650)\n\nDropping the fmdb: prefix left thirteen `\"minBoundMode\": minBoundMode`-style\nrenames to the same name in the Date, DatetimeLocal and Select views, the only\nnew maintainability issues Sonar reported on the PR.\n\n* fix: a 0.4.0 export imports again — the JCR-level mandatory of the six renamed properties is lifted for 0.5, the editor keeps requiring them\n\nReview of #312. A node that carries only the prefixed 0.4 value of optionsSourceKey,\noptionsNodeType or a relative offset could not be saved: the mandatory check of the new\nname runs on every save, import included, so the migration could never reach those\nfields (the CI fixture died on it). The flag comes off those six definitions for this\nrelease and moves to the editor''s fieldset overrides (mandatory: true), so contributors\nstill cannot save an offset without its amount and unit. It comes back in 0.6 with the\nremoval of the deprecated definitions.\n\n* fix: the migrations never move content backwards — leftover manual lists, values already renamed, migration-write mark, getI18Ns, logs after save\n\nReview of #312. ChoiceOptionsContentMigration reads ''options'' on the translations as\n0.3 storage only when the field carries none of the four options-mode mixins: a select\nswitched from a manual list to a source keeps the list the editor left behind, and was\npushed back to manual at every activation. MixinPropertyNamesMigration keeps a value\nalready present under the unprefixed name (a 0.4 import edited before the restart) and\nonly drops the prefixed one; it also renames the select''s fmdb:optionsEmptyLabel. Both\nwalk the translations with getI18Ns(). The migration-write mark the language sync\nconsults moves to MigrationWrites and is set by migrateBothWorkspaces around every pass,\nso no migration writing i18n options has to remember it. The per-node INFO is logged\nafter the save, and a workspace whose nodes all failed says so instead of ''nothing\nfound''. Unit tests: the thirteen names, a weakreference kept as is, both names present,\na switched select left alone.\n\n* refactor: the select''s empty-option label loses its prefix too — the thirteenth and last prefixed property\n\nReview of #312: with fmdb:optionsEmptyLabel left aside, ''a property is never namespaced''\nwas false the moment it was written. Renamed like the twelve others: definition, view,\neditor form, label keys in the four bundles, fixtures, the 0.4-shape Groovy fixture; the\n0.4 spelling stays as a hidden definition for this release and the startup migration\nrenames it on the translation nodes.\n\n* test: spec 48 proves the date field''s migration, the French list and the empty label; spec 219 pins a select switched to a source\n\nReview of #312. The 0.4-shape fixture''s report is asserted (a script error no longer\npasses as a log line), the date field gets the same pre-migration guard as the select,\nthe gate waits for the last renamed state (the date field in live), and the select\ncarries a French option list and an empty-option label through the migration. Spec 219\nswitches a manual select to a source, restarts the engine and checks the mode held.\n\n* docs: startup migrations in two waves, the historical sections keep their release''s spelling, the changelog names no class\n\nReview of #312. The 0.3→0.4 sections describe fmdb:options and fmdb:minBoundMode again,\nwith a pointer to the 0.5.0 rename; the startup-migrations section no longer promises\nthe removal in 0.5 of a migration that ships in 0.5; the thirteenth property and the\nlifted mandatory are documented; the changelog quotes the log line without its class\nprefix.\n\n* fix: the 0.4.0 → 0.5 upgrade deploys and migrates on a real instance — pickers without JCR mandatory, quiet engine-first run, no stamp over a 0.4 mode\n\nTested on a real 0.4.0 instance (Docker, release artifacts, the 0.4.0 playground, both\nworkspaces, both languages):\n\n- Jahia''s DefinitionsBundleChecker refused the engine 0.5 jar: a mandatory property added\n  to a deployed type (optionsRootCategory, optionsRootNode) is a MAJOR change and cancels\n  the deployment. The two pickers lose the JCR-level mandatory for 0.5 like the six other\n  renamed settings; the editor fieldset overrides carry the requirement.\n- Engine upgraded first, the activation run failed on every field (\"Couldn''t find\n  definition for property\"): the element types keep their cached definitions until the\n  elements module is redeployed. MixinPropertyNamesMigration now checks\n  getApplicablePropertyDefinition and leaves such nodes to the redeploy rerun with one\n  INFO line per workspace instead of a stack trace per node.\n- DateBoundsContentMigration ran before the rename at the redeploy and stamped ''date'' on\n  0.4 fields whose mode sat under fmdb:minBoundMode; the stamp then won over the 0.4\n  value. A field carrying a prefixed mode has a mode: it is left to the rename migration.\n\nAfter the fixes: engine-first run = two INFO lines, elements redeploy = 17 + 17 fields\nrenamed, the field dump is identical to the 0.4.0 one modulo the rename of 78 properties,\nnothing live-owned, a republish reaches live, and a 0.4.0 export imports then migrates at\nthe next engine start.\n\n* refactor: the rename migration in small methods — one outcome per node, one summary, one rename pass per owner (Sonar S3776, S135)\n\n* test: the fixture check reads the provisioning status, the leftover list is read on the translation node\n\nThird review of #312. cy.executeGroovy yields the provisioning status (''.installed'' /\n''.failed''), never the script''s report: spec 48 asserts the status and leaves the shape to\nits pre-migration guards. Spec 219 reads the leftover manual list on j:translation_en,\nthe only place it is still readable once the field''s types no longer declare ''options''.\n\n* test: spec 48 publishes both languages, spec 219 plants the leftover list it asserts\n\nThe French list only reaches live when fr is published: the fixture now publishes en and\nfr, so the LIVE assertion on the French options holds. Removing fmdbmix:manualOptions\nclears the translated ''options'' with it (verified on a 0.5 instance through the same\nGraphQL mutation the editor sends), so a mode switch leaves no leftover; spec 219 plants\none the way an import or a script would, then checks the restart leaves it — and the\nmode — alone.","tree":{"sha":"a39277dcb0afaaa33bb2897b041d0b928880250d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/a39277dcb0afaaa33bb2897b041d0b928880250d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/3d04fae284d907fcd96e0149c37ee8c73e1df360","verification":{"payload":"tree a39277dcb0afaaa33bb2897b041d0b928880250d\nparent f34d7a1b19414a226ba26922c62299a4f3973e79\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1789052471 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789052471 +0200\n\nfix: the mixin properties lose their fmdb: prefix, with a migration fo