e legacy residue on the radio — the select''s ''options'' is the unified property since #310\n\nThe first CI run of #312 failed spec 219 on the residue check: it asserted that\n''options'' had left the select''s translation node, while the migration now keeps a\n0.3 select''s values in place under that very name (normalised, mixin and mode\nstamped). The moved property is the radio''s ''choices'': that is where nothing may\nremain.\n\n* refactor: the migrations share one both-workspaces loop, the choice fixtures one node builder (Sonar duplication)\n\nThe Sonar quality gate flagged 4% duplicated new code: MixinPropertyNamesMigration\nrepeated the default-then-live loop of ListTitlesContentMigration and\nChoiceOptionsContentMigration, and the three sourced-choice fixture builders\nrepeated the same node assembly. The loop moves to\nElementsRedeployRetriggeredMigration.migrateBothWorkspaces(WorkspacePass); the\nfixtures share getChoiceFieldNode. Behaviour unchanged, 26 migration unit tests\ngreen.\n\n* style: plain shorthand for the destructured unprefixed properties (Sonar S6650)\n\nDropping the fmdb: prefix left thirteen `\"minBoundMode\": minBoundMode`-style\nrenames to the same name in the Date, DatetimeLocal and Select views, the only\nnew maintainability issues Sonar reported on the PR.\n\n* fix: a 0.4.0 export imports again — the JCR-level mandatory of the six renamed properties is lifted for 0.5, the editor keeps requiring them\n\nReview of #312. A node that carries only the prefixed 0.4 value of optionsSourceKey,\noptionsNodeType or a relative offset could not be saved: the mandatory check of the new\nname runs on every save, import included, so the migration could never reach those\nfields (the CI fixture died on it). The flag comes off those six definitions for this\nrelease and moves to the editor''s fieldset overrides (mandatory: true), so contributors\nstill cannot save an offset without its amount and unit. It comes back in 0.6 with the\nremoval of the deprecated definitions.\n\n* fix: the migrations never move content backwards — leftover manual lists, values already renamed, migration-write mark, getI18Ns, logs after save\n\nReview of #312. ChoiceOptionsContentMigration reads ''options'' on the translations as\n0.3 storage only when the field carries none of the four options-mode mixins: a select\nswitched from a manual list to a source keeps the list the editor left behind, and was\npushed back to manual at every activation. MixinPropertyNamesMigration keeps a value\nalready present under the unprefixed name (a 0.4 import edited before the restart) and\nonly drops the prefixed one; it also renames the select''s fmdb:optionsEmptyLabel. Both\nwalk the translations with getI18Ns(). The migration-write mark the language sync\nconsults moves to MigrationWrites and is set by migrateBothWorkspaces around every pass,\nso no migration writing i18n options has to remember it. The per-node INFO is logged\nafter the save, and a workspace whose nodes all failed says so instead of ''nothing\nfound''. Unit tests: the thirteen names, a weakreference kept as is, both names present,\na switched select left alone.\n\n* refactor: the select''s empty-option label loses its prefix too — the thirteenth and last prefixed property\n\nReview of #312: with fmdb:optionsEmptyLabel left aside, ''a property is never namespaced''\nwas false the moment it was written. Renamed like the twelve others: definition, view,\neditor form, label keys in the four bundles, fixtures, the 0.4-shape Groovy fixture; the\n0.4 spelling stays as a hidden definition for this release and the startup migration\nrenames it on the translation nodes.\n\n* test: spec 48 proves the date field''s migration, the French list and the empty label; spec 219 pins a select switched to a source\n\nReview of #312. The 0.4-shape fixture''s report is asserted (a script error no longer\npasses as a log line), the date field gets the same pre-migration guard as the select,\nthe gate waits for the last renamed state (the date field in live), and the select\ncarries a French option list and an empty-option label through the migration. Spec 219\nswitches a manual select to a source, restarts the engine and checks the mode held.\n\n* docs: startup migrations in two waves, the historical sections keep their release''s spelling, the changelog names no class\n\nReview of #312. The 0.3→0.4 sections describe fmdb:options and fmdb:minBoundMode again,\nwith a pointer to the 0.5.0 rename; the startup-migrations section no longer promises\nthe removal in 0.5 of a migration that ships in 0.5; the thirteenth property and the\nlifted mandatory are documented; the changelog quotes the log line without its class\nprefix.\n\n* fix: the 0.4.0 → 0.5 upgrade deploys and migrates on a real instance — pickers without JCR mandatory, quiet engine-first run, no stamp over a 0.4 mode\n\nTested on a real 0.4.0 instance (Docker, release artifacts, the 0.4.0 playground, both\nworkspaces, both languages):\n\n- Jahia''s DefinitionsBundleChecker refused the engine 0.5 jar: a mandatory property added\n  to a deployed type (optionsRootCategory, optionsRootNode) is a MAJOR change and cancels\n  the deployment. The two pickers lose the JCR-level mandatory for 0.5 like the six other\n  renamed settings; the editor fieldset overrides carry the requirement.\n- Engine upgraded first, the activation run failed on every field (\"Couldn''t find\n  definition for property\"): the element types keep their cached definitions until the\n  elements module is redeployed. MixinPropertyNamesMigration now checks\n  getApplicablePropertyDefinition and leaves such nodes to the redeploy rerun with one\n  INFO line per workspace instead of a stack trace per node.\n- DateBoundsContentMigration ran before the rename at the redeploy and stamped ''date'' on\n  0.4 fields whose mode sat under fmdb:minBoundMode; the stamp then won over the 0.4\n  value. A field carrying a prefixed mode has a mode: it is left to the rename migration.\n\nAfter the fixes: engine-first run = two INFO lines, elements redeploy = 17 + 17 fields\nrenamed, the field dump is identical to the 0.4.0 one modulo the rename of 78 properties,\nnothing live-owned, a republish reaches live, and a 0.4.0 export imports then migrates at\nthe next engine start.\n\n* refactor: the rename migration in small methods — one outcome per node, one summary, one rename pass per owner (Sonar S3776, S135)\n\n* test: the fixture check reads the provisioning status, the leftover list is read on the translation node\n\nThird review of #312. cy.executeGroovy yields the provisioning status (''.installed'' /\n''.failed''), never the script''s report: spec 48 asserts the status and leaves the shape to\nits pre-migration guards. Spec 219 reads the leftover manual list on j:translation_en,\nthe only place it is still readable once the field''s types no longer declare ''options''.\n\n* test: spec 48 publishes both languages, spec 219 plants the leftover list it asserts\n\nThe French list only reaches live when fr is published: the fixture now publishes en and\nfr, so the LIVE assertion on the French options holds. Removing fmdbmix:manualOptions\nclears the translated ''options'' with it (verified on a 0.5 instance through the same\nGraphQL mutation the editor sends), so a mode switch leaves no leftover; spec 219 plants\none the way an import or a script would, then checks the restart leaves it — and the\nmode — alone.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqosY3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMPwQAEBOaYeZXQY75lqw0FB7Dwvr\n8OrxfYay3q93Ra4O3je/OINuE0h0Ie1ySjpDym/k1v8ztAiP+PipS2HHqY/+5/lz\nYLZ0d/8dqiRc/V34yq3RtW+SGJrtDf+t6O7xxXEGCMG/j5cavYPjrnt0ugNL2Q87\nuGbLuZgy0e/tk/Br1uaWAH1hu6ZYa1KIRfJ0BwEBTiQUCsfAuXP44COBL+zux32N\nBO1o7y37/rBvKTcBCFmumKAeyx2LzS2JK4KHmJNrfbbOltsyNiQAHErsCSjLvriz\nxpCg/WyooQIl58C1wUUeijnCFneNdCHKHV3ode6rlYAkbSmBHVDkKYZXoGnD9smF\nG2XlXUmFf9g6qFgipu6lRjg6rbGanILOOESaPxVF1NpWdLHfCBszFB6mF