rl":"https://api.github.com/users/bpapez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bpapez","id":753358,"login":"bpapez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM1OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bpapez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bpapez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bpapez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bpapez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bpapez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bpapez","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/d62b5c4d517ec573d863f8f64be3d9568743085b","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGQ2MmI1YzRkNTE3ZWM1NzNkODYzZjhmNjRiZTNkOTU2ODc0MzA4NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/210631b162e79663a92b0efd59290711658832c5","sha":"210631b162e79663a92b0efd59290711658832c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/210631b162e79663a92b0efd59290711658832c5"}],"sha":"d62b5c4d517ec573d863f8f64be3d9568743085b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/d62b5c4d517ec573d863f8f64be3d9568743085b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/210631b162e79663a92b0efd59290711658832c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:33:40Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:33:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: the styling contract is complete and becomes a folder — guide, class hooks, variables (#303)\n\n* docs: every class hook a form renders is in the styling contract\n\nThe Class hooks table missed hooks the shipped markup carries, and the extended inputs had no styling documentation at all — a template set styling forms rode on undocumented internals (see luxe-jahia-demo#468 and industrial#16). Measured from the source at b5afcb0: 112 class names are rendered by formidable-elements and formidable-extended-inputs; the table gains the ones it lacked (form-element, fieldset-elements, content, options-source error, step number, btn-danger, message details, the rest of the file list, the two edit-mode wrappers), the actions zone section names its structure, and a new Extended inputs section documents the fmdbext-* hooks and the 21 --fmdbext-* variables with their defaults. Every class the two modules emit is now in this document; the visually-editable form (#297) documents its own on its branch.\n\n* chore: changelog entry for the styling guide, named after the pull request\n\n* docs: the styling contract says which revision it was measured against, and that no check keeps it so yet (#305)\n\n* docs: the styling contract names the four data attributes that are functional markers, not hooks\n\n* docs: the styling contract becomes a folder — a guide with the rendered markup, the class hooks, the variables\n\ndocs/styling/README.md opens the contract: where styles belong, a tree of the\nmarkup every form renders (which class on which element, what exists only in\nedit mode or only on a multi-step form), the conventions (two prefixes, hooks\nvs variables vs data attributes, hashed classes are private) and the line\nsaying against which revision the pages were measured (#305).\n\ndocs/styling/class-hooks.md keeps the tables and the paragraphs on the\nsurfaces, the conditional-logic wrapper, the form actions zone and the\nextended inputs; docs/styling/css-variables.md gathers every variable — the\nvalidation ones move here from custom-validation.md, which now points at the\ncontract, and the three range-slider variables get a table instead of a\nparenthesis in a class row.\n\nEvery stylesheet that defines hooks or variables opens with one line naming\nthe contract, so the next rename meets it. Links to docs/styling.md are\nrepointed (README, form-submission-flow, CmShell, richTextUtils.test).","tree":{"sha":"933be37850807cadb014f63dcb76acef2c958e1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/933be37850807cadb014f63dcb76acef2c958e1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/210631b162e79663a92b0efd59290711658832c5","verification":{"payload":"tree 933be37850807cadb014f63dcb76acef2c958e1b\nparent 64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1788960820 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788960820 +0200\n\ndocs: the styling contract is complete and becomes a folder — guide, class hooks, variables (#303)\n\n* docs: every class hook a form renders is in the styling contract\n\nThe Class hooks table missed hooks the shipped markup carries, and the extended inputs had no styling documentation at all — a template set styling forms rode on undocumented internals (see luxe-jahia-demo#468 and industrial#16). Measured from the source at b5afcb0: 112 class names are rendered by formidable-elements and formidable-extended-inputs; the table gains the ones it lacked (form-element, fieldset-elements, content, options-source error, step number, btn-danger, message details, the rest of the file list, the two edit-mode wrappers), the actions zone section names its structure, and a new Extended inputs section documents the fmdbext-* hooks and the 21 --fmdbext-* variables with their defaults. Every class the two modules emit is now in this document; the visually-editable form (#297) documents its own on its branch.\n\n* chore: changelog entry for the styling guide, named after the pull request\n\n* docs: the styling contract says which revision it was measured against, and that no check keeps it so yet (#305)\n\n* docs: the styling contract names the four data attributes that are functional markers, not hooks\n\n* docs: the styling contract becomes a folder — a guide with the rendered markup, the class hooks, the variables\n\ndocs/styling/README.md opens the contract: where styles belong, a tree of the\nmarkup every form renders (which class on which element, what exists only in\nedit mode or only on a multi-step form), the conventions (two prefixes, hooks\nvs variables vs data attributes, hashed classes are private) and the line\nsaying against which revision the pages were measured (#305).\n\ndocs/styling/class-hooks.md keeps the tables and the paragraphs on the\nsurfaces, the conditional-logic wrapper, the form actions zone and the\nextended inputs; docs/styling/css-variables.md gathers every variable — the\nvalidation ones move here from custom-validation.md, which now points at the\ncontract, and the three range-slider variables get a table instead of a\nparenthesis in a class row.\n\nEvery stylesheet that defines hooks or variables opens with one line naming\nthe contract, so the next rename meets it. Links to docs/styling.md are\nrepointed (README, form-submission-flow, CmShell, richTextUtils.test).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoWA0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArhwQAHBcBdTcrrbUZHN0HijTeddb\n8+GUm0EJmbmimzwV1C5lkLkvBSFoHCGNlK7mrPevaQ5fRxDliknLUA6pDRmt9qyI\nZpNSPa+/sFRun3qUyRr0HRdVsaXwUccn4YjrmZaUUJ0zWC9eSRs2BWQsSWKXr+nL\nU3elOeMn/xlJuVjcsNsHUZnQNbGGqcpy33mvIxpdRIAlCAX7/FYKPTZvCsAOR+P/\nEY4SE6s2//YcPM1YW36BXxLsFB5+1d0Wg/6sATlRminihirAx+6Hks9Pzbl8pp6v\nSb5QRfOO1+uSF8YM+mqGFg2xODY0vohGVUUlo2MHUOCpSb0g0E/ZojYt7qPH+No4\nqPxxAN+bqxYnvGidkOrsh6dBpu7ad+eS9Wy832VV4sBDo0B2kI2AUUdlKCjDtesT\nvWf11Zj9l+kbqfgAJWW28idvbfh4tZd02K0Ys50UCVeOMstFUi0vvz1NZ5p+89g+\nhS55ygERSzJmyfqXjnkXzdifnDZ1EzQWOQTV6MsI8B+oyA0rYTCG/DE4aDtffO4E\nfv7p4J0oYeovlfpnEhTzIACAmisqZXNjAhzr09PRCfStOKRzQX4vga8cTMpFP7y/\nq1uFy4CFJ8g8990DPVBSCEBxERfrz+cDFdv7veaN+WZNkU7qWSsWuFM2sJTTOEWX\nUNEO6VqlzVPuf41GlkPX\n=xMRZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T13:33:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/210631b162e79663a92b0efd59290711658832c5","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDIxMDYzMWIxNjJlNzk2NjNhOTJiMGVmZDU5MjkwNzExNjU4ODMyYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27","sha":"64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27"}],"sha":"210631b162e79663a92b0efd59290711658832c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/210631b162e79663a92b0efd59290711658832c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:11:21Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:11:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the form results tell the submitter''s time zone (#302)\n\n* feat: the form results tell the submitter''s time zone\n\nCloses #286. A submission stores the date and datetime values as typed, without a zone,\nand the results show them as typed since #285 — so a reader could not tell where 12:53\napplied. The form client now sends the browser''s zone with the submission\n(X-Formidable-Time-Zone, as it sends the captcha token and the logic state); the save-to-JCR\naction keeps it on the submission (timeZone) when it names a zone the platform knows — the\nheader is the client''s, and its value is shown to editors — and drops anything else. The\nresults show the zone with the submission''s metadata, after each datetime value\n(\"05/09/2026 12:53 (Europe/Paris)\"), and in the JSON and CSV exports; a submission without\none (posted outside a browser, or stored before) shows its values alone. Unit tests on the\nzone filter and the value formatting; spec 28 checks the stored zone is the browser''s; the\nexport, storage and flow docs list the property and the header.\n\n* chore: the changelog entry references this pull request\n\n* refactor: review round on the submitter''s time zone\n\n- SaveToJcrFormAction reads the known zone ids once (getAvailableZoneIds()\n  returns a fresh 600-entry copy per call) and logs at debug level the\n  header values it drops, so a browser zone list running ahead of the\n  JVM''s tzdb can be told apart from a submission posted outside a browser;\n  the length bound''s comment names the actual longest id (32 characters).\n- The header name and the browser-zone reader move out of the submission\n  hook into utils/timeZone.ts, next to the other submission headers'' home.\n- csv.test.ts asserts the header row and that each metadata value lands\n  under its own header: the two hand-maintained arrays must stay aligned.\n- docs/save-to-jcr.md: the Personal Data section lists the time zone as\n  the second request-derived value kept by default and says why; the\n  metadata bullet gives both reasons for an absent zone and states that\n  the zone is the submitter''s, not the value''s (so does the results code).\n\n* fix: the dropped-zone debug log builds its argument only when debug is on (Sonar S2629)","tree":{"sha":"da5fbe8ec3b30325e67b1284384236a277b2c64d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/da5fbe8ec3b30325e67b1284384236a277b2c64d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27","verification":{"payload":"tree da5fbe8ec3b30325e67b1284384236a277b2c64d\nparent 811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1788945081 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788945081 +0200\n\nfeat: the form results tell the submitter''s time zone (#302)\n\n* feat: the form results tell the submitter''s time zone\n\nCloses #286. A submission stores the date and datetime values as typed, without a zone,\nand the results show them as typed since #285 — so a reader could not tell where 12:53\napplied. The form client now sends the browser''s zone with the submission\n(X-Formidable-Time-Zone, as it sends the captcha token and the logic state); the save-to-JCR\naction keeps it on the submission (timeZone) when it names a zone the platform knows — the\nheader is the client''s, and its value is shown to editors — and drops anything else. The\nresults show the zone with the submission''s metadata, after each datetime value\n(\"05/09/2026 12:53 (Europe/Paris)\"), and in the JSON and CSV exports; a submission without\none (posted outside a browser, or stored before) shows its values alone. Unit tests on the\nzone filter and the value formatting; spec 28 checks the stored zone is the browser''s; the\nexport, storage and flow docs list the property and the header.\n\n* chore: the changelog entry references this pull request\n\n* refactor: review round on the submitter''s time zone\n\n- SaveToJcrFormAction reads the known zone ids once (getAvailableZoneIds()\n  returns a fresh 600-entry copy per call) and logs at debug level the\n  header values it drops, so a browser zone list running ahead of the\n  JVM''s tzdb can be told apart from a submission posted outside a browser;\n  the length bound''s comment names the actual longest id (32 characters).\n- The header name and the browser-zone reader move out of the submission\n  hook into utils/timeZone.ts, next to the other submission headers'' home.\n- csv.test.ts asserts the header row and that each metadata value lands\n  under its own header: the two hand-maintained arrays must stay aligned.\n- docs/save-to-jcr.md: the Personal Data section lists the time zone as\n  the second request-derived value kept by default and says why; the\n  metadata bullet gives both reasons for an absent zone and states that\n  the zone is the submitter''s, not the value''s (so does the results code).\n\n* fix: the dropped-zone debug log builds its argument only when debug is on (Sonar S2629)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoSK5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoa8QADbrXlIBVt93KxDMpmezsUUl\nUST+C5wu5rvEdDkpZy60zw9UeDhbOeyVPtTm8wO1ZVN5VGZksNyNSrgR3v/BVO7t\ncT0hbwD09x951u1HtiQiXmJYJAgFCIxF0a/rJlDWbwGpoHXQg2XQJiabnI9petaM\n5lMjEfQFiyh0k/c3dxYhFobFi2zm3FkIur2XVdlQtCirOb1sRho0PXafDBST9uPT\naCknk23zYvA5Pfvk1pDRM3IpzEqYbHLpsaWF2l3AVg+SXjjdxORpPw/bCrnUihim\nqEWTDwOUNsziqrLc+nUyk5MoMzM2/QfAxWSKhMkFJmPt7oxcNdNr+bzvi5ma4PkH\njpU0nCoFA2UK77kvAuab0oQjkPi+tBG0c0K96E+gVsQbbziYCzKi3Zsq4vYQAJG+\nNjnT2SdO4/u85GmWCe78BQvzYe1Cg8tTCsd0ksf4CkvAgw4keLQ3vrnpaKumrvys\n5jCBKnxKKqVvsEVkxMsCdIIsb8xTf8GYT41+wI6/u3J13iB9JL6/6r48ghZp3b3y\ncqPSePUuMnEj0iaeuE+ujAySLqXMdgmiobfF15D/HhCuS7+f49pyqIwajxH/UZRA\na21d0LJzTiNliVwS0LIoQuphzkPHguQ0WHmoJ0Yeb2lL0rWhvo6O4yU5cw6lyRyJ\nvK4cesb38udiddNCAjzO\n=oWGB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T09:11:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDY0YTliNzZjODJmMjYyOWM1YjY4NWVkMTllNjEyYzAwZGM3YmZiMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af","sha":"811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af"}],"sha":"64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/64a9b76c82f2629c5b685ed19e612c00dc7bfb27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:11:56Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:11:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: the cypress suite is type-checked before the integration run (#304)\n\n* ci: the Cypress suite is type-checked, in a second, before the integration run\n\nCloses #280. Nothing type-checked the specs: tests/tsconfig.json covers one folder level, so\ncypress/e2e/**/*.cy.ts never was, and lib-tsconfig.json covers the page objects only — a\nspec passing the wrong property shape (#275''s `options` for `choices`) stayed green until a\nforty-minute integration run. A typecheck-tsconfig.json includes the whole suite with the\nstrictness of tsconfig.json, `yarn typecheck` runs it, and the static-analysis CI job runs\nit too. The burn-down (8 errors): the content-integrity helpers typed their Apollo callbacks\nby parameter annotation, which the .then() overloads refuse when the callback returns a\nvalue — they read the result as the query''s shape instead — and mixed plain and chained\nreturns in one .then(), now all chains; a tampering spec read a name its type did not\ndeclare; a date spec called localDay() without its offset.\n\n* ci: one tsconfig for the editor, cypress and the type check; one today helper\n\n- tests/tsconfig.json is the suite''s single TypeScript config: it includes\n  every spec (cypress/**/*.ts), carries the lib and the types the specs\n  use, and `yarn typecheck` runs on it — what an editor reports and what\n  CI checks can no longer differ. typecheck-tsconfig.json is gone. Cypress\n  compiles the specs with the same file (ts-loader, transpile only), so\n  the options are type-level ones plus downlevelIteration; the emitted\n  code is otherwise untouched. The header says why strict mode is off.\n- localDay: one helper in support/constants, offset defaulting to today,\n  re-exported by the validation support module. The two same-name copies\n  had different signatures, and a bare call on the required-offset one\n  evaluated to \"NaN-NaN-NaN\" without failing the spec.","tree":{"sha":"339c24798c3032bf4f63525775ebb8b5fc8ce4a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/339c24798c3032bf4f63525775ebb8b5fc8ce4a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af","verification":{"payload":"tree 339c24798c3032bf4f63525775ebb8b5fc8ce4a2\nparent 5f5c43159e7ad54cd72dac209ba7dcd5db850eb3\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1788941516 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788941516 +0200\n\nci: the cypress suite is type-checked before the integration run (#304)\n\n* ci: the Cypress suite is type-checked, in a second, before the integration run\n\nCloses #280. Nothing type-checked the specs: tests/tsconfig.json covers one folder level, so\ncypress/e2e/**/*.cy.ts never was, and lib-tsconfig.json covers the page objects only — a\nspec passing the wrong property shape (#275''s `options` for `choices`) stayed green until a\nforty-minute integration run. A typecheck-tsconfig.json includes the whole suite with the\nstrictness of tsconfig.json, `yarn typecheck` runs it, and the static-analysis CI job runs\nit too. The burn-down (8 errors): the content-integrity helpers typed their Apollo callbacks\nby parameter annotation, which the .then() overloads refuse when the callback returns a\nvalue — they read the result as the query''s shape instead — and mixed plain and chained\nreturns in one .then(), now all chains; a tampering spec read a name its type did not\ndeclare; a date spec called localDay() without its offset.\n\n* ci: one tsconfig for the editor, cypress and the type check; one today helper\n\n- tests/tsconfig.json is the suite''s single TypeScript config: it includes\n  every spec (cypress/**/*.ts), carries the lib and the types the specs\n  use, and `yarn typecheck` runs on it — what an editor reports and what\n  CI checks can no longer differ. typecheck-tsconfig.json is gone. Cypress\n  compiles the specs with the same file (ts-loader, transpile only), so\n  the options are type-level ones plus downlevelIteration; the emitted\n  code is otherwise untouched. The header says why strict mode is off.\n- localDay: one helper in support/constants, offset defaulting to today,\n  re-exported by the validation support module. The two same-name copies\n  had different signatures, and a bare call on the required-offset one\n  evaluated to \"NaN-NaN-NaN\" without failing the spec.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoRTMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtRAQAJZbeNR07J5zpJncsHDTuZdj\n3pnEzfLgQLRX0WAPyq+oVYzvqxZT1m/4Jdns8pc8iLnyUs5wB5j2/kBeTbnpd2Y6\nPBjIMJKuI3XWnNg961ELz7ucfx1r8Nti2OUq7cYrGZFnWEIlp6xnhZbUH8r1HLGJ\nwdyc1syXSRJccHDdq7ltWJnSLJeNMO1ZQ9x7e0PeYFTNuacWX09cMdkxeKUA9tIO\nid8UWKRQF1A+3SaqjlBB4Fip+7QtkIb2Be0u5Ut8wtAeGLQ4VHpciOi1oXKc7Z/p\n+IoegimutUU/jUuJHLfOoW5Cz02GvaL/83XQIz6hdLQsdp9TBORjGOAHb5HYX8sw\neZzdc24kPlEMN9IkPVs6zua8XJDwcHMBgkJuWHObKGETf9cBjF+96c/G1kZPVvsC\nSKDoAL/iNEqxhNbHRtQPrdrgVk5byj2y0mVe4pTyFCewhgFg7hn28IsFXAJjjomU\nkFFWlgiGL8OiZ1tcpVtxlmLr50ECN6Wl5mAikrOO6EFo2+17910JR9mRibrDp/T6\nMsGBVzEXTmch0TS3rQtsjL3GRqryptUIRjwJMOPn2Cyl609T2Zu2qkqrs8cyNF3T\n1haaigBQvHfw41o0cy/lhneacsS6GokNLMh7zKbCRn2rZg2uyzNk7IjJaCq+tHEJ\nkrrra3P6GFIJercuATj4\n=Z5NZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T08:11:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDgxMTY2OWNkY2JiOTI0YjMxMDRkNDI5YmM3NjI4NjJjZGZhZjUyYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/5f5c43159e7ad54cd72dac209ba7dcd5db850eb3","sha":"5f5c43159e7ad54cd72dac209ba7dcd5db850eb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/5f5c43159e7ad54cd72dac209ba7dcd5db850eb3"}],"sha":"811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/811669cdcbb924b3104d429bc762862cdfaf52af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/5f5c43159e7ad54cd72dac209ba7dcd5db850eb3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:11:17Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:11:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: the jsp test template set no longer shadows the platform''s content template (#301)\n\n* fix: the jsp test template set no longer shadows the platform''s content template\n\nThe clone of content-template declared a view the module does not ship, and\nthe same-priority clone hid the default module''s wrapper on every site using\nthe set: the form preview was empty there and the Page Builder frame failed.\nThe clone is removed; the platform''s applies.\n\nFixes #293\n\n(cherry picked from commit 70a67c4ce26b8e4be4fd6537f516c4788d4f109c)\n\n* chore: the changelog entry references this pull request\n\n* test: the preview of a form under /contents must render the form\n\nSpec validation/47 requests the preview URL of a form created under the\ntest site''s /contents and asserts a non-empty page holding the form and\nits field: the regression #293 fixes was an HTTP 200 with a zero-byte\nbody, and nothing in the suite noticed. The site fixture already sits on\nthe JSP test template set, so the guard costs one request.\n\nThe changelog entry is withdrawn: the change only touches a test module\nthat never ships to a customer (label no-changelog).","tree":{"sha":"39da6e9dce4fe1c1414e5c172d6ef811d44817a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/39da6e9dce4fe1c1414e5c172d6ef811d44817a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/5f5c43159e7ad54cd72dac209ba7dcd5db850eb3","verification":{"payload":"tree 39da6e9dce4fe1c1414e5c172d6ef811d44817a0\nparent b5afcb015cf5d30e7034188c7c2c77a83d40a37b\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1788941477 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788941477 +0200\n\nfix: the jsp test template set no longer shadows the platform''s content template (#301)\n\n* fix: the jsp test template set no longer shadows the platform''s content template\n\nThe clone of content-template declared a view the module does not ship, and\nthe same-priority clone hid the default module''s wrapper on every site using\nthe set: the form preview was empty there and the Page Builder frame failed.\nThe clone is removed; the platform''s applies.\n\nFixes #293\n\n(cherry picked from commit 70a67c4ce26b8e4be4fd6537f516c4788d4f109c)\n\n* chore: the changelog entry references this pull request\n\n* test: the preview of a form under /contents must render the form\n\nSpec validation/47 requests the preview URL of a form created under the\ntest site''s /contents and asserts a non-empty page holding the form and\nits field: the regression #293 fixes was an HTTP 200 with a zero-byte\nbody, and nothing in the suite noticed. The site fixture already sits on\nthe JSP test template set, so the guard costs one request.\n\nThe changelog entry is withdrawn: the change only touches a test module\nthat never ships to a customer (label no-changelog).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoRSlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqCIQAGLZClyehP5OAlWTS+CxXAyx\n99cQ1zla2BX0iFzNzWzvMiLKCrMfj3sjgmQW4LTAaL0oVVgMU8l/8lUbWk7iejDn\nGP+ulPZB4dVzu3ZcS+1yPIU6WZule1dZdgk4AiLMAE3L11cKTX9DLHSZNAzYp507\nC4UtFpsSYdFFnXfRtn1VbWDydtmpVe9r5bfdSsziMTJlJeJGnAh4INnwScbfli+2\ncmIOYONdZ2uPVu16d7zn6/e5i8qdPpDRDtqMfyYFrOj3s43TMBDbNaFISGvan2/J\nlle5pXwUuTcIvrUXlHKaLC0nuVGApx+dX3Cq6I9gRPPqosT8jVp9uTRBp7EMUVbe\nh7t