//api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/77e103748895f3f2972bed12bae14d543665968e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/fa77931c9397008100ade5b569f55c065e5504e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:58:07Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:58:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(samples): help text above, below or on both sides of a field, from a third-party module (#298)\n\n* feat(samples): a text input''s help text placed above, below or on both sides of the field\n\nThe sample-tsx test module shows a third-party module adding a contributor setting to a\nbuilt-in field and honouring it: a mixin extending fmdb:inputText carries the position\n(up, the built-in rendering, down, or both); the module''s own form override surfaces it\nin the text input''s editor fieldset right under Help text and keeps the mixin always\nactivated, so there is no switch to flip; and an \"Input text - Help text position\" view,\npicked in the View chooser, renders the help where it was put — one block described to\nassistive technology, the repeat of \"both\" decorative and unlabelled. Spec 222 covers the\nlive markup and the editor form (the sample module is enabled on the test site by the\nspec); the extension guide gets a Case 4.\n\n* feat(samples): the help text position extends every built-in field with a help text\n\nhelpText is declared by each concrete field type, not by fmdbmix:element, so the sample\nmixin now extends the twelve built-in types declaring one (the optional types of\nformidable-extended-inputs are left out: the sample module does not depend on it). One form\noverride, carried by the mixin itself, places the setting under Help text in every one of\nthose types — the <main> fieldset of an override is the edited type''s own — at rank 1.4,\nahead of the options mode the choice fields put at 1.5. Still a single sample view, on the\ntext input. Spec 222 checks the editor form of a select as well; the guide follows.\n\n* feat(samples): the sample rendering takes the place of Formidable''s text input view\n\nNo view to pick any more: the sample registers a default view of fmdb:inputText with a\npriority above Formidable''s (0), so on a site enabled for the module every text input\nrenders through it and the help text goes where the contributor put it; the view says so\nin its header, and a data attribute tells its rendering from the built-in one. The mixin''s\nown editor fieldset, emptied by the move of its field under Help text, is hidden — it would\notherwise show as a bare switch — while the editor keeps adding the mixin on save. Spec 222\nfollows (no j:view, the attribute asserted), so does the guide. Verified on a local 8.2.4\ninstance: the takeover is site-scoped, sites without the module keep the built-in rendering.\n\n* docs(samples): a README of the sample module, the help text position walked through for integrators\n\n* docs(samples): one page per sample, the README as their table of contents\n\n* fix(samples): a masked text input keeps its pattern and formatted default, the view ordering rule told right\n\nReview of #298. The sample view dropped `mask`, and with it the HTML pattern the built-in view\nderives from it — the only format check a mask-only field has, browser and server alike — the\ndata-mask attribute and the formatting of a prefilled default: the mask tokens are now written\nout in the sample, like the validation attributes, so only the live formatting (Formidable''s\nisland) stays out of reach; spec 222 pins it on a masked field. The guide claimed views resolve\non the primary type before the mixins: the engine orders every candidate by priority, then module\ndisplay name, then view key, whatever type it was registered on — the paragraph now says so and\nnames priority as the only deterministic lever.\n\n* test: the id of the described help block is read on a fresh query\n\nSpec 222 chained `.invoke(''attr'', ''id'')` after `.and(''not.have.attr'', ''aria-hidden'')`, and\nCypress makes `have.attr` with the name alone yield the attribute''s value — undefined for an\nabsent one — so the invoke ran on nothing. The assertions on a block and the read of its id\nare now separate queries. Only that chain failed on CI: the three placements, the setting left\nunset, the masked field and the editor form all passed.\n\n* docs(samples): the pointer to the guide names what it explains, the ordering of same-named views","tree":{"sha":"59a59d650a989bcc2cc0e487b79d395167ec77a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/59a59d650a989bcc2cc0e487b79d395167ec77a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/fa77931c9397008100ade5b569f55c065e5504e7","verification":{"payload":"tree 59a59d650a989bcc2cc0e487b79d395167ec77a0\nparent 35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1788875887 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788875887 +0200\n\nfeat(samples): help text above, below or on both sides of a field, from a third-party module (#298)\n\n* feat(samples): a text input''s help text placed above, below or on both sides of the field\n\nThe sample-tsx test module shows a third-party module adding a contributor setting to a\nbuilt-in field and honouring it: a mixin extending fmdb:inputText carries the position\n(up, the built-in rendering, down, or both); the module''s own form override surfaces it\nin the text input''s editor fieldset right under Help text and keeps the mixin always\nactivated, so there is no switch to flip; and an \"Input text - Help text position\" view,\npicked in the View chooser, renders the help where it was put — one block described to\nassistive technology, the repeat of \"both\" decorative and unlabelled. Spec 222 covers the\nlive markup and the editor form (the sample module is enabled on the test site by the\nspec); the extension guide gets a Case 4.\n\n* feat(samples): the help text position extends every built-in field with a help text\n\nhelpText is declared by each concrete field type, not by fmdbmix:element, so the sample\nmixin now extends the twelve built-in types declaring one (the optional types of\nformidable-extended-inputs are left out: the sample module does not depend on it). One form\noverride, carried by the mixin itself, places the setting under Help text in every one of\nthose types — the <main> fieldset of an override is the edited type''s own — at rank 1.4,\nahead of the options mode the choice fields put at 1.5. Still a single sample view, on the\ntext input. Spec 222 checks the editor form of a select as well; the guide follows.\n\n* feat(samples): the sample rendering takes the place of Formidable''s text input view\n\nNo view to pick any more: the sample registers a default view of fmdb:inputText with a\npriority above Formidable''s (0), so on a site enabled for the module every text input\nrenders through it and the help text goes where the contributor put it; the view says so\nin its header, and a data attribute tells its rendering from the built-in one. The mixin''s\nown editor fieldset, emptied by the move of its field under Help text, is hidden — it would\notherwise show as a bare switch — while the editor keeps adding the mixin on save. Spec 222\nfollows (no j:view, the attribute asserted), so does the guide. Verified on a local 8.2.4\ninstance: the takeover is site-scoped, sites without the module keep the built-in rendering.\n\n* docs(samples): a README of the sample module, the help text position walked through for integrators\n\n* docs(samples): one page per sample, the README as their table of contents\n\n* fix(samples): a masked text input keeps its pattern and formatted default, the view ordering rule told right\n\nReview of #298. The sample view dropped `mask`, and with it the HTML pattern the built-in view\nderives from it — the only format check a mask-only field has, browser and server alike — the\ndata-mask attribute and the formatting of a prefilled default: the mask tokens are now written\nout in the sample, like the validation attributes, so only the live formatting (Formidable''s\nisland) stays out of reach; spec 222 pins it on a masked field. The guide claimed views resolve\non the primary type before the mixins: the engine orders every candidate by priority, then module\ndisplay name, then view key, whatever type it was registered on — the paragraph now says so and\nnames priority as the only deterministic lever.\n\n* test: the id of the described help block is read on a fresh query\n\nSpec 222 chained `.invoke(''attr'', ''id'')` after `.and(''not.have.attr'', ''aria-hidden'')`, and\nCypress makes `have.attr` with the name alone yield the attribute''s value — undefined for an\nabsent one — so the invoke ran on nothing. The assertions on a block and the read of its id\nare now separate queries. Only that chain failed on CI: the three placements, the setting left\nunset, the masked field and the editor form all passed.\n\n* docs(samples): the pointer to the guide names what it explains, the ordering of same-named views","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoBRvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqGgQADjwmCX+RoyS2rMes9cIWO7x\nP4FaThlv6Pgrqbx/ZCBQHMMxWu0uqVgOEoWR2tnlQi+LNYfsr98dIr1A8VOqne1I\nqBzzhWnGqX7jlU/iZGQBE0ugF4l/BYE1YMhWW63BrUOGRYwdswOc1hcwjudH2DrR\nXVPCQMg6iIGizFY7U8JAVGjaUCLX7cVdneU6TbpFSQ5fGf0iXz7DDU7u7ZvrREK5\nTlkL31D3Es63X7pl6SdQ++pYcMSc/VEOtEL+GXl0L2p/m8lzuYY0uq+v5BT/jb7u\nqMrGI92brygtve2AqX/D/sX+71YOctGwI+ln9MBvGP/YroAPArT5UoqSoV/3Ie8E\nTxlnmK9jRn5rjWvd6X2/fIn+09gsFLejez1kojV9eGx7wyiexIpRBmwxSGc7H47g\nDOqs9X043hTp9Fl0H2w77tVXSUvUZX0FggU6aOEmV1JYzhGc+i8CUv9C4Pmfj8z9\nfYFQCMY/0eGdYSfG6qe8FkwVI7hJLlvvGEdT51ICC4COrSrHh6O/7s1IXlr8Areu\n3I3/9HNHk0CyNbtLsYXFwhRPFYMpcPiPehiuXEW4iXxPWXchnfvyLwzJmS4FoR94\nfse9N59/4DqcDzqUcr2zMuHsLNQMwW7hKSm7P5SU+mzdqspCb+QfoM+gQ8P+c9e+\nRpG/KFiVZjMIV8qIprcf\n=E/s1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T13:58:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/fa77931c9397008100ade5b569f55c065e5504e7","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGZhNzc5MzFjOTM5NzAwODEwMGFkZTViNTY5ZjU1YzA2NWU1NTA0ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc","sha":"35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc"}],"sha":"fa77931c9397008100ade5b569f55c065e5504e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/fa77931c9397008100ade5b569f55c065e5504e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:56:11Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:56:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: form actions zone in the Page Builder edit view (#294)\n\n* feat: form actions zone in the Page Builder edit view\n\nOn a page, the Page Builder showed a form''s fields, steps and fieldsets but nothing\nof its actions: the list was not rendered, so a contributor could neither see which\nactions run on submission, nor tell that a form had none, nor add one from there —\nand a form without any action discards every submission.\n\nWhile authoring, the form now renders its action list as a zone of its own, inside\nthe form (a business stylesheet''s card keeps it) and under the buttons: a header,\none compact two-line card per action — rank in the execution order (a CSS counter;\nthe list is orderable, so a Page Builder drag reorders the pipeline), the type icon,\nthe title with the one telling parameter (recipient, forward target), and smaller the\ntype description its module declares for the Content Editor (the <type>.ui.tooltip\nbundle key, read through server.osgi.loadPropertiesResource: nothing duplicated, a\nthird-party action documented for the editor is documented for the zone) — then the\nlist''s own create button. The placeholder''s accepted type is the fmdbmix:formAction\nmixin, so jContent shows one \"New Form Action\" button (icon added to the engine) and\nthen the type chooser. A form without any action gets a warning instead of the cards.\n\nAuthoring chrome, deliberately not styled like the form, every value a variable.\nTo sit under the buttons, the form is a flex column while authoring and the island''s\nchildren wrapper is dissolved (display: contents); if either wrapper changes, the\nzone merely stays between the fields and the buttons. Nothing of it exists in live,\npreview or the cm view.\n\nCloses #292\n\n* feat: one icon for the form actions, results-oriented save-to-JCR tooltip\n\nThe zone header and the \"New Form Action\" button showed a lightning glyph while\njContent already shows the action list''s own type icon (four outward arrows) on the\nlist''s box and in the tree: two icons for one thing. The header now shows the list\ntype''s icon itself (resolved from the node type, `<module>/icons/<type>.png`, the way\nthe cards already resolve theirs) and the engine''s mixin icon is that same PNG — the\nbutton''s icon cannot be automatic, jContent takes the icon of the placeholder''s\naccepted type, the mixin the engine declares, which had none.\n\nThe save-to-JCR tooltip described storage (\"child nodes under a designated JCR path\")\ninstead of what the contributor gets: submissions kept in Jahia, to be reviewed in the\nForm Results screen. Reworded in the four bundles.\n\nThe zone header wraps in a narrow form card, and the changelog entry references the\npull request.\n\n* fix: show the forward target''s label on the action card, not its id\n\nThe contributor picks a forward target by the label the administrator configured\n(the choicelist shows labels); the card showed the stored id (crm01) instead. The\nlabel is resolved through the engine''s configuration service, falling back to the\nid when the target is no longer configured — worth seeing too.\n\n* fix: keep the actions zone''s Page Builder frame on the zone\n\nThe space above the zone was the zone''s own top margin; the Page Builder wraps the\nzone in a flex item whose box includes that margin, so the hover and selection frame\nstarted at the buttons row and read as a wider selection. The space now sits on the\nbuttons row while authoring.\n\n* fix: no dead grey below the New Form Action button\n\njContent gives the create placeholder a 28px minimum height and a 10px bottom margin;\nthe button is the last thing in the zone, so that margin only padded the grey below\nit. Dropped inside the zone.\n\n* feat: the action card''s key parameter comes from the type declaration\n\nThe parameter shown next to an action''s title was a hard-coded table in elements (to,\nto, targetId): a third-party action showed nothing, and the forward target''s label was\nresolved through the engine''s configuration service by name. The rule now lives in the\nengine, next to the action model, as ActionSummaryService: the key parameter is the\nfirst property the type declares after jcr:title that a contributor reads at a glance —\na single, visible, unprotected string edited as a small text or a choicelist — and a\nchoice is shown by the label its choicelist initializer gives it, the way the Content\nEditor showed it. Long texts, flags, numbers, references and lists are skipped, as are\nthe technical jcr:/j: properties.\n\nSame result for the engine''s types (recipient, recipient, target label, nothing for\nSave to JCR), nothing to register for a third-party action: the how-to documents how to\norder a CND so the telling property comes first. Elements only displays what the\nservice returns. The criterion is a pure function on the property''s declared\nattributes, unit-tested without Jahia classes (they cannot be mocked).\n\n* test: the accepted action type is read on the list''s module, not on its placeholder\n\nThe core writes the child-type constraint (nodetypes) on the module of the list\nand leaves the create placeholder untyped, so the spec looked for the mixin where\nit never is. It now asserts the list module declares fmdbmix:formAction and holds\nexactly one placeholder; the comments describing the placeholder follow.\n\n* fix: the action summary warning names the property and node, not the value\n\nCopilot review on #294: a failed label resolution logged the raw property\nvalue, which could carry contributor-entered data. Property name and node\npath are enough to find the case.\n\n* fix: readable zone hints, tooltip words kept apart, choice labels under test\n\nCopilot review on #294: the zone''s muted text (#6b7280 on #f4f5f7) read at 4.4:1,\nbelow AA — now #626977 (5.1:1), documented default updated; stripping the tooltip\nmarkup joined words separated by a <br/> — tags are replaced by a space before\nwhitespace collapses; the value-to-label match of a choicelist parameter is now a\npure function with its own tests (Jahia definitions cannot be mocked, the\ninitializer chaining stays covered by the Page Builder itself).\n\n* fix: the authoring views guard themselves, a blank choice label falls back, third-party type under test\n\nCopilot review on #294: the zone and card views relied on the form view''s edit-mode\ncheck, while a view can be requested directly in live or preview — each now returns\nnothing outside edit mode, and spec 47 requests both in live. A matching choice with\na blank label returned that blank and hid the parameter; the stored value is shown\ninstead. The spec also puts the test module''s own action on the form and reads its\nlabel, tooltip (declared for this) and icon through that module, the third-party\ncontract the docs advertise.\n\n* fix: the actions zone is an ordered list, and choice labels resolve as in the Content Editor\n\nCopilot review on #294: the execution order was DOM order plus a CSS counter on\ngeneric divs, so assistive technology had no list semantics — the cards now sit\nin an ol/li with the native numbering reset (the counter stays). The choicelist\ninitializers were called with a partial context; they now get what the core''s\nContentDefinitionHelper gives them — contextType, the dependent properties''\ncurrent values under their names, and a chain started from null — so a\nthird-party initializer resolves the same label here as in the editor.\n\n* fix: tooltips read as UTF-8 with entities decoded, forward label under test, no duplicated literal\n\nCopilot review on #294 and Sonar: the tooltip lookup went through Properties.load,\nwhich decodes ISO-8859-1 and would turn a JavaScript module''s raw UTF-8 accents into\nmojibake — the bundle is now read as text and parsed by a small Properties reader\nthat also resolves Java escapes (unit-tested); HTML entities of a rich tooltip are\ndecoded, since the text is rendered as React text; spec 47 configures a forward\ntarget and puts a forward action on the form, so the choicelist resolution through\nthe engine''s initializer is exercised end to end; the live requests of the guarded\nviews now require a 200 before asserting the markup is absent; the repeated\n\"dependentProperties\" literal is a constant.\n\n* fix: a long card title clips, and a dependentProperties option without a list is tolerated\n\nOwn review of the branch: the card title had the ellipsis rules but no min-width,\nso a long title overflowed the card instead of clipping; a choicelist declaring\ndependentProperties without a value made split() return null and the card fall\nback to the raw id through the catch. The styling doc''s overlong line is reflowed,\nand the how-to says the key parameter comes from the type''s own declarations.\n\n* test: the guarded authoring views are requested in live as fragments\n\nSpec 47 was red since 00d5b1f asked for a 200 on the direct live render of the\nauthoring views: a plain render URL (node.view.html) goes through the template\nwrapper, which resolves a page template named after the view and answers 404\nbefore the view runs (TemplateNodeFilter -> TemplateNotFoundException), so the\nview''s own guard was never exercised; the earlier version of the assertion only\npassed because it tolerated any status. The .ajax suffix skips the wrapper and\nrenders the view alone: a 200 now proves the view ran and yielded nothing.\n\n* fix: the action card reads its type through the platform, its own view yields to a module''s, the spec moves to the actions suite\n\nReview of #294. The card resolved the type tooltip by reading a bundle file it guessed the\nname and encoding of — blind to a site''s rewording, to a bundle named by the module''s\nmanifest, to dependency bundles and to a locale''s fallbacks, and wrong on ISO-8859-1 — and\nbuilt the icon URL unconditionally, so an action type shipping no icon got a broken image.\nThe engine now describes the type (label, tooltip, icon) through the platform''s own bundle\nchain, site first, and icon lookup, supertypes included; the view asks for it in the UI\nlocale, as the editor does for every label, and the .properties parser is gone with the file\nreading. What remains of the text helper strips only what reads as a tag (\"< 30 and > 0\"\nsurvives) and shows an out-of-range entity as the replacement character. The key parameter\nis read from the items a type declares including a re-declared inherited one. The card view\nsits below the default priority, so a module''s own hidden.authoring view wins for sure, and\nthe action guide says how. Spec 47 becomes actions/71 — it tests the authoring zone, not\nvalidation — and asserts preview as it asserts live.\n\n* refactor: the tooltip lookup through the bundle chain is a method of its own, not a nested ternary\n\n* fix: the action type label goes through the site bundle first, as its tooltip does and as the editor resolves it","tree":{"sha":"61b3d3ca09a8f1ab5547a1d9de7c78123472a0b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/61b3d3ca09a8f1ab5547a1d9de7c78123472a0b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc","verification":{"payload":"tree 61b3d3ca09a8f1ab5547a1d9de7c78123472a0b8\nparent fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1788875771 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788875771 +0200\n\nfeat: form actions zone in the Page Builder edit view (#294)\n\n* feat: form actions zone in the Page Builder edit view\n\nOn a page, the Page Builder showed a form''s fields, steps and fieldsets but nothing\nof its actions: the list was not rendered, so a contributor could neither see which\nactions run on submission, nor tell that a form had none, nor add one from there —\nand a form without any action discards every submission.\n\nWhile authoring, the form now renders its action list as a zone of its own, inside\nthe form (a business stylesheet''s card keeps it) and under the buttons: a header,\none compact two-line card per action — rank in the execution order (a CSS counter;\nthe list is orderable, so a Page Builder drag reorders the pipeline), the type icon,\nthe title with the one telling parameter (recipient, forward target), and smaller the\ntype description its module declares for the Content Editor (the <type>.ui.tooltip\nbundle key, read through server.osgi.loadPropertiesResource: nothing duplicated, a\nthird-party action documented for the editor is documented for the zone) — then the\nlist''s own create button. The placeholder''s accepted type is the fmdbmix:formAction\nmixin, so jContent shows one \"New Form Action\" button (icon added to the engine) and\nthen the type chooser. A form without any action gets a warning instead of the cards.\n\nAuthoring chrome, deliberately not styled like the form, every value a variable.\nTo sit under the buttons, the form is a flex column while authoring and the island''s\nchildren wrapper is dissolved (display: contents); if either wrapper changes, the\nzone merely stays between the fields and the buttons. Nothing of it exists in live,\npreview or the cm view.\n\nCloses #292\n\n* feat: one icon for the form actions, results-oriented save-to-JCR tooltip\n\nThe zone header and the \"New Form Action\" button showed a lightning glyph while\njContent already shows the action list''s own type icon (four outward arrows) on the\nlist''s box and in the tree: two icons for one thing. The header now shows the list\ntype''s icon itself (resolved from the node type, `<module>/icons/<type>.png`, the way\nthe cards already resolve theirs) and the engine''s mixin icon is that same PNG — the\nbutton''s icon cannot be automatic, jContent takes the icon of the placeholder''s\naccepted type, the mixin the engine declares, which had none.\n\nThe save-to-JCR tooltip described storage (\"child nodes under a designated JCR path\")\ninstead of what the contributor gets: submissions kept in Jahia, to be reviewed in the\nForm Results screen. Reworded in the four bundles.\n\nThe zone header wraps in a narrow form card, and the changelog entry references the\npull request.\n\n* fix: show the forward target''s label on the action card, not its id\n\nThe contributor picks a forward target by the label the administrator configured\n(the choicelist shows labels); the card showed the stored id (crm01) instead. The\nlabel is resolved through the engine''s configuration service, falling back to the\nid when the target is no longer configured — worth seeing too.\n\n* fix: keep the actions zone''s Page Builder frame on the zone\n\nThe space above the zone was the zone''s own top margin; the Page Builder wraps the\nzone in a flex item whose box includes that margin, so the hover and selection frame\nstarted at the buttons row and read as a wider selection. The space now sits on the\nbuttons row while authoring.\n\n* fix: no dead grey below the New Form Action button\n\njContent gives the create placeholder a 28px minimum height and a 10px bottom margin;\nthe button is the last thing in the zone, so that margin only padded the grey below\nit. Dropped inside the zone.\n\n* feat: the action card''s key parameter comes from the type declaration\n\nThe parameter shown next to an action''s title was a hard-coded table in elements (to,\nto, targetId): a third-party action showed nothing, and the forward target''s label was\nresolved through the engine''s configuration service by name. The rule now lives in the\nengine, next to the action model, as ActionSummaryService: the key parameter is the\nfirst property the type declares after jcr:title that a contributor reads at a glance —\na single, visible, unprotected string edited as a small text or a choicelist — and a\nchoice is shown by the label its choicelist initializer gives it, the way the Content\nEditor showed it. Long texts, flags, numbers, references and lists are skipped, as are\nthe technical jcr:/j: properties.\n\nSame result for the engine''s types (recipient, recipient, target label, nothing for\nSave to JCR), nothing to register for a third-party action: the how-to documents how to\norder a CND so the telling property comes first. Elements only displays what the\nservice returns. The criterion is a pure function on the property''s declared\nattributes, unit-tested without Jahia classes (they cannot be mocked).\n\n* test: the accepted action type is read on the list''s module, not on its placeholder\n\nThe core writes the child-type constraint (nodetypes) on the module of the list\nand leaves the create placeholder untyped, so the spec looked for the mixin where\nit never is. It now asserts the list module declares fmdbmix:formAction and holds\nexactly one placeholder; the comments describing the placeholder follow.\n\n* fix: the action summary warning names the property and node, not the value\n\nCopilot review on #294: a failed label resolution logged the raw property\nvalue, which could carry contributor-entered data. Property name and node\npath are enough to find the case.\n\n* fix: readable zone hints, tooltip words kept apart, choice labels under test\n\nCopilot review on #294: the zone''s muted text (#6b7280 on #f4f5f7) read at 4.4:1,\nbelow AA — now #626977 (5.1:1), documented default updated; stripping the tooltip\nmarkup joined words separated by a <br/> — tags are replaced by a space before\nwhitespace collapses; the value-to-label match of a choicelist parameter is now a\npure function with its own tests (Jahia definitions cannot be mocked, the\ninitializer chaining stays covered by the Page Builder itself).\n\n* fix: the authoring views guard themselves, a blank choice label falls back, third-party type under test\n\nCopilot review on #294: the zone and card views relied on the form view''s edit-mode\ncheck, while a view can be requested directly in live or preview — each now returns\nnothing outside edit mode, and spec 47 requests both in live. A matching choice with\na blank label returned that blank and hid the parameter; the stored value is shown\ninstead. The spec also puts the test module''s own action on the form and reads its\nlabel, tooltip (declared for this) and icon through that module, the third-party\ncontract the docs advertise.\n\n* fix: the actions zone is an ordered list, and choice labels resolve as in the Content Editor\n\nCopilot review on #294: the execution order was DOM order plus a CSS counter on\ngeneric divs, so assistive technology had no list semantics — the cards now sit\nin an ol/li with the native numbering reset (the counter stays). The choicelist\ninitializers were called with a partial context; they now get what the core''s\nContentDefinitionHelper gives them — contextType, the dependent properties''\ncurrent values under their names, and a chain started from null — so a\nthird-party initializer resolves the same label here as in the editor.\n\n* fix: tooltips read as UTF-8 with entities decoded, forward label under test, no duplicated literal\n\nCopilot review on #294 and Sonar: the tooltip lookup went through Properties.load,\nwhich decodes ISO-8859-1 and would turn a JavaScript module''s raw UTF-8 accents into\nmojibake — the bundle is now read as text and parsed by a small Properties reader\nthat also resolves Java escapes (unit-tested); HTML entities of a rich tooltip are\ndecoded, since the text is rendered as React text; spec 47 configures a forward\ntarget and puts a forward action on the form, so the choicelist resolution through\nthe engine''s initializer is exercised end to end; the live requests of the guarded\nviews now require a 200 before asserting the markup is absent; the repeated\n\"dependentProperties\" literal is a constant.\n\n* fix: a long card title clips, and a dependentProperties option without a list is tolerated\n\nOwn review of the branch: the card title had the ellipsis rules but no min-width,\nso a long title overflowed the card instead of clipping; a choicelist declaring\ndependentProperties without a value made split() return null and the card fall\nback to the raw id through the catch. The styling doc''s overlong line is reflowed,\nand the how-to says the key parameter comes from the type''s own declarations.\n\n* test: the guarded authoring views are requested in live as fragments\n\nSpec 47 was red since 00d5b1f asked for a 200 on the direct live render of the\nauthoring views: a plain render URL (node.view.html) goes through the template\nwrapper, which resolves a page template named after the view and answers 404\nbefore the view runs (TemplateNodeFilter -> TemplateNotFoundException), so the\nview''s own guard was never exercised; the earlier version of the assertion only\npassed because it tolerated any status. The .ajax suffix skips the wrapper and\nrenders the view alone: a 200 now proves the view ran and yielded nothing.\n\n* fix: the action card reads its type through the platform, its own view yields to a module''s, the spec moves to the actions suite\n\nReview of #294. The card resolved the type tooltip by reading a bundle file it guessed the\nname and encoding of — blind to a site''s rewording, to a bundle named by the module''s\nmanifest, to dependency bundles and to a locale''s fallbacks, and wrong on ISO-8859-1 — and\nbuilt the icon URL unconditionally, so an action type shipping no icon got a broken image.\nThe engine now describes the type (label, tooltip, icon) through the platform''s own bundle\nchain, site first, and icon lookup, supertypes included; the view asks for it in the UI\nlocale, as the editor does for every label, and the .properties parser is gone with the file\nreading. What remains of the text helper strips only what reads as a tag (\"< 30 and > 0\"\nsurvives) and shows an out-of-range entity as the replacement character. The key parameter\nis read from the items a type declares including a re-declared inherited one. The card view\nsits below the default priority, so a module''s own hidden.authoring view wins for sure, and\nthe action guide says how. Spec 47 becomes actions/71 — it tests the authoring zone, not\nvalidation — and asserts preview as it asserts live.\n\n* refactor: the tooltip lookup through the bundle chain is a method of its own, not a nested ternary\n\n* fix: the action type label goes through the site bundle first, as its tooltip does and as the editor resolves it","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoBP7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3oMQAExpSZ2ISP7RrDVjKhbHE3Zy\nZamLOhEpvPpfq1fILrh4uQgEPbOrr/9xE43ZRd2mJ0iv24+IYy9gAEA9TTcOcVIf\nQxZLbv2iYs17aSRSX1q7gLvkNwgmoraNHaoovFCYaUa2odJ4ZxNc3KEVkhvS5C+9\nXhAdEqiO/lxxlK3jN4ThPH7n1iNDSmeWRTPFmyYo2CHdm9BRRu0uZX783yzQvZqX\n4A/9HuY1f4tp8An996Pp4GMBolSKYyAIFpoZ1ulq2v2TAGmPmW7j4FvwLi0od9Bc\njbTwu8GCR9dvfdTY/izFsA9835Iddp1FiXqSwbeNB8BkUuUxrtxdUVWIZfL5SGse\nMlTZ5gE/qM3/pttDmCwyDSr31ELxm7zdPcIBGfVI4/Nh+eHOZcJ9kW/zfeSP+/U+\nIZ7VRIHHLwd2CW4XqSI3eQnueZ9jk6sfXVlw2f5WAjRjDOrdCKzRtDFesLoifkQ+\ni8XoK6DuzeMIp4JCLJcZ31Ael/7IZUOti27o1lM8YsUj7bJpOLvyBxh4tRdQmats\n9GknNBEElqlVlJoq/MmVD6J7Mj5QXixsrDgaJiKQZPUjTsfiJyRMQU2rACsVqgHD\nPp8P+Z4XgoSiOaJgr43DLbajplr9bxaPokEbqmztKw69eavwAN+euXNGB7UzNMRe\nzEOyvDyykM9vpiznLSlg\n=6/wC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T13:56:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKDM1ZmVkNGUyYWIyMmRjNTU1MzgzZDc4MjY1NjE0N2Q2MjIzNGNkZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881","sha":"fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881"}],"sha":"35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/35fed4e2ab22dc555383d782656147d62234cdfc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T16:04:05Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T16:04:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: date and datetime values read in the reader''s format in the form results (#285)\n\n* fix: date and datetime values read in the reader''s format in the form results\n\nThe submission detail showed date and datetime field values as the strings\nthe browser inputs post (\"2026-09-05T12:53\") while the Submitted metadata\nwas already formatted for the reader. The field metadata query now tells\nwhich fields carry a date or a datetime, and their values are formatted the\nsame way as the metadata (browser locale), parsed as local wall-clock time so\na date never shifts by a day west of Greenwich. Values that do not parse, and\nevery other field kind, are shown as stored; exports stay machine-readable.\n\nCloses #284\n\n* chore: changelog entry for #285\n\n* fix: a datetime answer with a fraction of a second is formatted like the others\n\nThe backend accepts HH:mm[:ss[.SSS]], the results formatter only read up to the\nseconds and showed such a value raw. The fraction is now matched (and ignored,\nthe short time style never shows it). The new test file follows the folder''s\nfour-space indentation.\n\n* fix: a date or datetime answer is shown as typed whatever the reader''s zone\n\nCopilot review on #285: the parts were rebuilt as a local Date, so a wall-clock\nvalue that does not exist in the reader''s zone (02:30 on a spring-forward day in\nNew York) failed the round-trip check and showed raw. The parts are now carried\nas UTC fields and formatted in UTC: no zone shifts or rejects them, which is the\nintent — values stay as typed, the zone question belongs to #286. Tests set TZ\nto a gap zone for the regression case.\n\n* test: the zone-specific cases stub TZ through Vitest\n\nThe engine build type-checks the tests without Node''s typings, so process.env\nbroke it (TS2580). vi.stubEnv sets the same variable, and vi.unstubAllEnvs\nrestores the runner''s zone after each case.\n\n* fix: a date answer with a year below 100 is shown as typed\n\nCopilot review on #285: Date.UTC() maps the years 0-99 to 1900-1999, so a valid\n\"0099-01-01\" failed the round-trip check and showed raw. The date is now built\nfrom the epoch with setUTCFullYear, which keeps any four-digit year.","tree":{"sha":"dc3bc6a78d2fb9adb548cb44d23ae038554f962f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/dc3bc6a78d2fb9adb548cb44d23ae038554f962f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881","verification":{"payload":"tree dc3bc6a78d2fb9adb548cb44d23ae038554f962f\nparent 1f0b4819e3b75ea467b551f51616d873c45b3b98\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1788797045 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788797045 +0200\n\nfix: date and datetime values read in the reader''s format in the form results (#285)\n\n* fix: date and datetime values read in the reader''s format in the form results\n\nThe submission detail showed date and datetime field values as the strings\nthe browser inputs post (\"2026-09-05T12:53\") while the Submitted metadata\nwas already formatted for the reader. The field metadata query now tells\nwhich fields carry a date or a datetime, and their values are formatted the\nsame way as the metadata (browser locale), parsed as local wall-clock time so\na date never shifts by a day west of Greenwich. Values that do not parse, and\nevery other field kind, are shown as stored; exports stay machine-readable.\n\nCloses #284\n\n* chore: changelog entry for #285\n\n* fix: a datetime answer with a fraction of a second is formatted like the others\n\nThe backend accepts HH:mm[:ss[.SSS]], the results formatter only read up to the\nseconds and showed such a value raw. The fraction is now matched (and ignored,\nthe short time style never shows it). The new test file follows the folder''s\nfour-space indentation.\n\n* fix: a date or datetime answer is shown as typed whatever the reader''s zone\n\nCopilot review on #285: the parts were rebuilt as a local Date, so a wall-clock\nvalue that does not exist in the reader''s zone (02:30 on a spring-forward day in\nNew York) failed the round-trip check and showed raw. The parts are now carried\nas UTC fields and formatted in UTC: no zone shifts or rejects them, which is the\nintent — values stay as typed, the zone question belongs to #286. Tests set TZ\nto a gap zone for the regression case.\n\n* test: the zone-specific cases stub TZ through Vitest\n\nThe engine build type-checks the tests without Node''s typings, so process.env\nbroke it (TS2580). vi.stubEnv sets the same variable, and vi.unstubAllEnvs\nrestores the runner''s zone after each case.\n\n* fix: a date answer with a year below 100 is shown as typed\n\nCopilot review on #285: Date.UTC() maps the years 0-99 to 1900-1999, so a valid\n\"0099-01-01\" failed the round-trip check and showed raw. The date is now built\nfrom the epoch with setUTCFullYear, which keeps any four-digit year.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnuB1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOf0QADv5jDtCPjujWSGKWm8ckv5F\nF16txRMR4U6yzpkuPd6uEMn0KVXKiHckN7rW7T+tgdv/L79T83wnMtrjv5Qa8NB/\nXXVACs83JKZs71/q9BFjA6P+PZZKAobSN/6i2RU3rAh4NhMmBKyKaW+H81qCrhiE\nFi9DqrpB6pyvjzj6uqRQM2AOJIay4MUGAVmDLRkmox7xFVulcHNp0ldY6unvERhd\njmC8d8DRbgon6HkPrQo1lJq/u8e/RBGw3MhAA+fAfQJLe/xlul1KhsR1zNYgEJzB\nwrf+rbPUyq03W9OtPNmavIthFdzaZRe1RoTQI4CUpU3YGLqTeoiZrM3tQ5QH12dS\nbVy9CuQy4joHgdfx8AhNtJOt1mrlwNSXac94RKqKsjciNNt2A8JNArTdmyMwayTk\nbWVpCbjy3WIQPkoyh1FggUO25OWg/7yo6e5kgOzzb2f03U2iJ0hNK74qgI06xp+m\ndRhTh3yq0j8WvtUC1lV4LloWgg5AukSnYL3Bt2wKrDAXt3Z9CWsNrGBQMdaCcdRd\ne2MJDXQy3MH/kiTkruf0rqMfxm/3asNd/DeWNlQWVyP0iaRE97Otwp+QHQEKMAsI\nW5xoTKuU1lG+fzbmz1sx5QwriqZABmnJz2w40z5esCsvDE96RydkiU9MogLqDpNV\nKAvCgS89ZXT6R2elMVYZ\n=PW/l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T16:04:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881","node_id":"C_kwDORjIIPtoAKGZjZjQ3Zjg5YWJiYjRhYjAwZWRlNTIwZWVjZGU2NmYyMDhmNDI4ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/formidable/commit/1f0b4819e3b75ea467b551f51616d873c45b3b98","sha":"1f0b4819e3b75ea467b551f51616d873c45b3b98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1f0b4819e3b75ea467b551f51616d873c45b3b98"}],"sha":"fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/fcf47f89abbb4ab00ede520eecde66f208f42881"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55382113?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hduchesne","id":55382113,"login":"hduchesne","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MzgyMTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hduchesne","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/commits/1f0b4819e3b75ea467b551f51616d873c45b3b98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T15:21:14Z","email":"55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hervé Duchesne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T15:21:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: the file field forgets its files when the form is reset (#290)\n\n* fix: the file field forgets its files when the form is reset\n\nThe list of selected files under a file field is client state: a native form\nreset — the Reset button, or the form coming back after a successful\nsubmission — emptied the input but left the list on screen, and the visitor\nbelieved the previous file was still attached. The field now listens to the\nform''s reset event and clears its list, notice and custom validity, the way\nthe range slider already restores its value.\n\nCloses #288\n\n* chore: changelog entry for #290\n\n* test: the reset also clears the ignored-file notice and the blocking message\n\nCopilot review on #290: the reset case only attached an accepted file, so the two\nother traces the reset clears were never exercised. A new case resets after a mixed\nselection (the notice disappears) and after an invalid-only one (the custom\nvalidity is released). The changelog entry names the moment the visitor saw the\nstale list: after a reset, or when starting another submission.","tree":{"sha":"99f18af38bd9e24d3853c8e619d989d7ca180a77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/trees/99f18af38bd9e24d3853c8e619d989d7ca180a77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/formidable/git/commits/1f0b4819e3b75ea467b551f51616d873c45b3b98","verification":{"payload":"tree 99f18af38bd9e24d3853c8e619d989d7ca180a77\nparent 78bf4f76fb35390594c45e74e497f0caa4046796\nauthor Hervé Duchesne <55382113+hduchesne@users.noreply.github.com> 1788794474 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788794474 +0200\n\nfix: the file field forgets its files when the form is reset (#290)\n\n* fix: the file field forgets its files when the form is reset\n\nThe list of selected files under a file field is client state: a native form\nreset — the Reset button, or the form coming back after a successful\nsubmission — emptied the input but left the list on screen, and the visitor\nbelieved the previous file was still attached. The field now listens to the\nform''s reset event and clears its list, notice and custom validity, the way\nthe range slider already restores its value.\n\nCloses #288\n\n* chore: changelog entry for #290\n\n* test: the reset also clears the ignored-file notice and the blocking message\n\nCopilot review on #290: the reset case only attached an accepted file, so the two\nother traces the reset clears were never exercised. A new case resets after a mixed\nselection (the notice disappears) and after an invalid-only one (the custom\nvalidity is released). The changelog entry names the moment the visitor saw the\nstale list: after a reset, or when starting another submission.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqntZqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl4wQAGjkPQeV3IU5qyRX2TejQV0b\nU2lV050DlhzapaG4olx3qjmTbSCEOKAjB78SEfMuifJ4ngKoLAoex8Qi32lf6jAd\nWWDaLXO1ABgO0lU+1zCZWG7Zk9kVGvqDNKh2g8fTjMr/nqapalCunsQd2dMjViLZ\nPdBZgdPK0Gea9f+TuDgpEXRI2WIPJkHW9jhQMWgtT/Vsl6lSzI2ApFve5As