idence backfill — fixes P0 AI crash\n\nBackfill was lost in the main-branch reset. This single line prevents\nTypeError: Cannot set properties of undefined (setting ''teacher'') which\nsilently swallows all AI responses after ~5 topics covered for any user\nwith pre-rollout localStorage memory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcaa16b3d922a2d7f1b7526e9cbf3a49e339bb33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/trees/dcaa16b3d922a2d7f1b7526e9cbf3a49e339bb33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/commits/218d876dfe222643ba7e1f016619a70c9b1c3877","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54392220?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM","id":54392220,"login":"RajaMDM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzkyMjIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM/braindrop/commit/218d876dfe222643ba7e1f016619a70c9b1c3877","node_id":"C_kwDORjeei9oAKDIxOGQ4NzZkZmUyMjI2NDNiYTdlMWYwMTY2MTlhNzBjOWIxYzM4Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM/braindrop/commit/4f840c93e49e5c575d981d47ad3eb5d16889049d","sha":"4f840c93e49e5c575d981d47ad3eb5d16889049d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/4f840c93e49e5c575d981d47ad3eb5d16889049d"}],"sha":"218d876dfe222643ba7e1f016619a70c9b1c3877","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/218d876dfe222643ba7e1f016619a70c9b1c3877"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54392220?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM","id":54392220,"login":"RajaMDM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzkyMjIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/4f840c93e49e5c575d981d47ad3eb5d16889049d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-24T02:27:02Z","email":"raja.cloudmdm@gmail.com","name":"RajaMDM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-24T02:28:37Z","email":"raja.cloudmdm@gmail.com","name":"RajaMDM"},"message":"fix(grounding): hard anti-hallucination rules on numeric facts + KB-only stance\n\nReported: AI was making up numbers. Root cause in the prompt: \"NCERT content is\nPRIMARY\" was soft guidance, not a hard constraint. Free-tier Llama 3.3 and\nGemini 2.5 Flash both invent plausible-sounding numbers when the retrieved KB\ndoesn''t contain the specific value.\n\nThree prompt surfaces updated:\n\n1. buildSystemPrompt (explain/socratic/examprep/tutor modes)\n   - Added explicit \"GROUNDING RULES (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\" section placed before style\n     rules so the model attends to it.\n   - Rule: ONLY state numeric values that appear verbatim in retrieved KB chunks.\n     If not in KB, say \"check page X of NCERT\" instead of guessing.\n   - Rule: paraphrase/quote definitions from KB. Do not paraphrase from memory.\n   - Rule: Indian examples ARE ALLOWED but only for analogies, never as factual\n     claims (closes a loophole where the model cited imaginary cricket stats).\n\n2. buildSystemPrompt minimal (quiz/flashcard modes)\n   - Questions, correct answers, and explanations must all derive from KB.\n   - If a specific fact can''t be found in KB, generate fewer questions rather\n     than inventing answers (prevents a quiz with wrong \"correct\" answers).\n   - Math questions: solve step-by-step internally; correct option must be\n     mathematically verifiable.\n\n3. buildClassroomPrompt (classroom teacher agent)\n   - Same grounding rules applied to the Teacher agent''s voice.\n   - Teacher now says \"let me check our textbook\" when unsure, instead of\n     confabulating. More honest classroom dynamic.\n\nThe classmate agents are not grounded (they are students reacting to what the\nTeacher said, so factual accuracy flows through the Teacher). That was intentional\nand unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"12d8c5a730f6d06c69fdbdbd3952441a6c776ffd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/trees/12d8c5a730f6d06c69fdbdbd3952441a6c776ffd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/commits/4f840c93e49e5c575d981d47ad3eb5d16889049d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54392220?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM","id":54392220,"login":"RajaMDM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzkyMjIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM/braindrop/commit/4f840c93e49e5c575d981d47ad3eb5d16889049d","node_id":"C_kwDORjeei9oAKDRmODQwYzkzZTQ5ZTVjNTc1ZDk4MWQ0N2FkM2ViNWQxNjg4OTA0OWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM/braindrop/commit/c75049f13eaf79fe147e15f44b0286bb2e656649","sha":"c75049f13eaf79fe147e15f44b0286bb2e656649","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/c75049f13eaf79fe147e15f44b0286bb2e656649"}],"sha":"4f840c93e49e5c575d981d47ad3eb5d16889049d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/4f840c93e49e5c575d981d47ad3eb5d16889049d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/c75049f13eaf79fe147e15f44b0286bb2e656649/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-16T07:43:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-16T07:43:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(classroom): add provider fallback chain to teacher call\n\nClassroom mode picked a single provider for the teacher and returned\nnull if that one call threw — no retry, no fallback. One flaky engine\n(e.g. NVIDIA returning a transient error) killed the entire classroom\nsession with ''AI is temporarily unavailable''.\n\nMirror the fallback pattern from callAI: try the preferred provider\nfirst, then iterate through all available providers until one succeeds.\nlogEvent now records the actual provider that served the reply, not\nthe originally-preferred one.","tree":{"sha":"e3e34d63b5a5494a97ca05de0974f91b5996ae20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/trees/e3e34d63b5a5494a97ca05de0974f91b5996ae20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/commits/c75049f13eaf79fe147e15f44b0286bb2e656649","verification":{"payload":"tree e3e34d63b5a5494a97ca05de0974f91b5996ae20\nparent a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1776325432 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1776325432 +0000\n\nfix(classroom): add provider fallback chain to teacher call\n\nClassroom mode picked a single provider for the teacher and returned\nnull if that one call threw — no retry, no fallback. One flaky engine\n(e.g. NVIDIA returning a transient error) killed the entire classroom\nsession with ''AI is temporarily unavailable''.\n\nMirror the fallback pattern from callAI: try the preferred provider\nfirst, then iterate through all available providers until one succeeds.\nlogEvent now records the actual provider that served the reply, not\nthe originally-preferred one.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMgNxYB+\nz2UuyyMshNvaJflMnrPTPiV4aBkGbISo367xtzI0yZZai4saFsC30TVS+D+QamROJjk+TqYMJMLw\nTgY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-16T07:43:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM/braindrop/commit/c75049f13eaf79fe147e15f44b0286bb2e656649","node_id":"C_kwDORjeei9oAKGM3NTA0OWYxM2VhZjc5ZmUxNDdlMTVmNDRiMDI4NmJiMmU2NTY2NDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM/braindrop/commit/a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667","sha":"a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667"}],"sha":"c75049f13eaf79fe147e15f44b0286bb2e656649","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/c75049f13eaf79fe147e15f44b0286bb2e656649"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-16T07:40:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-16T07:40:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(ai): route AI calls through /guest/* — unbreak site after Apr 4 restore\n\nThe Cloudflare Worker was upgraded post-Apr 4 to require X-Google-Token\non bare endpoints (/claude, /gemini, /nvidia, /groq) and added /guest/*\nendpoints for non-auth''d traffic. The Apr 4 code hit bare paths with\nonly X-User-Email → Worker returned 401 → every provider fell through\nthe try loop → \"AI engines are busy\" for every request.\n\nMinimal surgical fix:\n- proxyPath() prepends /guest when no bd_gtoken is stored\n- proxyHeaders() forwards X-Google-Token when one is present (no-op\n  today since AuthContext doesn''t persist the raw JWT, but future-proof)\n- All 14 AI endpoint URLs in callProvider + callProviderWithSys now go\n  through proxyPath()\n\nOllama path unchanged — it''s a localhost call, not proxied.\n\nEveryone routes through /guest/* today (IP-rate-limited at 30 req/hr,\nplenty for a single student). When Google Sign-In is rewired to store\nbd_gtoken, those users will seamlessly switch to the auth''d endpoints.","tree":{"sha":"d3c95575ebae8d7c4d88e0e4d5596bab879e3deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/trees/d3c95575ebae8d7c4d88e0e4d5596bab879e3deb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/commits/a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667","verification":{"payload":"tree d3c95575ebae8d7c4d88e0e4d5596bab879e3deb\nparent 6142cf268d4f222a02987410a18805adb6e99906\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1776325225 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1776325225 +0000\n\nfix(ai): route AI calls through /guest/* — unbreak site after Apr 4 restore\n\nThe Cloudflare Worker was upgraded post-Apr 4 to require X-Google-Token\non bare endpoints (/claude, /gemini, /nvidia, /groq) and added /guest/*\nendpoints for non-auth''d traffic. The Apr 4 code hit bare paths with\nonly X-User-Email → Worker returned 401 → every provider fell through\nthe try loop → \"AI engines are busy\" for every request.\n\nMinimal surgical fix:\n- proxyPath() prepends /guest when no bd_gtoken is stored\n- proxyHeaders() forwards X-Google-Token when one is present (no-op\n  today since AuthContext doesn''t persist the raw JWT, but future-proof)\n- All 14 AI endpoint URLs in callProvider + callProviderWithSys now go\n  through proxyPath()\n\nOllama path unchanged — it''s a localhost call, not proxied.\n\nEveryone routes through /guest/* today (IP-rate-limited at 30 req/hr,\nplenty for a single student). When Google Sign-In is rewired to store\nbd_gtoken, those users will seamlessly switch to the auth''d endpoints.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDa4luYy\nHwFLnDX5hqMzUZMX2TVe5DP9bWarWm/SlmB6UyTPkHzKUoRuMhrpz5m00S8tNWkxQrR4D506E+gw\ncAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-16T07:40:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM/braindrop/commit/a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667","node_id":"C_kwDORjeei9oAKGEwZWE2OTIyZDZjZTMxYzIxMzI4NzA0ZjY4YzVjYTZmNjhmMjQ2Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM/braindrop/commit/6142cf268d4f222a02987410a18805adb6e99906","sha":"6142cf268d4f222a02987410a18805adb6e99906","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/6142cf268d4f222a02987410a18805adb6e99906"}],"sha":"a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/a0ea6922d6ce31c21328704f68c5ca6f68f24667"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54392220?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RajaMDM","id":54392220,"login":"RajaMDM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzkyMjIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/6142cf268d4f222a02987410a18805adb6e99906/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-04T02:56:47Z","email":"raja.cloudmdm@gmail.com","name":"RajaMDM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-04T02:56:47Z","email":"raja.cloudmdm@gmail.com","name":"RajaMDM"},"message":"remove: MagicBlock auto-generation from all modes\n\nAI-generated canvas visualizations are unreliable — blank canvases,\nhuge gaps, broken drawings. Removed the entire 2KB MagicBlock template\nfrom the system prompt.\n\nWhat changed:\n- AI no longer generates <magic-block> in any response\n- System prompt explicitly says \"Do NOT include magic-block tags\"\n- Responses are now clean text with LaTeX math, ASCII diagrams, examples\n- /sim command still works for deliberate simulation requests\n- ~2KB removed from every system prompt = faster responses, less truncation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fa6371d097d137a1bdcb1c545b398017f043c97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/trees/4fa6371d097d137a1bdcb1c545b398017f043c97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/commits