ithub.com/users/RajaMDM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RajaMDM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/commits/16834359cd46557e13d3646bdec4f42b543bc00c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-03T13:41:03Z","email":"raja.cloudmdm@gmail.com","name":"RajaMDM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-03T13:41:03Z","email":"raja.cloudmdm@gmail.com","name":"RajaMDM"},"message":"fix: \"No AI providers\" error on mobile — removed localStorage dependency\n\nRoot cause: getAvailableProviders() checked localStorage(''bd2'') for\nprovider keys like ''ck'', ''gk'', ''nv''. On fresh mobile devices, localStorage\nis empty so ALL providers showed as unavailable — \"No AI providers\nconfigured. Please add an API key in Settings.\"\n\nBut API keys are server-side now — there''s nothing to configure!\n\nFix: getAvailableProviders() now returns hardcoded list of the 4\nconfigured providers (nvidia, groq, gemini, claude). No localStorage\ncheck needed since all keys live in the Cloudflare Worker.\n\nAlso removed all \"API key\" and \"Settings\" references from error messages.\nUsers now see \"AI is temporarily unavailable\" instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d8cd3bbd300bce9cac39a07ad4e649654c5fffe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/trees/1d8cd3bbd300bce9cac39a07ad4e649654c5fffe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RajaMDM/braindrop/git/commits/16834359cd46557e13d3646bdec4f42b543bc00c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54392220?v=4","events_url":