ttps://github.com/rodmgwgu","id":117670175,"login":"rodmgwgu","node_id":"U_kgDOBwOBHw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodmgwgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodmgwgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodmgwgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodmgwgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodmgwgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodmgwgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WGU-Open-edX/tutor-mfe-build-extra-certs/commits/dac5e04c60418984432bc4b38ce2fd5cc7f97f11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:19:34Z","email":"117670175+rodmgwgu@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Rodrigo Mendez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:19:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(): Python support (#1)\n\n* feat: add REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE and SSL_CERT_FILE to Dockerfile patches\n\nPython''s requests/urllib3 does not use the system CA store by default;\nit uses certifi''s bundled CAs. This means even though the VPN cert was\ninstalled into /etc/ssl/certs via update-ca-certificates, Python HTTPS\ncalls (e.g., tiktoken downloading tokenizer data during collectstatic)\nstill failed with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED.\n\nSetting REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE and SSL_CERT_FILE to the system CA bundle\npath makes all Python TLS clients trust the installed VPN certificate\nduring both build and runtime.\n\n* squash!: bump version","tree":{"sha":"131fc21a4a4fd96f5ffb8cc643741a4c749facb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WGU-Open-edX/tutor-mfe-build-extra-certs/git/trees/131fc21a4a4fd96f5ffb8cc643741a4c749facb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WGU-Open-edX/tutor-mfe-build-extra-certs/git/commits/dac5e04c60418984432bc4b38ce2fd5cc7f97f11","verification":{"payload":"tree 131fc21a4a4fd96f5ffb8cc643741a4c749facb1\nparent 0314a2a8d0f67e4a981e76654bac76b331d67809\nauthor Rodrigo Mendez <117670175+rodmgwgu@users.noreply.github.com> 1786641574 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786641574 -0600\n\nfeat(): Python support (#1)\n\n* feat: add REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE and SSL_CERT_FILE to Dockerfile patches\n\nPython''s requests/urllib3 does not use the system CA store by default;\nit uses certifi''s bundled CAs. This means even though the VPN cert was\ninstalled into /etc/ssl/certs via update-ca-certificates, Python HTTPS\ncalls (e.g., tiktoken downloading tokenizer data during collectstatic)\nstill failed with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED.\n\nSetting REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE and SSL_CERT_FILE to the system CA bundle\npath makes all Python TLS clients trust the installed VPN certificate\nduring both build and runtime.\n\n* squash!: bump version","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqffymCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU30QAAbOX58yhhHqfyUsAmpSyDSr\nxqyFiCzka8vTN6UD2Uxvd5JhdTzjXICGtoh7itQZuCeoYXZVHxNpj8ij7YsFe+7R\nbHaQLYN0E8XTEQokzSBoua3zMGQdTvMTJp8FgK+wvwCdxbGTNH7/sbOAMO2KVfVg\nxGgJCYgMcPM53AC9fiXEgLDETYup7otX27+38BFTlCZc+iDwWBgr6SKPaSZUSGOI\nCc/0nsmSD+gB+PcXhcq/VSxrgDDR4Y00zaRhWleos5zHzJiB1dy/xz4/y0p5Zd8A\nULcBjMoGVybTXxpxmAfNNBYQxZVswgIm6+LvzIAtWXvgxVN9GTIYPYz16Xa1+WDC\nEVSxyt7WrIfJ3NVOK2Tn4cj+x5A7NRQGHZa3kTq9rdvrV5YpfNsQDNQlIZ8AFEEK\n3e4FCD+zQdIfSPWt8WssjczXpXmVjI3RP/5qXdu3XFrGHSzkwvobHnL+KfBgYFjg\nkw+nI+Ioo3WYcYtuy3454srlFW4hmmw0xA7u+FQQvxOGktV+qZ3+S39wo/j+iCrj\n0g2z6YqobJAGwiIKU9GO50p1hLw9Mx6psy83NiIwGc56N24iEWs5oDULuYc2V/Tc\n7NBt2Xj2nEQqUhAn0ZDpAQ+cE1YQ7U8aPeTrdOdyURgPuCdIUBMjaYqpubXkLxtt\nuPG22wCA0CPQijyW6Lsz\n=Hda1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T17:20:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other